\p \v 8 \rb “Go ahead,”|לֵ֑כִי\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb told|וַתֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb her.|לָ֥הּ\rb* \rb And the girl|הָֽעַלְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb went|וַתֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and called|וַתִּקְרָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the boy’s|הַיָּֽלֶד׃\rb* \rb mother.|אֵ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֣הּ\rb* \rb “Take|הֵילִ֜יכִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb child|הַיֶּ֤לֶד\rb* \rb and nurse him|וְהֵינִקִ֣הוּ\rb* \rb for me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will pay|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your wages.”|שְׂכָרֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb So the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֧ח\rb* \rb the boy|הַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb* \rb and nursed him.|וַתְּנִיקֵֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When the child|הַיֶּ֗לֶד\rb* \rb had grown older,|וַיִגְדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb she brought him|וַתְּבִאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb daughter,|לְבַת־\rb* \rb and he became|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb son.|לְבֵ֑ן\rb* \rb She named him|וַתִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 2:10 \fqa Moses \ft sounds like a Hebrew term that means \fqa to lift out\ft .\f* \rb and explained,|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb “I drew him out|מְשִׁיתִֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the water.”|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb*
\s1 The Rejection and Flight of Moses
\r \ref Acts 7:23–29|ACT 7:23-29\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb One day,|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb after Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb had grown up,|וַיִּגְדַּ֤ל\rb* \rb he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own people|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*\f + \fr 2:11 \ft Or \fqa his brothers\f* \rb and observed|וַיַּ֖רְא\rb* \rb their hard labor.|בְּסִבְלֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb He saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb beating|מַכֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb a Hebrew,|עִבְרִ֖י\rb* \rb one of his own people.|מֵאֶחָֽיו׃\rb* \v 12 \rb After looking|וַיִּ֤פֶן\rb* \rb this way|כֹּה֙\rb* \rb and that|וָכֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and seeing|וַיַּ֖רְא\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one,|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb he struck down|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb and hid his body|וַֽיִּטְמְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the sand.|בַּחֽוֹל׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb The next|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Moses went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb Hebrews|עִבְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb fighting.|נִצִּ֑ים\rb* \rb He asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb the one in the wrong,|לָֽרָשָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are you attacking|תַכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb your companion?”|רֵעֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb But the man replied,|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb made|שָֽׂמְךָ֞\rb* \rb you|לְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb ruler|שַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb and judge|וְשֹׁפֵט֙\rb* \rb over us?|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*\f + \fr 2:14 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:27|ACT 7:27\ref* and Acts 7:35\f* \rb Are you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb planning|אֹמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb to kill me|הַלְהָרְגֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you killed|הָרַ֖גְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptian?|הַמִּצְרִ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 2:14 \ft LXX \fqa Are you planning to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?\ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:28|ACT 7:28\ref*\f*”
\p \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb was afraid|וַיִּירָ֤א\rb* \rb and thought,|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “This thing I have done|הַדָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb has surely|אָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb become known.”|נוֹדַ֥ע\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb about this matter,|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb he sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to kill|לַהֲרֹ֣ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֤ח\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb where he sat down|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb beside|עַֽל־\rb* \rb a well.|הַבְּאֵֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Now the priest|וּלְכֹהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb had seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb daughters,|בָּנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb and they came|וַתָּבֹ֣אנָה\rb* \rb to draw water|וַתִּדְלֶ֗נָה\rb* \rb and fill|וַתְּמַלֶּ֙אנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the troughs|הָ֣רְהָטִ֔ים\rb* \rb to water|לְהַשְׁק֖וֹת\rb* \rb their father’s|אֲבִיהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb flock.|צֹ֥אן\rb* \v 17 \rb And when some shepherds|הָרֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb came along|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb and drove them away,|וַיְגָרְשׁ֑וּם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb to help them|וַיּ֣וֹשִׁעָ֔ן\rb* \rb and watered|וַיַּ֖שְׁקְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their flock.|צֹאנָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb When the daughters returned|וַתָּבֹ֕אנָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb Reuel,|רְעוּאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 2:18 \fqa Reuel \ft was also called \fqa Jethro\ft ; see \ref Exodus 3:1|EXO 3:1\ref*.\f* \rb he asked them,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb have you returned|בֹּ֖א\rb* \rb so early|מִהַרְתֶּ֥ן\rb* \rb today?”|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “An Egyptian|מִצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb rescued us|הִצִּילָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the shepherds,”|הָרֹעִ֑ים\rb* \rb they replied.|וַתֹּאמַ֕רְןָ\rb* \rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb “He even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb drew water|דָּלֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |דָלָה֙\rb* \rb for us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and watered|וַיַּ֖שְׁקְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock.”|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “So where is he?”|וְאַיּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb their father asked.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּה֙\rb* \rb did you leave the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb behind?|עֲזַבְתֶּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Invite|קִרְאֶ֥ן\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to have something to eat.”|וְיֹ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb agreed|וַיּ֥וֹאֶל\rb* \rb to stay|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the man,|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb and he gave|וַיִּתֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Zipporah|צִפֹּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Moses in marriage.|לְמֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 22 \rb And she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son,|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and Moses named him|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Gershom,|גֵּרְשֹׁ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:22 \fqa Gershom \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa foreigner\ft .\f*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb saying,|אָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “I have become|הָיִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb in a foreign|נָכְרִיָּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb land.”|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb*
\s1 God Hears the Cry of the Israelites
\p \v 23 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb After a long|הָֽרַבִּ֜ים\rb*\rb |הָהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb time,|בַיָּמִ֨ים\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb died.|וַיָּ֙מָת֙\rb* \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb groaned|וַיֵּאָנְח֧וּ\rb* \rb and cried out|וַיִּזְעָ֑קוּ\rb* \rb under their|מִן־\rb* \rb burden of slavery,|הָעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and their cry for deliverance|שַׁוְעָתָ֛ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb bondage|הָעֲבֹדָֽה׃\rb* \rb ascended|וַתַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb their groaning,|נַאֲקָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and He|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Isaac,|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Jacob.|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \v 25 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and|אֱלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb took notice.|וַיֵּ֖דַע\rb*
\c 3
\s1 Moses at the Burning Bush
\r \ref Acts 7:30–38|ACT 7:30-38\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Meanwhile, Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb shepherding|רֹעֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock|צֹ֛אן\rb* \rb of his father-in-law|חֹתְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jethro,|יִתְר֥וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Moses’ father-in-law \fqa Jethro \ft was also called \fqa Reuel\ft ; see \ref Exodus 2:18|EXO 2:18\ref*.\f* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of Midian.|מִדְיָ֑ן\rb* \rb He led|וַיִּנְהַ֤ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּאן֙\rb* \rb to the far side|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֛א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Horeb,|חֹרֵֽבָה׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb the mountain|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \v 2 \rb There the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 3:2 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָ֥ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַ֠יֵּרָא\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb in a blazing|בְּלַבַּת־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb from within|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb a bush.|הַסְּנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb Moses saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the bush|הַסְּנֶה֙\rb* \rb ablaze|בֹּעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with fire,|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |וְהַסְּנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb but it was not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb consumed.|אֻכָּֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb thought,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I must go over|אָסֻֽרָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb and see|וְאֶרְאֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb marvelous|הַגָּדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb sight.|הַמַּרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb Why is|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb the bush|הַסְּנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb burning up?”|יִבְעַ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he had gone over|סָ֣ר\rb* \rb to look,|לִרְא֑וֹת\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֨יו\rb* \rb from within|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the bush,|הַסְּנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb “Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses!”|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*
\p \rb “Here|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb* \rb I am,”|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb he answered.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb come|תִּקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb any closer,”|הֲלֹ֑ם\rb* \rb God said.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Take off|שַׁל־\rb* \rb your sandals,|נְעָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |רַגְלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb are standing|עוֹמֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb is holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb ground.”|אַדְמַת־\rb*\f + \fr 3:5 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:33|ACT 7:33\ref*\f* \v 6 \rb Then He said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your father,|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Isaac,|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and the God|וֵאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob.”|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 22:32|MAT 22:32\ref*, Mark 12:26, Luke 20:37, and Acts 7:32\f*
\p \rb At this, Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb hid|וַיַּסְתֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb his face,|פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was afraid|יָרֵ֔א\rb* \rb to look|מֵהַבִּ֖יט\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb God.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I have indeed seen|רָאֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |רָאִ֛יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the affliction|עֳנִ֥י\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Egypt.|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I have heard them|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb crying out|צַעֲקָתָ֤ם\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their oppressors,|נֹֽגְשָׂ֔יו\rb* \rb and|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am aware|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of their sufferings.|מַכְאֹבָֽיו׃\rb* \v 8 \rb I have come down|וָאֵרֵ֞ד\rb* \rb to rescue them|לְהַצִּיל֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and to bring them up|וּֽלְהַעֲלֹתוֹ֮\rb* \rb out of that|הַהִוא֒\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a good|טוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb and spacious|וּרְחָבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb land,|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey—|וּדְבָ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the home|מְק֤וֹם\rb* \rb of the Canaanites,|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַ֣חִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites.|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the cry|צַעֲקַ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb has reached|בָּ֣אָה\rb* \rb Me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb and I have|וְגַם־\rb* \rb seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb how severely|הַלַּ֔חַץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are oppressing them.|לֹחֲצִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Therefore,|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb go!|לְכָ֔ה\rb* \rb I am sending|וְאֶֽשְׁלָחֲךָ֖\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb to bring|וְהוֹצֵ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of Egypt.”|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:34|ACT 7:34\ref*\f*
\p \v 11 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb God,|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb am I,|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I should go|אֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb bring|אוֹצִ֛יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of Egypt?”|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb “I will surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb be|אֶֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you,”|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb God said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “and this|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb will be the sign|הָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb to you|לְּךָ֣\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb have sent you:|שְׁלַחְתִּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb When you have brought the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb out|בְּהוֹצִֽיאֲךָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb all of you will worship|תַּֽעַבְדוּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb God|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb mountain.”|הָהָ֥ר\rb*\f + \fr 3:12 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:7|ACT 7:7\ref*\f*
\p \v 13 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb God,|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb “Suppose|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb go|בָא֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to them,|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘The God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to you,’|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and they ask|וְאָֽמְרוּ־\rb* \rb me,|לִ֣י\rb* \rb ‘What|מַה־\rb* \rb is His name?’|שְּׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb should I tell|אֹמַ֖ר\rb* \rb them?”|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “I AM|אֶֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb WHO|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I AM.|אֶֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 3:14 \ft Or \ft I WILL BE WHAT I WILL BE\f* \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb*\rb |תֹאמַר֙\rb* \rb you are to say|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to the Israelites:|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb ‘I AM|אֶֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֥נִי\rb* \rb to you.’”|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb also|ע֨וֹד\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Say|תֹאמַר֮\rb*\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb ‘The LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your fathers—|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*  \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Isaac,|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb and the God|וֵאלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jacob—|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*  \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to you.’|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb This|זֶה־\rb* \rb is My name|שְּׁמִ֣י\rb* \rb forever,|לְעֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb and this|וְזֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is how I am to be remembered|זִכְרִ֖י\rb* \rb in every generation.|לְדֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |דֹּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Go,|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb assemble|וְאָֽסַפְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb ‘The LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of your fathers—|אֲבֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb*  \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb and Jacob—|וְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*  \rb has appeared|נִרְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb and said:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb I have surely attended to|פָּקֹ֤ד\rb*\rb |פָּקַ֙דְתִּי֙\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb have seen what has been done|הֶעָשׂ֥וּי\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in Egypt.|בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 17 \rb And I have promised|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to bring you up|אַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֮\rb* \rb out of your affliction|מֵעֳנִ֣י\rb* \rb in Egypt,|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Canaanites,|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַ֣חִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites—|וְהַיְבוּסִ֑י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey.’|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb The elders of Israel will listen|וְשָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to what you say,|לְקֹלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and you|אַתָּה֩\rb* \rb must go|וּבָאתָ֡\rb* \rb with them|וְזִקְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and tell|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb ‘The LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews,|הָֽעִבְרִיִּים֙\rb* \rb has met|נִקְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb with us.|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָּ֞א\rb* \rb let us take|נֵֽלֲכָה־\rb* \rb a three-day|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb into the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb so that we may sacrifice|וְנִזְבְּחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.’|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb allow|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb you to go|לַהֲלֹ֑ךְ\rb* \rb unless|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb a mighty hand compels him.|חֲזָקָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:19 \ft Literally \fqa except by a mighty hand\f* \rb |בְּיָ֥ד\rb*\v 20 \rb So I will stretch out|וְשָׁלַחְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb and strike|וְהִכֵּיתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb with all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the wonders|נִפְלְאֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will perform|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb among them.|בְּקִרְבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb And after|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that,|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb he will release|יְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb And I will grant|וְנָתַתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|הָֽעָם־\rb* \rb such favor|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb that when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you leave,|תֵֽלֵכ֔וּן\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go away|תֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb empty-handed.|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Every|אִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb woman shall ask|וְשָׁאֲלָ֨ה\rb* \rb her neighbor|מִשְּׁכֶנְתָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and any woman staying|וּמִגָּרַ֣ת\rb* \rb in her house|בֵּיתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb for silver|כֶ֛סֶף\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb and gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb jewelry|כְּלֵי־\rb* \rb and clothing,|וּשְׂמָלֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and you will put them|וְשַׂמְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your sons|בְּנֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and daughters.|בְּנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb So you will plunder|וְנִצַּלְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians.”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\c 4
\s1 Moses’ Staff
\p \v 1 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb answered,|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb “What if|וְהֵן֙\rb* \rb they do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb believe|יַאֲמִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to my voice?|בְּקֹלִ֑י\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they may say,|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb appeared|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to you.’”|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb “What is that|מַזֶּה\rb* \rb in your hand?”|בְיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \rb “A staff,”|מַטֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “Throw|הַשְׁלִיכֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb it on the ground,”|אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb said the LORD.|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb So Moses threw|וַיַּשְׁלִיכֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it on the ground,|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb and it became|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb a snake,|לְנָחָ֑שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 4:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa nachash\ft , in contrast to Aaron’s staff, which became a \fqa tannin\ft in \ref Exodus 7:10|EXO 7:10\ref*\f* \rb and he|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֥נָס\rb* \rb from it.|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb “Stretch out|שְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֔\rb* \rb and grab it|וֶאֱחֹ֖ז\rb* \rb by the tail,”|בִּזְנָב֑וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb who reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb and caught|וַיַּ֣חֲזֶק\rb* \rb the snake,|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and it turned back|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb into a staff|לְמַטֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb in his hand.|בְּכַפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “This is so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb they may believe|יַאֲמִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers—|אֲבֹתָ֑ם\rb*  \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Isaac,|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and the God|וֵאלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jacob—|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*  \rb has appeared|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to you.”|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb*
\s1 Moses’ Hand
\p \v 6 \rb Furthermore,|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to Moses,|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb “Put|הָֽבֵא־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb inside your cloak.|בְּחֵיקֶ֔ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa into your bosom\ft ; twice in this verse and twice in verse 7\f*” \rb So he put|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb inside his cloak,|בְּחֵיק֑וֹ\rb* \rb and when he took it out,|וַיּ֣וֹצִאָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb was leprous,|מְצֹרַ֥עַת\rb*\f + \fr 4:6 \ft The Hebrew word traditionally translated as \fqa leprous\ft was used for various skin diseases; see \ref Leviticus 13|LEV 13\ref*.\f* \rb white as snow.|כַּשָּֽׁלֶג׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb “Put your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb back|הָשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb your cloak,”|חֵיקֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb said the LORD.|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb So Moses put his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb back|וַיָּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb his cloak,|חֵיק֑וֹ\rb* \rb and when he took it out,|וַיּֽוֹצִאָהּ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽחֵיק֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb it was restored,|שָׁ֖בָה\rb* \rb like the rest of his skin.|כִּבְשָׂרֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And the LORD said,|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb they refuse|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to believe|יַאֲמִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb heed|יִשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb the witness|לְקֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb sign,|הָאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb they may believe|וְהֶֽאֱמִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb that|לְקֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of the second.|הָאַחֲרֽוֹן׃\rb*\rb |הָאֹ֥ת\rb* \v 9 \rb But|וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb they do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb believe|יַאֲמִ֡ינוּ\rb* \rb even|גַּם֩\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb signs|הָאֹת֜וֹת\rb* \rb or listen|יִשְׁמְעוּן֙\rb* \rb to your voice,|לְקֹלֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֙\rb* \rb some water|מִמֵּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb from the Nile|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and pour|וְשָׁפַכְתָּ֖\rb* \rb it on the dry ground.|הַיַּבָּשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb Then|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you take|תִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Nile|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb will become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb blood|לְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb on the ground.”|בַּיַּבָּֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\s1 The Appointment of Aaron
\p \v 10 \rb “Please,|בִּ֣י\rb* \rb Lord,”|אֲדֹנָי֒\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb “I|אָנֹ֗כִי\rb* \rb have never|לֹא֩\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb been eloquent,|דְּבָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb neither|גַּ֤ם\rb* \rb in the past|מִתְּמוֹל֙\rb*\rb |מִשִּׁלְשֹׁ֔ם\rb* \rb nor|גַּ֛ם\rb* \rb since|מֵאָ֥ז\rb* \rb You have spoken|דַּבֶּרְךָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your servant,|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb am slow|כְבַד־\rb* \rb of speech|פֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb and|וּכְבַ֥ד\rb* \rb tongue.”|לָשׁ֖וֹן\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb gave|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb man|לָֽאָדָם֒\rb* \rb his mouth?|פֶּה֮\rb* \rb Or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb makes|יָשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb the mute|אִלֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb the deaf,|חֵרֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |א֥וֹ\rb* \rb the sighted|פִקֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb the blind?|עִוֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb Is it not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb I,|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD?|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb go!|לֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb I|וְאָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will help you|אֶֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb as you speak,|פִּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and I will teach you|וְהוֹרֵיתִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to say.”|תְּדַבֵּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb But Moses replied,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Please,|בִּ֣י\rb* \rb Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb send|שְֽׁלַֽח־\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb* \rb someone else.”|בְּיַד־\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁלָֽח׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the anger|אַ֨ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Moses,|בְּמֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb and He said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Is not|הֲלֹ֨א\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb the Levite|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb your brother?|אָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb can speak well,|דַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |יְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֤ם\rb* \rb he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is now|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb on his way|יֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to meet you.|לִקְרָאתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb When he sees you,|וְרָאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb he will be glad|וְשָׂמַ֥ח\rb* \rb in his heart.|בְּלִבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb You are to speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and put|וְשַׂמְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his mouth.|בְּפִ֑יו\rb* \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will help|אֶֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb both of you to speak,|פִּ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְעִם־\rb*\rb |פִּ֔יהוּ\rb* \rb and I will teach|וְהוֹרֵיתִ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to do.|תַּעֲשֽׂוּן׃\rb* \v 16 \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb will speak|וְדִבֶּר־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb for you.|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb He|הוּא֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָ֤יָה\rb* \rb your|לְּךָ֣\rb* \rb spokesman,|לְפֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and it will be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb as if you were|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb to him.|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \v 17 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb take|תִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb staff|הַמַּטֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you can perform|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb signs with it.”|הָאֹתֹֽת׃פ\rb*
\s1 Moses Leaves for Egypt
\p \v 18 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb back|וַיָּ֣שָׁב׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father-in-law|חֹֽתְנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Jethro|יֶ֣תֶר\rb*\f + \fr 4:18 \ft Moses’ father-in-law \fqa Jethro \ft was also called \fqa Reuel\ft ; see \ref Exodus 2:18|EXO 2:18\ref*.\f* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb “Please|נָּ֗א\rb* \rb let me return|וְאָשׁ֙וּבָה֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣לֲכָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my brothers|אַחַ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to see|וְאֶרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb if they are still|הַעוֹדָ֣ם\rb* \rb alive.”|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*
\p \rb “Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in peace,”|לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb Jethro replied.|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |יִתְר֛וֹ\rb*\rb |לְמֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb had said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb in Midian,|בְּמִדְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb back|שֻׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|הָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who sought|הַֽמְבַקְשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to kill you|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb are dead.”|מֵ֙תוּ֙\rb* \v 20 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and sons,|בָּנָ֗יו\rb* \rb put them|וַיַּרְכִּבֵם֙\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb a donkey,|הַחֲמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and headed back|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb*\rb |אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb to Egypt.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb And he|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the staff|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb in his hand.|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb instructed|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb “When you go|בְּלֶכְתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb back|לָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb see that|רְאֵ֗ה\rb* \rb you perform|וַעֲשִׂיתָ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wonders|הַמֹּֽפְתִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have put|שַׂ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb within your power.|בְיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb But I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will harden|אֲחַזֵּ֣ק\rb*\f + \fr 4:21 \ft Or \fqa stiffen \ft or \fqa strengthen\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb so that he will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb let the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb go.|יְשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Then tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh that|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb is My firstborn|בְכֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb son,|בְּנִ֥י\rb* \v 23 \rb and I told you|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb to let My son|בְּנִי֙\rb* \rb go|שַׁלַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that he may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb But since you have refused|וַתְּמָאֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to let him go,|לְשַׁלְּח֑וֹ\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb will kill|הֹרֵ֔ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your firstborn|בְּכֹרֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb son!’”|בִּנְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Now at a lodging place|בַּמָּל֑וֹן\rb* \rb along the way,|בַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb met Moses|וַיִּפְגְּשֵׁ֣הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 4:24 \ft Hebrew \fqa him\f* \rb and was about|וַיְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to kill him.|הֲמִיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 25 \rb But Zipporah|צִפֹּרָ֜ה\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a flint knife,|צֹ֗ר\rb* \rb cut off|וַתִּכְרֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her son’s|בְּנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb foreskin,|עָרְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb and touched it|וַתַּגַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to Moses’ feet.|לְרַגְלָ֑יו\rb*\f + \fr 4:25 \ft Hebrew \fqa his feet\f* \rb “Surely|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb a bridegroom|חֲתַן־\rb* \rb of blood|דָּמִ֛ים\rb* \rb to me,”|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb she said.|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb So the LORD let him alone.|וַיִּ֖רֶף\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb (When|אָ֚ז\rb* \rb she said,|אָֽמְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb “bridegroom|חֲתַ֥ן\rb* \rb of blood,”|דָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb she was referring to the circumcision.)|לַמּוּלֹֽת׃פ\rb*
\s1 The People Believe Moses and Aaron
\p \v 27 \rb Meanwhile, the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb and meet|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness.”|הַמִּדְבָּ֑רָה\rb* \rb So he went|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and met Moses|וַֽיִּפְגְּשֵׁ֛הוּ\rb* \rb at the mountain|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and kissed|וַיִּשַּׁק־\rb* \rb him.|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 28 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַֽהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had sent him|שְׁלָח֑וֹ\rb* \rb to say,|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the signs|הָאֹתֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had commanded him to perform.|צִוָּֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and assembled|וַיַּ֣אַסְפ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 30 \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb relayed|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb And Moses performed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb the signs|הָאֹתֹ֖ת\rb* \rb before|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 31 \rb and they|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb believed.|וַֽיַּאֲמֵ֖ן\rb* \rb And when they heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֡וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had attended|פָקַ֨ד\rb* \rb to the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and|וְכִ֤י\rb* \rb had seen|רָאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their affliction,|עָנְיָ֔ם\rb* \rb they bowed down|וַֽיִּקְּד֖וּ\rb* \rb and worshiped.|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוּֽוּ׃\rb*
\c 5
\s1 Pharaoh’s First Refusal
\p \v 1 \rb After that,|וְאַחַ֗ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb went|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Let My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may hold a feast|וְיָחֹ֥גּוּ\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb in the wilderness.’”|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb But Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I should obey|אֶשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb His voice|בְּקֹל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and let Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb go?|לְשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb let Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb go.”|אֲשַׁלֵּֽחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “The God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews|הָעִבְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb has met|נִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb with us,”|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb they answered.|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Please|נָּ֡א\rb* \rb let us go on|נֵ֣לֲכָה\rb* \rb a three-day|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִ֜ים\rb* \rb journey|דֶּרֶךְ֩\rb* \rb into the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb to sacrifice|וְנִזְבְּחָה֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb or|פֶּ֨ן־\rb* \rb He may strike us|יִפְגָּעֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb with plagues|בַּדֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb with the sword.”|בֶחָֽרֶב׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb But the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb do you draw|תַּפְרִ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb away from their work?|מִמַּֽעֲשָׂ֑יו\rb* \rb Get back|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to your labor!”|לְסִבְלֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb also said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Look,|הֵן־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb are now numerous,|רַבִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and you would be stopping|וְהִשְׁבַּתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb from their labor.”|מִסִּבְלֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Bricks and Straw
\p \v 6 \rb That same|הַה֑וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb* \rb the taskmasters|הַנֹּגְשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb of the people|בָּעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their foremen:|שֹׁטְרָ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 7 \rb “You shall no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|תֹאסִפ֞וּן\rb* \rb supply|לָתֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the people|לָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb with straw|תֶּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb for making|לִלְבֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb bricks.|הַלְּבֵנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |כִּתְמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֑ם\rb* \rb They|הֵ֚ם\rb* \rb must go|יֵֽלְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb and gather|וְקֹשְׁשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb their own|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb straw.|תֶּֽבֶן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But require|תָּשִׂ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb of them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the same quota|מַתְכֹּ֨נֶת\rb* \rb of bricks|הַלְּבֵנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb as|הֵם֩\rb*\rb |עֹשִׂ֨ים\rb* \rb before;|תְּמ֤וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁם֙\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb reduce it.|תִגְרְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are lazy;|נִרְפִּ֣ים\rb* \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb they|הֵ֤ם\rb* \rb are crying out,|צֹֽעֲקִים֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Let us go|נֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and sacrifice|נִזְבְּחָ֥ה\rb* \rb to our God.’|לֵאלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Make the work harder|תִּכְבַּ֧ד\rb*\rb |הָעֲבֹדָ֛ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb so they will be occupied|וְיַעֲשׂוּ־\rb*\rb |בָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb and pay no attention|יִשְׁע֖וּ\rb* \rb to these lies.”|שָֽׁקֶר׃\rb*\rb |בְּדִבְרֵי־\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So the taskmasters|נֹגְשֵׂ֤י\rb* \rb and foremen|וְשֹׁ֣טְרָ֔יו\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֨צְא֜וּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb them,|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘I am no longer|אֵינֶ֛נִּי\rb* \rb giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb straw.|תֶּֽבֶן׃\rb* \v 11 \rb |אַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb Go|לְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb and get|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb your own|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb straw|תֶּ֔בֶן\rb* \rb wherever|מֵאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you can find it;|תִּמְצָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your workload|מֵעֲבֹדַתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will in no way|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb be reduced.’”|נִגְרָ֛ע\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb So the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb scattered|וַיָּ֥פֶץ\rb* \rb all over|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to gather|לְקֹשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb stubble|קַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for straw.|לַתֶּֽבֶן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb The taskmasters|וְהַנֹּגְשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb kept pressing them,|אָצִ֣ים\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Fulfill|כַּלּ֤וּ\rb* \rb your quota|דְּבַר־\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂיכֶם֙\rb* \rb each day,|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb just as you did when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb straw|הַתֶּֽבֶן׃\rb* \rb was provided.”|בִּהְי֥וֹת\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the Israelite|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb foremen,|שֹֽׁטְרֵי֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb taskmasters|נֹגְשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb had set|שָׂ֣מוּ\rb* \rb over the people,|עֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb were beaten|וַיֻּכּ֗וּ\rb* \rb and asked,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֡וּעַ\rb* \rb have you not|לֹא֩\rb* \rb fulfilled|כִלִּיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb your quota|חָקְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb of bricks|לִלְבֹּן֙\rb* \rb yesterday|כִּתְמ֣וֹל\rb* \rb or today,|גַּם־\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb as you did before?”|תְּמ֖וֹל\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֔ם\rb*
\s1 The Cry of the Israelites
\p \v 15 \rb So the Israelite|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb foremen|שֹֽׁטְרֵי֙\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and appealed|וַיִּצְעֲק֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh:|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb are you treating|תַעֲשֶׂ֦ה\rb* \rb your servants|לַעֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb this way?|כֹ֖ה\rb* \v 16 \rb No|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb straw|תֶּ֗בֶן\rb* \rb has been given|נִתָּן֙\rb* \rb to your servants,|לַעֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb yet we are told,|אֹמְרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb ‘Make|עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb bricks!’|וּלְבֵנִ֛ים\rb* \rb Look,|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb are being beaten,|מֻכִּ֖ים\rb* \rb but the fault|וְחָטָ֥את\rb* \rb is with your own people.”|עַמֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “You|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are slackers!”|נִרְפִּ֥ים\rb* \rb Pharaoh replied.|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Slackers!|נִרְפִּ֑ים\rb* \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb keep saying,|אֹֽמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb ‘Let us go|נֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and sacrifice|נִזְבְּחָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.’|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb get to|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb work.|עִבְד֔וּ\rb* \rb You|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will be given|יִנָּתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb straw,|וְתֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb yet you must deliver|תִּתֵּֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb the full quota|וְתֹ֥כֶן\rb* \rb of bricks.”|לְבֵנִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb The Israelite|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb foremen|שֹֽׁטְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb realized|וַיִּרְא֞וּ\rb* \rb they were in trouble|בְּרָ֣ע\rb* \rb when they were told,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb reduce|תִגְרְע֥וּ\rb* \rb your daily|י֥וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb quota|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of bricks.”|מִלִּבְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \v 20 \rb When they left|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb they confronted|וַֽיִּפְגְּעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb who stood|נִצָּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb waiting to meet them.|לִקְרָאתָ֑ם\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb “May the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb look upon you|יֵ֧רֶא\rb* \rb and judge you,”|וְיִשְׁפֹּ֑ט\rb* \rb the foremen said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “for|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb you have made us a stench|הִבְאַשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |רֵיחֵ֗נוּ\rb* \rb before|בְּעֵינֵ֤י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb and his officials;|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb you have placed|לָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb in their hand|בְּיָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb to kill us!”|לְהָרְגֵֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb* \rb why|לָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb have You brought trouble|הֲרֵעֹ֙תָה֙\rb* \rb upon this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people?|לָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb Is this|זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb You sent me?|שְׁלַחְתָּֽנִי׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Ever since|וּמֵאָ֞ז\rb* \rb I went|בָּ֤אתִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb in Your name,|בִּשְׁמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb he has brought trouble|הֵרַ֖ע\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people,|לָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb and You have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb delivered|וְהַצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb in any way.”|הִצַּ֖לְתָּ\rb*
\c 6
\s1 God Promises Deliverance
\p \v 1 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb you will see|תִרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to Pharaoh,|לְפַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb because of My mighty|חֲזָקָה֙\rb* \rb hand|בְיָ֤ד\rb* \rb he will let the people go;|יְשַׁלְּחֵ֔ם\rb* \rb because of My strong|חֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb hand|וּבְיָ֣ד\rb* \rb he will drive them out of|יְגָרְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb his land.”|מֵאַרְצֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb God also|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb told|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb I appeared|וָאֵרָ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Isaac,|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb as God|בְּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Almighty,|שַׁדָּ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 6:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb but by My name|וּשְׁמִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb I did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb make Myself known|נוֹדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb I also|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb established|הֲקִמֹ֤תִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִי֙\rb* \rb with them|אִתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan,|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |מְגֻרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they lived as foreigners.|גָּ֥רוּ\rb* \v 5 \rb Furthermore,|וְגַ֣ם׀\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the groaning|נַאֲקַת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are enslaving,|מַעֲבִדִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and I have remembered|וָאֶזְכֹּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant.|בְּרִיתִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the Israelites:|לִבְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb ‘I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD,|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb and I will bring|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb out from under|מִתַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb the yoke|סִבְלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and deliver|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from their bondage.|מֵעֲבֹדָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb I will redeem|וְגָאַלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb with an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb arm|בִּזְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb and with mighty|גְּדֹלִֽים׃\rb* \rb acts of judgment.|וּבִשְׁפָטִ֖ים\rb* \v 7 \rb I will take|וְלָקַחְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb as My own|לִי֙\rb* \rb people,|לְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and I will be|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God.|לֵֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who brought|הַמּוֹצִ֣יא\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb out from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the yoke|סִבְל֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the Egyptians.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I swore|נָשָׂ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb to Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as a possession.|מוֹרָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD!’”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb relayed|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb this message|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb but on account of their broken|מִקֹּ֣צֶר\rb* \rb spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb and cruel|קָשָֽׁה׃פ\rb* \rb bondage,|וּמֵעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb they did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen|שָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him.|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb “Go|בֹּ֣א\rb* \rb and tell|דַבֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to let the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb go out|וִֽישַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of his land.”|מֵאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But in the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb “If|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb then why|וְאֵיךְ֙\rb* \rb would Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb listen to me,|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb since I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am unskilled|עֲרַ֥ל\rb* \rb in speech?|שְׂפָתָֽיִם׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 6:12 \ft Hebrew \fqa I have uncircumcised lips\ft ; also in verse 30\f*”
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֒\rb* \rb and gave them a charge|וַיְצַוֵּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb concerning|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb both the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to bring|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Genealogies of Moses and Aaron
\p \v 14 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were the heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers’|אֲבֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb houses:|בֵית־\rb*
\li1 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Reuben,|רְאוּבֵ֜ן\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹ֣ר\rb* \rb of Israel, were|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb Hanoch|חֲנ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb and Pallu,|וּפַלּוּא֙\rb* \rb Hezron|חֶצְר֣וֹן\rb* \rb and Carmi.|וְכַרְמִ֔י\rb* \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Reuben.|רְאוּבֵֽן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 15 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Simeon were|שִׁמְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb Jemuel,|יְמוּאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb Jamin,|וְיָמִ֤ין\rb* \rb Ohad,|וְאֹ֙הַד֙\rb* \rb Jachin,|וְיָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb Zohar,|וְצֹ֔חַר\rb*\f + \fr 6:15 \fqa Zohar \ft is a variant of \fqa Zerah\ft ; see \ref Numbers 26:13|NUM 26:13\ref* and 1 Chronicles 4:24.\f* \rb and Shaul,|וְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of a Canaanite woman.|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֑ית\rb* \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Simeon.|שִׁמְעֽוֹן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 16 \rb These|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb were the names|שְׁמ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִי֙\rb* \rb according to their records:|לְתֹ֣לְדֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb Gershon,|גֵּרְשׁ֕וֹן\rb* \rb Kohath,|וּקְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb and Merari.|וּמְרָרִ֑י\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb Levi|לֵוִ֔י\rb* \rb lived|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb 137|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |וּמְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 17 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Gershon were|גֵרְשׁ֛וֹן\rb* \rb Libni|לִבְנִ֥י\rb* \rb and Shimei,|וְשִׁמְעִ֖י\rb* \rb by their clans.|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 18 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Kohath were|קְהָ֔ת\rb* \rb Amram,|עַמְרָ֣ם\rb* \rb Izhar,|וְיִצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb Hebron,|וְחֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb and Uzziel.|וְעֻזִּיאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Kohath|קְהָ֔ת\rb* \rb lived|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb 133|שָׁלֹ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |וּמְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 19 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Merari were|מְרָרִ֖י\rb* \rb Mahli|מַחְלִ֣י\rb* \rb and Mushi.|וּמוּשִׁ֑י\rb*
\li1 \rb These|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb were the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb according to their records.|לְתֹלְדֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 20 \rb And Amram|עַמְרָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb married|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb his father’s sister|דֹּֽדָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb Jochebed,|יוֹכֶ֤בֶד\rb* \rb and she bore|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb Amram|עַמְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb lived|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb 137|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |וּמְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 21 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Izhar were|יִצְהָ֑ר\rb* \rb Korah,|קֹ֥רַח\rb* \rb Nepheg,|וָנֶ֖פֶג\rb* \rb and Zichri.|וְזִכְרִֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 22 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Uzziel were|עֻזִּיאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Mishael,|מִֽישָׁאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Elzaphan,|וְאֶלְצָפָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 6:22 \fqa Elzaphan \ft is a variant of \fqa Elizaphan\ft ; see \ref Numbers 3:30|NUM 3:30\ref*.\f* \rb and Sithri.|וְסִתְרִֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 23 \rb And Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb married|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb Elisheba,|אֱלִישֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Amminadab|עַמִּינָדָ֛ב\rb* \rb and sister|אֲח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Nahshon,|נַחְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb and she bore|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Abihu,|אֲבִיה֔וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ithamar.|אִֽיתָמָֽר׃\rb*
\li1 \v 24 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Korah were|קֹ֔רַח\rb* \rb Assir,|אַסִּ֥יר\rb* \rb Elkanah,|וְאֶלְקָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Abiasaph.|וַאֲבִיאָסָ֑ף\rb*\f + \fr 6:24 \fqa Abiasaph \ft is a variant of \fqa Ebiasaph\ft ; \ref see 1|1\ref* Chronicles 6:23 and 1 Chronicles 9:19.\f* \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Korahites.|הַקָּרְחִֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 25 \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb Eleazar|וְאֶלְעָזָ֨ר\rb* \rb married|לָקַֽח־\rb*\rb |לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb one of the daughters|מִבְּנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of Putiel,|פּֽוּטִיאֵל֙\rb* \rb and she bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Phinehas.|פִּֽינְחָ֑ס\rb*
\li1 \rb These|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb were the heads|רָאשֵׁ֛י\rb* \rb of the Levite|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb families|אֲב֥וֹת\rb* \rb by their clans.|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb It was this|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said,|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb “Bring the Israelites|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb out|הוֹצִ֜יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb their divisions.”|צִבְאֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 27 \rb |הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \rb were the ones who spoke|הַֽמְדַבְּרִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb in order to bring|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb on the day that|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb* \v 29 \rb He|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb tell|דַּבֵּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb say|דֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb to you.”|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb But in the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb “Since|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am unskilled|עֲרַ֣ל\rb* \rb in speech,|שְׂפָתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb why|וְאֵ֕יךְ\rb* \rb would Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃פ\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to me?”|אֵלַ֖י\rb*
\c 7
\s1 God Commands Moses and Aaron
\p \v 1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “See,|רְאֵ֛ה\rb* \rb I have made|נְתַתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb you like God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb to Pharaoh,|לְפַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your prophet.|נְבִיאֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are to speak|תְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I command you,|אֲצַוֶּ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb and your brother|אָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb is to tell|יְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb to let the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb go|וְשִׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of his land.|מֵאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will harden|אַקְשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb heart,|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and though I will multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My signs|אֹתֹתַ֛י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and wonders|מוֹפְתַ֖י\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to you.|אֲלֵכֶם֙\rb*
\p \rb Then I will lay|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb on Egypt,|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and by mighty|גְּדֹלִֽים׃\rb* \rb acts of judgment|בִּשְׁפָטִ֖ים\rb* \rb I will bring|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the divisions|צִבְאֹתַ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \v 5 \rb And the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb when I stretch out|בִּנְטֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and bring|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out from among them.”|מִתּוֹכָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb had commanded them.|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \v 7 \rb Moses|וּמֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb was eighty|שְׁמֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַֽהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb was eighty-three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb when they spoke|בְּדַבְּרָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh.|פַּרְעֹֽה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Aaron’s Staff
\p \v 8 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “When|כִּי֩\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb tells you,|יְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb ‘Perform|תְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a miracle,’|מוֹפֵ֑ת\rb* \rb you are to say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb to Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb ‘Take|קַ֧ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your staff|מַטְּךָ֛\rb* \rb and throw it down|וְהַשְׁלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb Pharaoh,’|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb and it will become|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a serpent.|לְתַנִּֽין׃\rb*\f + \fr 7:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa tannin\ft ; here and in verse 10, in contrast to Moses’ staff, which became a \fqa nachash\ft in \ref Exodus 4:3|EXO 4:3\ref* and was noted again in Exodus 7:15\f*”
\p \v 10 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂוּ\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded.|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb his staff down|מַטֵּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and his officials,|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and it became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a serpent.|לְתַנִּֽין׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb the wise men|לַֽחֲכָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and sorcerers|וְלַֽמְכַשְּׁפִ֑ים\rb* \rb and magicians|חַרְטֻמֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and they|הֵ֜ם\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb the same things|כֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb by their magic arts.|בְּלַהֲטֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 12 \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb one threw down|וַיַּשְׁלִ֙יכוּ֙\rb* \rb his staff,|מַטֵּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and it became|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb a serpent.|לְתַנִּינִ֑ם\rb* \rb But Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb staff|מַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb swallowed up|וַיִּבְלַ֥ע\rb* \rb the other staffs.|מַטֹּתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Still, Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb was hardened,|וַיֶּחֱזַק֙\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \ft Or \fqa stiffened \ft or \fqa strengthened\ft ; also in verse 22\f* \rb and he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*
\s1 The First Plague: Blood
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb is unyielding;|כָּבֵ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Or \fqa heavy \ft or \fqa stubborn\f* \rb he refuses|מֵאֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to let the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb go.|לְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \v 15 \rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֞ה\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb as you see him|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb walking out|יֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to the water.|הַמַּ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb Wait|וְנִצַּבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bank|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Nile|הַיְאֹ֑ר\rb* \rb to meet him,|לִקְרָאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and take|תִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb the staff|וְהַמַּטֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb was changed|נֶהְפַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb into a snake.|לְנָחָ֖שׁ\rb* \v 16 \rb Then say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb ‘The LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews,|הָעִבְרִים֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֤נִי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to tell you:|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb Let My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me|וְיַֽעַבְדֻ֖נִי\rb* \rb in the wilderness.|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb But|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb now|כֹּֽה׃\rb* \rb you have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb listened.|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \v 17 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb By this|בְּזֹ֣את\rb* \rb you will know|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb with the staff|בַּמַּטֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in my hand|בְּיָדִ֗י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb will strike|מַכֶּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Nile,|בַּיְאֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and it will turn|וְנֶהֶפְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb to blood.|לְדָֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb The fish|וְהַדָּגָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the Nile|בַּיְאֹ֛ר\rb* \rb will die,|תָּמ֖וּת\rb* \rb the river|הַיְאֹ֑ר\rb* \rb will stink,|וּבָאַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb and the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb will be unable|וְנִלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb its|הַיְאֹֽר׃ס\rb* \rb water.’”|מַ֖יִם\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֡ן\rb* \rb ‘Take|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb your staff|מַטְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and stretch out|וּנְטֵֽה־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֩\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵימֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Egypt—|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb over|עַֽל־\rb* \rb their rivers|נַהֲרֹתָ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and canals|יְאֹרֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and ponds|אַגְמֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |מֵימֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the reservoirs—|מִקְוֵ֥ה\rb* \rb that they may become|וְיִֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb blood.’|דָ֑ם\rb* \rb There will be|וְהָ֤יָה\rb* \rb blood|דָם֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb even in the vessels of wood|וּבָעֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb and stone.”|וּבָאֲבָנִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb*\rb |כֵן֩\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb had commanded;|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּלְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and his officials,|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb Aaron raised|וַיָּ֤רֶם\rb* \rb the staff|בַּמַּטֶּה֙\rb*\f + \fr 7:20 \ft Hebrew \fqa he raised the staff\ft ; see verse 19; some translators \fqa Moses raised the staff\ft .\f* \rb and struck|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Nile,|בַּיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בַּיְאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb was turned|וַיֵּהָֽפְכ֛וּ\rb* \rb to blood.|לְדָֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb The fish|וְהַדָּגָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the Nile|בַּיְאֹ֥ר\rb* \rb died,|מֵ֙תָה֙\rb* \rb and the river|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb smelled so bad|וַיִּבְאַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb that the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb could|יָכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb drink|לִשְׁתּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb its|הַיְאֹ֑ר\rb* \rb water.|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb And there was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb But the magicians|חַרְטֻמֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb the same things|כֵ֛ן\rb* \rb by their magic arts.|בְּלָטֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb So Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb was hardened,|וַיֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb and he would not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to Moses and Aaron,|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \v 23 \rb Instead, Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb turned around,|וַיִּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his palace,|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb take|שָׁ֥ת\rb* \rb any|גַּם־\rb* \rb of this|לָזֹֽאת׃\rb* \rb to heart.|לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \v 24 \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb dug|וַיַּחְפְּר֧וּ\rb* \rb around|סְבִיבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb the Nile|הַיְאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb for water|מַ֣יִם\rb* \rb to drink,|לִשְׁתּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they could|יָֽכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb drink|לִשְׁתֹּ֔ת\rb* \rb the water|מִמֵּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb from the river.|הַיְאֹֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb And seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb full days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb passed|וַיִּמָּלֵ֖א\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had struck|הַכּוֹת־\rb* \rb the Nile.|הַיְאֹֽר׃פ\rb*
\c 8
\s1 The Second Plague: Frogs
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Go|בֹּ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and tell him that|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Let My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb* \v 2 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb refuse|מָאֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to let them go,|לְשַׁלֵּ֑חַ\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will plague|נֹגֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb your whole country|גְּבוּלְךָ֖\rb* \rb with frogs.|בַּֽצְפַרְדְּעִֽים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb The Nile|הַיְאֹר֮\rb* \rb will teem|וְשָׁרַ֣ץ\rb* \rb with frogs,|צְפַרְדְּעִים֒\rb* \rb and they will come|וְעָלוּ֙\rb*\rb |וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb into your palace|בְּבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and up to your bedroom|וּבַחֲדַ֥ר\rb*\rb |מִשְׁכָּבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and onto|וְעַל־\rb* \rb your bed,|מִטָּתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb into the houses|וּבְבֵ֤ית\rb* \rb of your officials|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and your people,|וּבְעַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and into your ovens|וּבְתַנּוּרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and kneading bowls.|וּבְמִשְׁאֲרוֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb The frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִֽים׃\rb* \rb will come up|יַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb on you|וּבְכָ֥ה\rb* \rb and your people|וּֽבְעַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your officials.’”|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb ‘Stretch out|נְטֵ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֙\rb* \rb with your staff|בְּמַטֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the rivers|הַ֨נְּהָרֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and canals|הַיְאֹרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and ponds,|הָאֲגַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb and cause the frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb to come up onto|וְהַ֥עַל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּ֤ט\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the waters|מֵימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and the frogs|הַצְּפַרְדֵּ֔עַ\rb* \rb came up|וַתַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb and covered|וַתְּכַ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb But the magicians|הַֽחֲרְטֻמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb the same thing|כֵ֥ן\rb* \rb by their magic arts,|בְּלָטֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and they also brought frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb onto|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֜ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וּֽלְאַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Pray|הַעְתִּ֣ירוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to take|וְיָסֵר֙\rb* \rb the frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֔ים\rb* \rb away from me|מִמֶּ֖נִּי\rb* \rb and my people.|וּמֵֽעַמִּ֑י\rb* \rb Then I will let your people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb go,|וַאֲשַׁלְּחָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that they may sacrifice|וְיִזְבְּח֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Pharaoh,|לְפַרְעֹה֮\rb* \rb “You may have the honor|הִתְפָּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb over me.|עָלַי֒\rb* \rb When|לְמָתַ֣י׀\rb* \rb shall I pray|אַעְתִּ֣יר\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb and your officials|וְלַעֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and your people|וּֽלְעַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb that the frogs|הַֽצֲפַרְדְּעִ֔ים\rb* \rb (except for those|תִּשָּׁאַֽרְנָה׃\rb*\rb |רַ֥ק\rb* \rb in the Nile)|בַּיְאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb may be taken away|לְהַכְרִית֙\rb* \rb from|מִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb you and your houses?”|וּמִבָּתֶּ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb “Tomorrow,”|לְמָחָ֑ר\rb* \rb Pharaoh answered.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “May it be as you say,”|כִּדְבָ֣רְךָ֔\rb* \rb Moses replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may know|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֖ין\rb* \rb like the LORD|כַּיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb The frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֗ים\rb* \rb will depart|וְסָר֣וּ\rb* \rb from you|מִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and your houses|וּמִבָּ֣תֶּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and your officials|וּמֵעֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and your people;|וּמֵעַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb they will remain|תִּשָּׁאַֽרְנָה׃\rb* \rb only|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb in the Nile.”|בַּיְאֹ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb After Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb had left|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb cried out to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for help|וַיִּצְעַ֤ק\rb* \rb with|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb the frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had brought|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb against Pharaoh.|לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb as Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb requested,|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb and the frogs|הַֽצְפַרְדְּעִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the houses,|הַבָּתִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the courtyards,|הַחֲצֵרֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb and the fields|הַשָּׂדֹֽת׃\rb* \rb died.|וַיָּמֻ֙תוּ֙\rb* \v 14 \rb They were piled|וַיִּצְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into countless heaps,|חֳמָרִ֣ם\rb*\rb |חֳמָרִ֑ם\rb* \rb and there was a terrible stench|וַתִּבְאַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb saw that|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb there was|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb relief, however,|הָֽרְוָחָ֔ה\rb* \rb he hardened|וְהַכְבֵּד֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:15 \ft Or \fqa made heavy\ft ; also in verse 32\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to Moses and Aaron,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*
\s1 The Third Plague: Gnats
\p \v 16 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb ‘Stretch out|נְטֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your staff|מַטְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and strike|וְהַ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dust|עֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the earth,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb that it may turn into|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb swarms of gnats|לְכִנִּ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb This they did,|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb and when Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּט֩\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֤וֹ\rb* \rb with his staff|בְמַטֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dust|עֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the earth,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb gnats|הַכִּנָּ֔ם\rb* \rb came upon|וַתְּהִי֙\rb* \rb man|בָּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and beast.|וּבַבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the dust|עֲפַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb turned into|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb gnats|כִנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb The magicians|הַחַרְטֻמִּ֧ים\rb* \rb tried|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ־\rb*\rb |כֵ֨ן\rb* \rb to produce|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gnats|הַכִּנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb using their magic arts,|בְּלָטֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb but they could|יָכֹ֑לוּ\rb* \rb not.|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb And the gnats|הַכִּנָּ֔ם\rb* \rb remained|וַתְּהִי֙\rb* \rb on man|בָּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and beast.|וּבַבְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “This|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is the finger|אֶצְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb of God,”|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb the magicians|הַֽחַרְטֻמִּים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh.|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb But Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb was hardened,|וַיֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb*\f + \fr 8:19 \ft Or \fqa stiffened \ft or \fqa strengthened\f* \rb and he would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*
\s1 The Fourth Plague: Flies
\p \v 20 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Get up early|הַשְׁכֵּ֤ם\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַּבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb and when Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb goes out|יוֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to the water,|הַמָּ֑יְמָה\rb* \rb stand|וְהִתְיַצֵּב֙\rb* \rb before him|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and tell him|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Let My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb* \v 21 \rb But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will not|אֵינְךָ֮\rb* \rb let My people|עַמִּי֒\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb go,|מְשַׁלֵּ֣חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will send|מַשְׁלִ֨יחַ\rb* \rb swarms of flies|הֶעָרֹ֑ב\rb*\f + \fr 8:21 \ft Literally \fqa a noxious mixture\ft ; also in verses 22, 24, 29, and 31\f* \rb upon you|בְּךָ֜\rb* \rb and your officials|וּבַעֲבָדֶ֧יךָ\rb* \rb and your people|וּֽבְעַמְּךָ֛\rb* \rb and your houses.|וּבְבָתֶּ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb The houses|בָּתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and even|וְגַ֥ם\rb* \rb the ground|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb where they stand|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb will be full|וּמָ֨לְא֜וּ\rb* \rb of flies.|הֶ֣עָרֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb But on that|הַה֜וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb I will give special treatment|וְהִפְלֵיתִי֩\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen,|גֹּ֗שֶׁן\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb live;|עֹמֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb no|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb swarms of flies|עָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb will be found|הֱיֽוֹת־\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb In this way|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you will know|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I,|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb am in|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb a distinction|פְדֻ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 8:23 \ft LXX and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa I will set redemption\f* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and your people.|עַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb This|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb sign|הָאֹ֥ת\rb* \rb will take place|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb tomorrow.’”|לְמָחָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb so.|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb Thick|כָּבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb swarms of flies|עָרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb poured|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb into Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥יתָה\rb* \rb and into the houses|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of his officials.|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb Throughout|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb was ruined|תִּשָּׁחֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb by|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb swarms of flies.|הֶעָרֹֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וּֽלְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Go,|לְכ֛וּ\rb* \rb sacrifice|זִבְח֥וּ\rb* \rb to your God|לֵֽאלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb within this land.”|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “It would not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be right|נָכוֹן֙\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb that,|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the sacrifices we offer|נִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb would be detestable|תּוֹעֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the Egyptians.|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb we offer sacrifices|נִזְבַּ֞ח\rb* \rb that are|אֶת־\rb* \rb detestable|תּוֹעֲבַ֥ת\rb* \rb before|לְעֵינֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the Egyptians,|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb will they not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb stone us?|יִסְקְלֻֽנוּ׃\rb* \v 27 \rb We must make|נֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb a three-day|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb into the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְזָבַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He commands us.”|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb answered,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb will let you go|אֲשַׁלַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וּזְבַחְתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb but|רַ֛ק\rb* \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go|לָלֶ֑כֶת\rb* \rb very far.|הַרְחֵ֥ק\rb*\rb |תַרְחִ֖יקוּ\rb* \rb Now pray|הַעְתִּ֖ירוּ\rb* \rb for me.”|בַּעֲדִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb “As soon as I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb leave you,”|יוֹצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמָּךְ֙\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I will pray|וְהַעְתַּרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb so that tomorrow|מָחָ֑ר\rb* \rb the swarms of flies|הֶעָרֹ֗ב\rb* \rb will depart|וְסָ֣ר\rb* \rb from Pharaoh|מִפַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb* \rb and his officials|מֵעֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb and his people.|וּמֵעַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb But|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb must not|אַל־\rb* \rb act deceitfully|הָתֵ֔ל\rb* \rb again|יֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb by refusing|לְבִלְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to let the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb go|שַׁלַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and prayed|וַיֶּעְתַּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 31 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb as Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb requested.|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb He removed|וַיָּ֙סַר֙\rb* \rb the swarms of flies|הֶעָרֹ֔ב\rb* \rb from Pharaoh|מִפַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb and his officials|מֵעֲבָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb and his people;|וּמֵעַמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb one fly|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb remained.|נִשְׁאַ֖ר\rb* \v 32 \rb But Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|וַיַּכְבֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb time|בַּפַּ֣עַם\rb* \rb as well,|גַּ֖ם\rb* \rb and he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb let the people|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb go.|שִׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\c 9
\s1 The Fifth Plague: Livestock
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Go|בֹּ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and tell him|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews,|הָֽעִבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Let My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb* \v 2 \rb But|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb continue|וְעוֹדְךָ֖\rb* \rb to restrain|מַחֲזִ֥יק\rb* \rb them|בָּֽם׃\rb* \rb and refuse|מָאֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to let them go,|לְשַׁלֵּ֑חַ\rb* \v 3 \rb then|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb will bring|הוֹיָ֗ה\rb* \rb a severe|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb plague|דֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb on your livestock|בְּמִקְנְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the field—|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb on your horses,|בַּסּוּסִ֤ים\rb* \rb donkeys,|בַּֽחֲמֹרִים֙\rb* \rb camels,|בַּגְּמַלִּ֔ים\rb* \rb herds,|בַּבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb and flocks.|וּבַצֹּ֑אן\rb* \v 4 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will make a distinction|וְהִפְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb the livestock|מִקְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb and the livestock|מִקְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb so that no animal|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb belonging to|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will die.’”|יָמ֛וּת\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb set|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb a time,|מוֹעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb in the land.”|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And the next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb just that.|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb All|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the livestock|מִקְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb but not|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb animal|וּמִמִּקְנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb belonging to the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb died.|מֵ֥ת\rb* \v 7 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb sent officials|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb and found that|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb none|לֹא־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb of the livestock|מִמִּקְנֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb of the Israelites|עַד־\rb* \rb had died.|מֵ֛ת\rb* \rb But Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb was hardened,|וַיִּכְבַּד֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:7 \ft Or \fqa made heavy\ft ; also in verse 34\f* \rb and he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb let the people|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb go.|שִׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 The Sixth Plague: Boils
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹן֒\rb* \rb “Take|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb handfuls|מְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |חָפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb of soot|פִּ֖יחַ\rb* \rb from the furnace;|כִּבְשָׁ֑ן\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh,|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb is to toss it|וּזְרָק֥וֹ\rb* \rb into the air.|הַשָּׁמַ֖יְמָה\rb* \v 9 \rb It will become|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb fine dust|לְאָבָ֔ק\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all the|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb festering|אֲבַעְבֻּעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb boils|לִשְׁחִ֥ין\rb* \rb will break out|פֹּרֵ֛חַ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and beast|הַבְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land.”|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So they took|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb soot|פִּ֣יחַ\rb* \rb from the furnace|הַכִּבְשָׁ֗ן\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh.|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb tossed|וַיִּזְרֹ֥ק\rb* \rb it|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb into the air,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יְמָה\rb* \rb and|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb festering|אֲבַעְבֻּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb boils|שְׁחִין֙\rb* \rb broke out|פֹּרֵ֕חַ\rb* \rb on man|בָּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and beast.|וּבַבְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb The magicians|הַֽחַרְטֻמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb could|יָכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb stand|לַעֲמֹ֛ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb because|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the boils|הַשְּׁחִ֑ין\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הַשְּׁחִ֔ין\rb* \rb had broken out|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb on them|בַּֽחֲרְטֻמִּ֖ם\rb* \rb and on all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|וַיְחַזֵּ֤ק\rb*\f + \fr 9:12 \ft Or \fqa stiffened \ft or \fqa strengthened\ft ; also in verse 35\f* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb heart,|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Seventh Plague: Hail
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Get up early|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb stand|וְהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and tell him|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews,|הָֽעִבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Let My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Otherwise,|כִּ֣י׀\rb*\rb |בַּפַּ֣עַם\rb*\rb |הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb will send|שֹׁלֵ֜חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My plagues|מַגֵּפֹתַי֙\rb* \rb against|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb you|לִבְּךָ֔\rb*\f + \fr 9:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa against your heart \ft or \fqa against your inner man\f* \rb and your officials|וּבַעֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and your people,|וּבְעַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so|בַּעֲב֣וּר\rb* \rb you may know|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb like Me|כָּמֹ֖נִי\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb by this time|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb I could have stretched out|שָׁלַ֣חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb and struck|וָאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֛\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb your people|עַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb with a plague|בַּדָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb to wipe you|וַתִּכָּחֵ֖ד\rb* \rb off|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb But|וְאוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb I have raised you up|הֶעֱמַדְתִּ֔יךָ\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \ft Or \fqa have spared you\f* \rb for this very purpose,|זֹאת֙\rb*\rb |בַּעֲב֥וּר\rb* \rb that|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb I might display|הַרְאֹתְךָ֣\rb* \rb My power|כֹּחִ֑י\rb* \rb to you,|אֶת־\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \ft LXX \fqa in you\f* \rb and that|וּלְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb might be proclaimed|סַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 9:17|ROM 9:17\ref*\f* \v 17 \rb Still,|עוֹדְךָ֖\rb* \rb you lord it|מִסְתּוֹלֵ֣ל\rb* \rb over My people|בְּעַמִּ֑י\rb* \rb and do not|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb allow them to go.|שַׁלְּחָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb at this time|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֔ר\rb* \rb I will rain down|מַמְטִיר֙\rb* \rb the worst|כָּבֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb hail|בָּרָ֖ד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has ever|לֹא־\rb* \rb fallen|הָיָ֤ה\rb*\rb |כָמֹ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb on Egypt,|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb it was founded|הִוָּסְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb now.|עָֽתָּה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb give orders now|שְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb to shelter|הָעֵז֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your livestock|מִקְנְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb have in the field.|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֨ם\rb* \rb or beast|וְהַבְּהֵמָ֜ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb remains|יִמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb in the field|בַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and is not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb brought|יֵֽאָסֵף֙\rb* \rb inside|הַבַּ֔יְתָה\rb* \rb will die|וָמֵֽתוּ׃\rb* \rb when the hail|הַבָּרָ֖ד\rb* \rb comes down|וְיָרַ֧ד\rb* \rb upon them.’”|עֲלֵהֶ֛ם\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Those among Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb officials|מֵֽעַבְדֵ֖י\rb* \rb who feared|הַיָּרֵא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb hurried to bring|הֵנִ֛יס\rb* \rb their servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and livestock|מִקְנֵ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb shelter,|הַבָּתִּֽים׃\rb* \v 21 \rb but those who|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb disregarded|שָׂ֛ם\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb*\rb |לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb left|וַֽיַּעֲזֹ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and livestock|מִקְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the field.|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה\rb* \rb “Stretch out|נְטֵ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb heaven,|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that hail|בָרָ֖ד\rb* \rb may fall|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb on all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt—|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֣ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and beast|הַבְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְעַ֛ל\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֥שֶׂב\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb throughout the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּ֨ט\rb* \rb his staff|מַטֵּהוּ֮\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb heaven,|הַשָּׁמַיִם֒\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb sent|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb thunder|קֹלֹת֙\rb* \rb and hail,|וּבָרָ֔ד\rb* \rb and lightning|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb struck|וַתִּ֥הֲלַךְ\rb* \rb the earth.|אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb rained down|וַיַּמְטֵ֧ר\rb* \rb hail|בָּרָ֖ד\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb The hail|בָרָ֔ד\rb* \rb fell|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb and the lightning|וְאֵ֕שׁ\rb* \rb continued flashing|מִתְלַקַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb through it.|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb The hail|הַבָּרָ֑ד\rb* \rb was so|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb severe|כָּבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb like it|כָמֹ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb had ever been seen|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from the time|מֵאָ֖ז\rb* \rb it became|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a nation.|לְגֽוֹי׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the hail|הַבָּרָ֜ד\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the field,|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb both man|מֵאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb beast;|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb it|הַבָּרָ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb beat down|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֤שֶׂב\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb and stripped|שִׁבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb tree.|עֵ֥ץ\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \v 26 \rb The only|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb place where it did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb hail|בָּרָֽד׃\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen,|גֹּ֔שֶׁן\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb lived.|שָׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron.|וּֽלְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “This time|הַפָּ֑עַם\rb* \rb I have sinned,”|חָטָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb he said.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is righteous,|הַצַּדִּ֔יק\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb and my people|וְעַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb are wicked.|הָרְשָׁעִֽים׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Pray|הַעְתִּ֙ירוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for there has been|מִֽהְיֹ֛ת\rb* \rb enough|וְרַ֕ב\rb* \rb of God’s|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb thunder|קֹלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and hail.|וּבָרָ֑ד\rb* \rb I will let you go;|וַאֲשַׁלְּחָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb need to stay|לַעֲמֹֽד׃\rb* \rb any longer.”|תֹסִפ֖וּן\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “When I have left|כְּצֵאתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb I will spread out|אֶפְרֹ֥שׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my hands|כַּפַּ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb The thunder|הַקֹּל֣וֹת\rb* \rb will cease,|יֶחְדָּל֗וּן\rb* \rb and there will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb more|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb hail,|וְהַבָּרָד֙\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may know|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb is the LORD’s.|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \v 30 \rb But as for you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and your officials,|וַעֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you still do not|טֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb fear|תִּֽירְא֔וּן\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.”|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb (Now the flax|וְהַפִּשְׁתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and barley|וְהַשְּׂעֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb were destroyed,|נֻכָּ֑תָה\rb* \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the barley|הַשְּׂעֹרָה֙\rb*\rb |אָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb was ripe and the flax|וְהַפִּשְׁתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was in bloom;|גִּבְעֹֽל׃\rb* \v 32 \rb but the wheat|וְהַחִטָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and spelt|וְהַכֻּסֶּ֖מֶת\rb* \rb were not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroyed,|נֻכּ֑וּ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb are late crops.)|אֲפִילֹ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֤ם\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb went out of the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and spread out|וַיִּפְרֹ֥שׂ\rb* \rb his hands|כַּפָּ֖יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb The thunder|הַקֹּלוֹת֙\rb* \rb and hail|וְהַבָּרָ֔ד\rb* \rb ceased,|וַֽיַּחְדְּל֤וּ\rb* \rb and the rain|וּמָטָ֖ר\rb* \rb no longer|לֹא־\rb* \rb poured down|נִתַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb on the land.|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb When Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the rain|הַמָּטָ֧ר\rb* \rb and hail|וְהַבָּרָ֛ד\rb* \rb and thunder|וְהַקֹּלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb had ceased,|חָדַ֨ל\rb* \rb he sinned|לַחֲטֹ֑א\rb* \rb again|וַיֹּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and hardened|וַיַּכְבֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb his heart—|לִבּ֖וֹ\rb*  \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and his officials.|וַעֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb* \v 35 \rb So Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb was hardened,|וַֽיֶּחֱזַק֙\rb* \rb and he would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb let the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb go,|שִׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\c 10
\s1 The Eighth Plague: Locusts
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Go|בֹּ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb have hardened|הִכְבַּ֤דְתִּי\rb*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Or \fqa made heavy\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the hearts|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of his officials,|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb I may perform|שִׁתִ֛י\rb* \rb these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb miraculous signs of Mine|אֹתֹתַ֥י\rb* \rb among them,|בְּקִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and that|וּלְמַ֡עַן\rb* \rb you may tell|תְּסַפֵּר֩\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb your children|בִנְךָ֜\rb* \rb and grandchildren|וּבֶן־\rb*\rb |בִּנְךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb severely I dealt|הִתְעַלַּ֙לְתִּי֙\rb* \rb with the Egyptians|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb when I performed|שַׂ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb miraculous signs|אֹתֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb among them,|בָ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb so that all of you may know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹן֮\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֒\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Hebrews,|הָֽעִבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֣י\rb* \rb will you refuse|מֵאַ֔נְתָּ\rb* \rb to humble yourself|לֵעָנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb before Me?|מִפָּנָ֑י\rb* \rb Let My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb so that they may worship Me.|וְיַֽעַבְדֻֽנִי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb But|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb refuse|מָאֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to let My people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb go,|לְשַׁלֵּ֣חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb locusts|אַרְבֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb into your territory|בִּגְבֻלֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb tomorrow.|מָחָ֛ר\rb* \v 5 \rb They will cover|וְכִסָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the face|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb so that no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb one can|יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb They will devour|וְאָכַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb whatever is|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb left|הַנִּשְׁאֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb after|הַפְּלֵטָ֗ה\rb* \rb the hail|הַבָּרָ֔ד\rb* \rb and eat|וְאָכַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb tree|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb that grows|הַצֹּמֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb in your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb fields.|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb They will fill|וּמָלְא֨וּ\rb* \rb your houses|בָתֶּ֜יךָ\rb* \rb and the houses|וּבָתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb your officials|עֲבָדֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb and|וּבָתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb Egyptian—|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb something|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb nor your grandfathers|וַאֲב֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb have seen|רָא֤וּ\rb* \rb since the day|מִיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb they came into|הֱיוֹתָם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb this land.’”|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb Then Moses turned|וַיִּ֥פֶן\rb* \rb and left|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s presence.|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb officials|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb asked him,|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb “How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַי֙\rb* \rb will this|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb man be|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb to us?|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb Let the people|הָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may worship|וְיַֽעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Do you not yet realize|תֵּדַ֔ע\rb*\rb |הֲטֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb lies in ruins?”|אָבְדָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb were brought back|וַיּוּשַׁ֞ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh.|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb “Go,|לְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb worship|עִבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,”|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb he said.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “But who exactly|מִ֥י\rb*\rb |וָמִ֖י\rb* \rb will be going?”|הַהֹלְכִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb “We will go|נֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb with our young|בִּנְעָרֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and old,”|וּבִזְקֵנֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “We will go|נֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb with our sons|בְּבָנֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבִבְנוֹתֵ֜נוּ\rb* \rb and with our flocks|בְּצֹאנֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb and herds,|וּבִבְקָרֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we must hold a feast|חַג־\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then Pharaoh|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb told them,|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |כֵ֤ן\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֨י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb if I ever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb let you go|אֲשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb with your little ones.|טַפְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Clearly|רְא֕וּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you are bent|נֶ֥גֶד\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb on evil.|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \v 11 \rb No,|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb only the men|הַגְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb may go|לְכֽוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb and worship|וְעִבְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb that is what you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have been requesting.”|מְבַקְשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb And Moses and Aaron were driven|וַיְגָ֣רֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹֽה׃פ\rb* \rb presence.|פְּנֵ֥י\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Stretch out|נְטֵ֨ה\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֜\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb so that the locusts|בָּֽאַרְבֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb may swarm|וְיַ֖עַל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb it|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and devour|וְיֹאכַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֣שֶׂב\rb* \rb in the land—|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the hail|הַבָּרָֽד׃\rb* \rb has left behind.”|הִשְׁאִ֖יר\rb*
