\p \v 16 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb quickly|וַיְמַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb summoned|לִקְרֹ֖א\rb* \rb Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וּֽלְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “I have sinned|חָטָ֛אתִי\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and against you.|וְלָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb forgive|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb my sin|חַטָּאתִי֙\rb* \rb once more|אַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |הַפַּ֔עַם\rb* \rb and appeal|וְהַעְתִּ֖ירוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb that He may remove|וְיָסֵר֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb death|הַמָּ֥וֶת\rb* \rb from me.”|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*\rb |רַ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb So Moses left|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb presence and appealed|וַיֶּעְתַּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb changed the wind|וַיַּהֲפֹ֨ךְ\rb* \rb to a very strong|חָזָ֣ק\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb west|יָם֙\rb* \rb wind|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb that carried off|וַיִּשָּׂא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the locusts|הָ֣אַרְבֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb and blew them|וַיִּתְקָעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb into the Red|סּ֑וּף\rb* \rb Sea.|יָ֣מָּה\rb*\f + \fr 10:19 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb Not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb locust|אַרְבֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb remained|נִשְׁאַר֙\rb* \rb anywhere|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb in|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
