\s1 The Ninth Plague: Darkness
\p \v 21 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Stretch out|נְטֵ֤ה\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb heaven,|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that darkness|חֹ֖שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb may spread|וִ֥יהִי\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt—|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*  \rb a palpable|וְיָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb darkness.”|חֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb heaven,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and total|אֲפֵלָ֛ה\rb* \rb darkness|חֹֽשֶׁךְ־\rb* \rb covered|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days.|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 23 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb could see|רָא֞וּ\rb* \rb anyone else,|אָחִ֗יו\rb* \rb and for three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb no one|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb left|קָ֛מוּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb his place.|מִתַּחְתָּ֖יו\rb* \rb Yet all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb light|א֖וֹר\rb* \rb in their dwellings.|בְּמוֹשְׁבֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Go,|לְכוּ֙\rb* \rb worship|עִבְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb Even|גַּֽם־\rb* \rb your little ones|טַפְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb may go|יֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with you;|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb only|רַ֛ק\rb* \rb your flocks|צֹאנְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and herds|וּבְקַרְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb must stay behind.”|יֻצָּ֑ג\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb must also|גַּם־\rb* \rb provide us|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb with|בְּיָדֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֣ים\rb* \rb and burnt offerings|וְעֹל֑וֹת\rb* \rb to present|וְעָשִׂ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God.|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb our livestock|מִקְנֵ֜נוּ\rb* \rb must go|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with us;|עִמָּ֗נוּ\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb a hoof|פַּרְסָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be left behind,|תִשָּׁאֵר֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb we will need|נִקַּ֔ח\rb* \rb some of them|מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb to worship|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and we will|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|נֵדַ֗ע\rb* \rb how|מַֽה־\rb* \rb we are to worship|נַּעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb we arrive.”|בֹּאֵ֖נוּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|וַיְחַזֵּ֥ק\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb heart,|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and he was unwilling|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to let them go.|לְשַׁלְּחָֽם׃\rb* \v 28 \rb “Depart|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb from me!”|מֵעָלָ֑י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb to Moses.|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb “Make sure|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb never|אֶל־\rb* \rb see|רְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb my face|פָּנַ֔י\rb* \rb again,|תֹּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֛וֹם\rb* \rb you see|רְאֹתְךָ֥\rb* \rb my face,|פָנַ֖י\rb* \rb you will die.”|תָּמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb “As|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you say,”|דִּבַּ֑רְתָּ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb “I will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb see|רְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb* \rb again.”|אֹסִ֥ף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*
\c 11
\s1 The Plague on the Firstborn Foretold
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “I will bring|אָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb more|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb plague.|נֶ֤גַע\rb* \rb After|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that,|כֵ֕ן\rb* \rb he will allow you to leave|יְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb this place.|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb And when he lets you go,|כְּשַׁ֨לְּח֔וֹ\rb* \rb he will drive you out|גָּרֵ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |יְגָרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb completely.|כָּלָ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Now|נָ֖א\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb announce|דַּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb that men|אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and women alike|וְאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb should ask|וְיִשְׁאֲל֞וּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb their neighbors|רְעוּתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb for articles|כְּלֵי־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֖סֶף\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb and gold.”|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Egyptians.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Moreover,|גַּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb himself|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb was highly|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb regarded|גָּד֤וֹל\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb by|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb officials|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb* \rb and by the people.|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb declared,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘About midnight|כַּחֲצֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will go|יוֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb throughout|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb firstborn son|בְּכוֹר֮\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb will die,|וּמֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the firstborn|מִבְּכ֤וֹר\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb who sits|הַיֹּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his throne,|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the servant girl|הַשִּׁפְחָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb behind|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the hand mill,|הָרֵחָ֑יִם\rb* \rb as well as the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the cattle.|בְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Then a great|גְדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb cry|צְעָקָ֥ה\rb* \rb will go out|וְהָֽיְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Such|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb an outcry|כָּמֹ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb has never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb been heard before|נִהְיָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be heard|וְכָמֹ֖הוּ\rb* \rb again.|תֹסִֽף׃\rb* \v 7 \rb But among all|וּלְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb even a dog|כֶּ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |לְשֹׁנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb will snarl|יֶֽחֱרַץ־\rb* \rb at man|לְמֵאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb or beast.’|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 11:7 \ft Some translators close this quotation at the end of the verse.\f*
\p \rb Then|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb you will know|תֵּֽדְע֔וּן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb makes a distinction|יַפְלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb officials|עֲבָדֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb of yours will come|וְיָרְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֜י\rb* \rb and bow|וְהִשְׁתַּֽחֲוּוּ־\rb* \rb before me,|לִ֣י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Go,|צֵ֤א\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb follow you!’|בְּרַגְלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that,|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb I will depart.”|אֵצֵ֑א\rb*
\p \rb And hot|בָּחֳרִי־\rb* \rb with anger,|אָֽף׃ס\rb* \rb Moses left|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb presence.|מֵֽעִם־\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to you,|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb My wonders|מוֹפְתַ֖י\rb* \rb may be multiplied|רְב֥וֹת\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb wonders|הַמֹּפְתִ֥ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh,|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb but the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|וַיְחַזֵּ֤ק\rb*\f + \fr 11:10 \ft Or \fqa stiffened \ft or \fqa strengthened\f* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb so that he would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb let the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb go out|שִׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of his land.|מֵאַרְצֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\c 12
\s1 The First Passover
\r \ref Numbers 9:1–14|NUM 9:1-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “This|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֧דֶשׁ\rb* \rb is the beginning|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of months|חֳדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb for you;|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb it shall be|הוּא֙\rb* \rb the first|רִאשׁ֥וֹן\rb* \rb month|לְחָדְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of your|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb year.|הַשָּׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Tell|דַּבְּר֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb that on the tenth|בֶּעָשֹׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day of this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb each man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb must select|וְיִקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb a lamb|שֶׂ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft The Hebrew word can mean \fqa lamb \ft or \fqa kid\ft ; also in verses 4 and 5.\f* \rb for his family,|אָבֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |לְבֵית־\rb* \rb one|שֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb per household.|לַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \v 4 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the household|הַבַּיִת֮\rb*\rb |מִהְיֹ֣ת\rb* \rb is too small|יִמְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb for a whole lamb,|מִשֶּׂה֒\rb* \rb they are to|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb share with|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb the nearest|הַקָּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb neighbor|וּשְׁכֵנ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb based on the number|בְּמִכְסַ֣ת\rb* \rb of people,|נְפָשֹׁ֑ת\rb* \rb and apportion|תָּכֹ֖סּוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the lamb|הַשֶּֽׂה׃\rb* \rb accordingly.|אִ֚ישׁ\rb*\rb |אָכְל֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Your|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb lamb|שֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb must be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb male,|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb and you may take|תִּקָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb it from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sheep|הַכְּבָשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb or the goats.|הָעִזִּ֖ים\rb* \v 6 \rb You must|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb keep|לְמִשְׁמֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb it|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the fourteenth|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb month,|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb when the whole|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the congregation|עֲדַֽת־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will slaughter|וְשָׁחֲט֣וּ\rb* \rb the animals|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb twilight.|הָעַרְבָּֽיִם׃\rb*\f + \fr 12:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings\f* \v 7 \rb They are to take|וְלָֽקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and put|וְנָֽתְנ֛וּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb the sides|הַמְּזוּזֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb tops of the doorframes|הַמַּשְׁק֑וֹף\rb*\f + \fr 12:7 \ft Literally \fqa on the two doorposts and on the lintel\ft ; similarly in verses 22 and 23\f* \rb of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the houses|הַבָּ֣תִּ֔ים\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they eat the lambs.|יֹאכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb They are to eat|וְאָכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb that|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb night,|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb roasted|צְלִי־\rb* \rb over the fire,|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb along with unleavened bread|וּמַצּ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and bitter herbs.|מְרֹרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |יֹאכְלֻֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb eat|תֹּאכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb any of|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb the meat raw|נָ֔א\rb* \rb or cooked|מְבֻשָּׁ֖ל\rb* \rb in boiling|וּבָשֵׁ֥ל\rb* \rb water,|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb but only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb roasted|צְלִי־\rb* \rb over the fire—|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשׁ֥וֹ\rb* \rb and|עַל־\rb* \rb legs|כְּרָעָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and inner parts.|קִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb leave|תוֹתִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb any of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning;|בֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb the morning|בֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb you must burn up|בָּאֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׂרֹֽפוּ׃\rb* \rb any part|מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb that is left over.|וְהַנֹּתָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb This is how|וְכָכָה֮\rb* \rb you are to eat it:|תֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֒\rb* \rb You must be fully dressed for travel,|מָתְנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 12:11 \ft Literally \fqa Gird up your loins\f* \rb |חֲגֻרִ֔ים\rb*\rb with your sandals|נַֽעֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb on your feet|בְּרַגְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and your staff|וּמַקֶּלְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in your hand.|בְּיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb You are to eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in haste;|בְּחִפָּז֔וֹן\rb* \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is the LORD’s|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb Passover.|פֶּ֥סַח\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb On that|הַזֶּה֒\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb I will pass|וְעָבַרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb through the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֮\rb* \rb and strike down|וְהִכֵּיתִ֤י\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb firstborn male,|בְּכוֹר֙\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb both man|מֵאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb beast,|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and I will execute|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb judgment|שְׁפָטִ֖ים\rb* \rb against all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb The blood|הַדָּ֨ם\rb* \rb on|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb the houses|הַבָּתִּים֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are staying|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb a sign;|לְאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb when I see|וְרָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blood,|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb I will pass|וּפָסַחְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb over you.|עֲלֵכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb No|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb plague|נֶ֙גֶף֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb on you|בָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb to destroy you|לְמַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb* \rb when I strike|בְּהַכֹּתִ֖י\rb* \rb the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\s1 The Feast of Unleavened Bread
\r \ref Leviticus 23:4–8|LEV 23:4-8\ref*; \ref Numbers 28:16–25|NUM 28:16-25\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 16:1–8|DEU 16:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb And this|הַזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb a memorial|לְזִכָּר֔וֹן\rb* \rb for you,|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb and you are to celebrate|וְחַגֹּתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb as a feast|חַ֣ג\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |תְּחָגֻּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \v 15 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb you must eat|תֹּאכֵ֔לוּ\rb*\rb |אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb unleavened bread.|מַצּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb On the first|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you are to remove|תַּשְׁבִּ֥יתוּ\rb* \rb the leaven|שְּׂאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb from your houses.|מִבָּתֵּיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb eats|אֹכֵ֣ל\rb* \rb anything leavened|חָמֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb from the first|הָרִאשֹׁ֖ן\rb* \rb day|מִיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb through|עַד־\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִֽי׃\rb*\rb |י֥וֹם\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֞ה\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֤פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִוא֙\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb On the first|הָרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb you are to hold|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assembly,|מִקְרָא־\rb* \rb and another|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |מִקְרָא־\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day.|וּבַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb You must|בָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb do|יֵעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb any work|מְלָאכָה֙\rb* \rb on those days,|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb except to prepare|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the meals—|יֵאָכֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb*  \rb that|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is all|לְבַדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb you may do.|יֵעָשֶׂ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb So you are to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast of Unleavened Bread,|הַמַּצּוֹת֒\rb*\f + \fr 12:17 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten\f* \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb very|בְּעֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I brought|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb* \rb your divisions|צִבְאוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb You must keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \v 18 \rb In the first month|בָּרִאשֹׁ֡ן\rb* \rb you are to eat|תֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb unleavened bread,|מַצֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb from the evening|בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb of the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb day|י֤וֹם\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb* \rb the evening|בָּעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb of the twenty-first|הָאֶחָ֧ד\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֛ים\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day.|י֣וֹם\rb* \v 19 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb there must be no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leaven|שְׂאֹ֕ר\rb* \rb found|יִמָּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb in your houses.|בְּבָתֵּיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb If|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb eats|אֹכֵ֣ל\rb* \rb something leavened,|מַחְמֶ֗צֶת\rb* \rb that|הַהִוא֙\rb* \rb person,|הַנֶּ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb whether a foreigner|בַּגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb or native|וּבְאֶזְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֞ה\rb* \rb from the congregation|מֵעֲדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \v 20 \rb You are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to eat|תֹאכֵ֑לוּ\rb* \rb anything|כָּל־\rb* \rb leavened;|מַחְמֶ֖צֶת\rb* \rb eat|תֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb your homes.”|מוֹשְׁבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “Go at once|מִֽשְׁכ֗וּ\rb* \rb and select|וּקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb a lamb|צֹ֛אן\rb* \rb for each family,|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשַׁחֲט֥וּ\rb* \rb the Passover lamb.|הַפָּֽסַח׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Take|וּלְקַחְתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb a cluster|אֲגֻדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of hyssop,|אֵז֗וֹב\rb* \rb dip|וּטְבַלְתֶּם֮\rb* \rb it into the blood|בַּדָּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the basin,|בַּסַּף֒\rb* \rb and brush|וְהִגַּעְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בַּסָּ֑ף\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the top|הַמַּשְׁקוֹף֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb sides of the doorframe.|הַמְּזוּזֹ֔ת\rb* \rb None|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of you|וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb shall go out|תֵצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb the door|מִפֶּֽתַח־\rb* \rb of his house|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb passes through|וְעָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb to strike down|לִנְגֹּ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians,|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb He will see|וְרָאָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the top|הַמַּשְׁק֔וֹף\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb sides of the doorframe|הַמְּזוּזֹ֑ת\rb*\rb |יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and will pass|וּפָסַ֤ח\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb that doorway;|הַפֶּ֔תַח\rb* \rb so He will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb allow|יִתֵּן֙\rb* \rb the destroyer|הַמַּשְׁחִ֔ית\rb* \rb to enter|לָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your houses|בָּתֵּיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and strike you down.|לִנְגֹּֽף׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And you are to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb command|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb as a|עַד־\rb* \rb permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb statute|לְחָק־\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb and your descendants.|וּלְבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 25 \rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will give|יִתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He promised,|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb you are to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb service.|הָעֲבֹדָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your children|בְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb ask you,|יֹאמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb ‘What|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb does this service|הָעֲבֹדָ֥ה\rb* \rb mean|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb to you?’|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 27 \rb you are to reply,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֡ם\rb* \rb ‘It|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb is the Passover|פֶּ֨סַח\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶֽבַח־\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb passed|פָּ֠סַח\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the houses|בָּתֵּ֤י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb when He struck down|בְּנָגְפּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb the Egyptians|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and spared|הִצִּ֑יל\rb* \rb our homes.’”|בָּתֵּ֣ינוּ\rb*
\p \rb Then the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb bowed down|וַיִּקֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb and worshiped.|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוּֽוּ׃\rb* \v 28 \rb And the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb just what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb and Aaron.|וְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |עָשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Tenth Plague: Death of the Firstborn
\p \v 29 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb at midnight|בַּחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֮\rb* \rb struck down|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכוֹר֮\rb* \rb male in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb from the firstborn|מִבְּכֹ֤ר\rb* \rb of Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb who sat|הַיֹּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his throne,|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the prisoner|הַשְּׁבִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the dungeon,|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַבּ֑וֹר\rb* \rb as well as all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb among the livestock.|בְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb During the night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֜ה\rb* \rb got up—|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb*  \rb he|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb the Egyptians—|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*  \rb and there was|וַתְּהִ֛י\rb* \rb loud|גְדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb wailing|צְעָקָ֥ה\rb* \rb in Egypt;|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb for there was no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb house|בַּ֔יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb someone dead.|מֵֽת׃\rb*
\s1 The Exodus Begins
\p \v 31 \rb Then Pharaoh summoned|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וּֽלְאַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb by night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Get up,|ק֤וּמוּ\rb* \rb leave|צְּאוּ֙\rb*\rb |מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb my people,|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb the Israelites!|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Go,|וּלְכ֛וּ\rb* \rb worship|עִבְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb as you have requested.|כְּדַבֶּרְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 32 \rb Take|קְח֛וּ\rb* \rb your flocks|צֹאנְכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb herds|בְּקַרְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb as well,|גַּם־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have said,|דִּבַּרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and depart!|וָלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb And bless|וּבֵֽרַכְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִֽי׃\rb* \rb also.”|גַּם־\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb And in order to send them|לְשַׁלְּחָ֣ם\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb quickly,|לְמַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb urged|וַתֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb the people on.|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “For otherwise,”|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they said,|אָמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “we are all|כֻּלָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb going to die!”|מֵתִֽים׃\rb* \v 34 \rb So the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb their dough|בְּצֵק֖וֹ\rb* \rb before|טֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb it was leavened,|יֶחְמָ֑ץ\rb* \rb carrying it on|עַל־\rb* \rb their shoulders|שִׁכְמָֽם׃\rb* \rb in kneading bowls|מִשְׁאֲרֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb wrapped|צְרֻרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb in clothing.|בְּשִׂמְלֹתָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb Furthermore, the Israelites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb acted|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb on Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb and asked|וַֽיִּשְׁאֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb for articles|כְּלֵי־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֛סֶף\rb* \rb and|וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and for clothing.|וּשְׂמָלֹֽת׃\rb* \v 36 \rb And the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb such favor|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb that they granted their request.|וַיַּשְׁאִל֑וּם\rb* \rb In this way they plundered|וַֽיְנַצְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb journeyed|וַיִּסְע֧וּ\rb* \rb from Rameses|מֵרַעְמְסֵ֖ס\rb* \rb to Succoth|סֻכֹּ֑תָה\rb*\f + \fr 12:37 \fqa Succoth \ft means \fqa booths \ft or \fqa shelters \ft or \fqa tabernacles\ft .\f* \rb with about 600,000|כְּשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֨וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֧לֶף\rb* \rb men|הַגְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb on foot,|רַגְלִ֛י\rb* \rb besides|לְבַ֥ד\rb* \rb women and children.|מִטָּֽף׃\rb* \v 38 \rb And a mixed|עֵ֥רֶב\rb* \rb multitude|רַ֖ב\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb went up|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb with them,|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb along with great droves of|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb livestock,|מִקְנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb both flocks|וְצֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and herds.|וּבָקָ֔ר\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb Since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb their dough|הַבָּצֵ֜ק\rb* \rb had no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb leaven,|חָמֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb the people baked|וַיֹּאפ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb what they had brought|הוֹצִ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb into unleavened|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb loaves.|עֻגֹ֥ת\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb when they had been driven out|גֹרְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb they could|יָֽכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb delay|לְהִתְמַהְמֵ֔הַּ\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb prepared|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb any provisions|צֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb for themselves.|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 40 \rb Now the duration|וּמוֹשַׁב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites’|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb stay|יָשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 12:40 \ft MT; SP \fqa in Canaan and Egypt\ft ; LXX \fqa in Egypt and Canaan\f* \rb was 430|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \v 41 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb At the end|מִקֵּץ֙\rb* \rb of the 430|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb very|בְּעֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb day,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb divisions|צִבְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb went out|יָֽצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 42 \rb Because the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb kept a vigil|שִׁמֻּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb that|הוּא֙\rb* \rb night|לֵ֣יל\rb* \rb to bring them|לְהוֹצִיאָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |הֽוּא־\rb* \rb this same|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb night is to be a vigil|הַלַּ֤יְלָה\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to be observed|שִׁמֻּרִ֛ים\rb* \rb by all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתָֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 Instructions for the Passover
\p \v 43 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb is the statute|חֻקַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Passover:|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb* \rb No|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb foreigner|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֖ר\rb* \rb is to eat|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb of it.|בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 44 \rb But any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb slave who|עֶ֥בֶד\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb has been purchased|מִקְנַת־\rb*\rb |כָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb may eat|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb of it,|בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb after you have circumcised him.|וּמַלְתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אָ֖ז\rb* \v 45 \rb A temporary resident|תּוֹשָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb or hired hand|וְשָׂכִ֖יר\rb* \rb shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb eat|יֹ֥אכַל־\rb* \rb the Passover.|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 46 \rb It must be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb inside one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb house.|בְּבַ֤יִת\rb* \rb You are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to take|תוֹצִ֧יא\rb* \rb any of|מִן־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb outside|מִן־\rb*\rb |ח֑וּצָה\rb* \rb the house,|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb and you may not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb break|תִשְׁבְּרוּ־\rb* \rb any of the bones.|וְעֶ֖צֶם\rb*
\p \v 47 \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb must celebrate|יַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb it.|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 48 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֗ר\rb* \rb resides|יָג֨וּר\rb* \rb with|אִתְּךָ֜\rb* \rb you and wants to celebrate|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַיהוָה֒\rb* \rb Passover,|פֶסַח֮\rb* \rb all the|כָל־\rb* \rb males in the household|זָכָ֗ר\rb* \rb must be circumcised;|הִמּ֧וֹל\rb* \rb then|וְאָז֙\rb* \rb he may come near|יִקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb to celebrate it,|לַעֲשֹׂת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he shall be|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb like a native|כְּאֶזְרַ֣ח\rb* \rb of the land.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb But no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb uncircumcised man|עָרֵ֖ל\rb* \rb may eat|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb of it.|בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 49 \rb The same|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb law|תּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb shall apply|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to both the native|לָֽאֶזְרָ֑ח\rb* \rb and the foreigner|וְלַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb who resides|הַגָּ֥ר\rb* \rb among you.”|בְּתוֹכְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 50 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb this—|כֵּ֥ן\rb*  \rb they did|עָשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron.|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \v 51 \rb And|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb on that|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb very|בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|הוֹצִ֨יא\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb their divisions.|צִבְאֹתָֽם׃פ\rb*
