\s1 The Dedication of the Firstborn
\r \ref Deuteronomy 15:19–23|DEU 15:19-23\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Consecrate|קַדֶּשׁ־\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֨י\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb firstborn male.|בְּכ֜וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Cited in \ref Luke 2:23|LUK 2:23\ref*\f* \rb The firstborn|פֶּ֤טֶר\rb* \rb from every|כָּל־\rb* \rb womb|רֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb among the Israelites|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb belongs|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb to Me,|לִ֖י\rb* \rb both of man|בָּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and beast.”|וּבַבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “Remember|זָכ֞וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb day,|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb the day|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you came out|יְצָאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of slavery;|עֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצִ֧יא\rb* \rb of it|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb by the strength|בְּחֹ֣זֶק\rb* \rb of His hand.|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb And nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb leavened|חָמֵֽץ׃\rb* \rb shall be eaten.|יֵאָכֵ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Today,|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb in the month|בְּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib,|הָאָבִֽיב׃\rb*\f + \fr 13:4 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are leaving.|יֹצְאִ֑ים\rb* \v 5 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb when|כִֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb brings|יְבִֽיאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Canaanites,|הַֽ֠כְּנַעֲנִי\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַחִתִּ֨י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָאֱמֹרִ֜י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַחִוִּ֣י\rb* \rb and Jebusites—|וְהַיְבוּסִ֗י\rb*  \rb the land|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb that He would give|לָ֣תֶת\rb* \rb you,|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey—|וּדְבָ֑שׁ\rb*  \rb you shall keep|וְעָבַדְתָּ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb service|הָעֲבֹדָ֥ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb month.|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb you are to eat|תֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb unleavened bread,|מַצֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb and on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb there shall be a feast|חַ֖ג\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Unleavened bread|מַצּוֹת֙\rb* \rb shall be eaten|יֵֽאָכֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb during those seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days.|הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb Nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb leavened|חָמֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb may be found|יֵרָאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb among you,|לְךָ֜\rb* \rb nor shall|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb leaven|שְׂאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb be found|יֵרָאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb anywhere within|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb borders.|גְּבֻלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And on that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb you are to explain|וְהִגַּדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to your son,|לְבִנְךָ֔\rb* \rb ‘This is because of|בַּעֲב֣וּר\rb* \rb what|זֶ֗ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb when I came out|בְּצֵאתִ֖י\rb* \rb of Egypt.’|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb It shall be|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֜וֹת\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֨\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֗\rb* \rb and a reminder|וּלְזִכָּרוֹן֙\rb* \rb on your forehead|בֵּ֣ין\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb the Law|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is to be|תִּהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb on your lips.|בְּפִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֣ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצִֽאֲךָ֥\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Therefore you shall keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb statute|הַחֻקָּ֥ה\rb* \rb at the appointed time|לְמוֹעֲדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb year|מִיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb after year.|יָמִֽימָה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb And|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb after|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb brings|יְבִֽאֲךָ֤\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb and gives it|וּנְתָנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to you,|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your fathers,|וְלַֽאֲבֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \v 12 \rb you are to present|וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהֹוָ֑ה\rb* \rb the firstborn male|פֶּֽטֶר־\rb* \rb of every|כָל־\rb* \rb womb.|רֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|פֶּ֣טֶר׀\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֣גֶר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb males|הַזְּכָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of your|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְךָ֛\rb* \rb livestock|בְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb belong to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb You must redeem|תִּפְדֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb firstborn|פֶּ֤טֶר\rb* \rb donkey|חֲמֹר֙\rb* \rb with a lamb,|בְשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb redeem it,|תִפְדֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb you are to break its neck.|וַעֲרַפְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb And every|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb of your sons|בְּבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you must redeem.|תִּפְדֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb In the future,|מָחָ֖ר\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your son|בִנְךָ֛\rb* \rb asks you,|יִשְׁאָלְךָ֥\rb* \rb ‘What|מַה־\rb* \rb does this|זֹּ֑את\rb* \rb mean?’|לֵאמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb ‘With a mighty|בְּחֹ֣זֶק\rb* \rb hand|יָ֗ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought us out|הוֹצִיאָ֧נוּ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֮\rb* \rb stubbornly refused|הִקְשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb to let us go,|לְשַׁלְּחֵנוּ֒\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֤ה\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּהֲרֹ֨ג\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכוֹר֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb both|מִבְּכֹ֥ר\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb beast.|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb This is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֩\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֹבֵ֜חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb the firstborn|פֶּ֤טֶר\rb* \rb male|הַזְּכָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb womb,|רֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb but I redeem|אֶפְדֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of my sons.’|בָּנַ֖י\rb* \v 16 \rb So it shall serve as|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a sign|לְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your hand|יָ֣דְכָ֔ה\rb* \rb and a symbol|וּלְטוֹטָפֹ֖ת\rb* \rb on your forehead,|בֵּ֣ין\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb with a mighty|בְּחֹ֣זֶק\rb* \rb hand|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought us out|הוֹצִיאָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb of Egypt.”|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Pillars of Cloud and Fire
\p \v 17 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb let the people|הָעָם֒\rb* \rb go,|בְּשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb lead them|נָחָ֣ם\rb* \rb along the road|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb through the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines,|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb though|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb was shorter.|קָר֖וֹב\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*\rb |פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb said,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “If the people face|בִּרְאֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb war,|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb they|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb might change their minds|יִנָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb and return|וְשָׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt.”|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb led the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb around|וַיַּסֵּ֨ב\rb* \rb by the way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb toward the Red|ס֑וּף\rb* \rb Sea.|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb And the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb left|עָל֥וּ\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb arrayed for battle.|וַחֲמֻשִׁ֛ים\rb*\f + \fr 13:18 \ft LXX \fqa left the land of Egypt in the fifth generation\f*
\p \v 19 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the bones|עַצְמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb* \rb Joseph had made the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb swear a solemn oath|הַשְׁבֵּ֨עַ\rb*\rb |הִשְׁבִּ֜יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb when he said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb will surely attend to|פָּקֹ֨ד\rb*\rb |יִפְקֹ֤ד\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and then you must carry|וְהַעֲלִיתֶ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמֹתַ֛י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb from this place.”|מִזֶּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:19 \ft \ref Genesis 50:25|GEN 50:25\ref*\f*
\p \v 20 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Succoth|מִסֻּכֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb and camped|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Etham|בְאֵתָ֔ם\rb* \rb on the edge|בִּקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the wilderness.|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb went|הֹלֵךְ֩\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb in a pillar|בְּעַמּ֤וּד\rb* \rb of cloud|עָנָן֙\rb* \rb to guide|לַנְחֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb their way|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb by day,|יוֹמָ֜ם\rb* \rb and in a pillar|בְּעַמּ֥וּד\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to give them light|לְהָאִ֣יר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb by night,|וְלַ֛יְלָה\rb* \rb so that they could travel|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb* \rb or night.|וָלָֽיְלָה׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the pillar|עַמּ֤וּד\rb* \rb of cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֔ם\rb* \rb nor the pillar|וְעַמּ֥וּד\rb* \rb of fire|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb by night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb left|יָמִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb its place before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 14
\s1 Pharaoh Pursues the Israelites
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּר֮\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb turn back|וְיָשֻׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb and encamp|וְיַחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb*\rb |פִּ֣י\rb* \rb Pi-hahiroth,|הַחִירֹ֔ת\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Migdol|מִגְדֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the sea.|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb You are to encamp|תַחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּֽם׃\rb* \rb directly opposite|לִפְנֵי֙\rb*\rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb Baal-zephon.|צְפֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |נִכְח֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb For Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb will say|וְאָמַ֤ר\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb ‘They|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb are wandering the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb in confusion;|נְבֻכִ֥ים\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb* \rb has boxed them|סָגַ֥ר\rb* \rb in.’|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 4 \rb And I will harden|וְחִזַּקְתִּ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 14:4 \ft Or \fqa stiffen \ft or \fqa strengthen\ft ; similarly in verses 8 and 17\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֮\rb* \rb heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb so that he will pursue|וְרָדַ֣ף\rb* \rb them.|אַחֲרֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb But I will gain honor|וְאִכָּבְדָ֤ה\rb* \rb by means of Pharaoh|בְּפַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his army,|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֥וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD.”|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb So this is what|כֵֽן׃\rb* \rb the Israelites did.|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb When the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּד֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb had fled,|בָרַ֖ח\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֤ה\rb* \rb and his officials|וַעֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb changed|וַ֠יֵּהָפֵךְ\rb* \rb their minds|לְבַ֨ב\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb them|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּֽאמרוּ֙\rb* \rb “What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb have we done?|עָשִׂ֔ינוּ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb We have released|שִׁלַּ֥חְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from serving us.”|מֵעָבְדֵֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Pharaoh prepared|וַיֶּאְסֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his chariot|רִכְבּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and took|לָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb his army|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb with him.|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb He took|וַיִּקַּ֗ח\rb* \rb 600|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the best|בָּח֔וּר\rb* \rb chariots,|רֶ֙כֶב֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the other chariots|רֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb with officers|וְשָׁלִשִׁ֖ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all of them.|כֻּלּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And the LORD|יְהֹוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|וַיְחַזֵּ֣ק\rb* \rb the heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that he pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֕ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who were marching out|יֹצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb defiantly.|בְּיָ֥ד\rb*\f + \fr 14:8 \ft Or \fqa marching out boldly\ft ; literally \fqa marching out with an upraised hand\f* \rb |רָמָֽה׃\rb*\v 9 \rb The Egyptians—|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb horses|סוּס֙\rb* \rb and chariots,|רֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb horsemen|וּפָרָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb and troops—|וְחֵיל֑וֹ\rb* \rb pursued the Israelites|וַיִּרְדְּפ֨וּ\rb* \rb and|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb overtook|וַיַּשִּׂ֤יגוּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb as they camped|חֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּי֙\rb* \rb Pi-hahiroth,|הַֽחִירֹ֔ת\rb* \rb opposite|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb Baal-zephon.|צְפֹֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb As Pharaoh|וּפַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb approached,|הִקְרִ֑יב\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked up|וַיִּשְׂאוּ֩\rb*\rb |עֵינֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֣יִם׀\rb* \rb marching|נֹסֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb after them,|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and they|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were terrified|וַיִּֽירְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and cried out|וַיִּצְעֲק֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb They said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb “Was it because|אֵין־\rb* \rb there were no|הַֽמִבְּלִ֤י\rb* \rb graves|קְבָרִים֙\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb that you brought us|לְקַחְתָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb into the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb to die?|לָמ֣וּת\rb* \rb What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֹּאת֙\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb by bringing us out|לְהוֹצִיאָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb of Egypt?|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Did we not|הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb say|דִּבַּ֨רְנוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְמִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Leave us alone|חֲדַ֥ל\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb so that we may serve|וְנַֽעַבְדָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians’?|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it would have been better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb for us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb to serve|עֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb than to die|מִמֻּתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness.”|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid.|תִּירָאוּ֒\rb* \rb Stand firm|הִֽתְיַצְב֗וּ\rb* \rb and you will see|וּרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb salvation,|יְשׁוּעַ֣ת\rb* \rb which He will accomplish|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today;|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb the Egyptians|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you see today,|רְאִיתֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb you will never|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb again.|תֹסִ֛יפוּ\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \v 14 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will fight|יִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb for you;|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb need only to be still.”|תַּחֲרִישֽׁוּן׃פ\rb*
\s1 Parting the Red Sea
\p \v 15 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Why|מַה־\rb* \rb are you crying out|תִּצְעַ֖ק\rb* \rb to Me?|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb Tell|דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to go forward.|וְיִסָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb And as for you,|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb lift up|הָרֵ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your staff|מַטְּךָ֗\rb* \rb and stretch out|וּנְטֵ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֛\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and divide it,|וּבְקָעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb so that the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb can go|וְיָבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb on dry ground.|בַּיַּבָּשָֽׁה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb And I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb will harden|מְחַזֵּק֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hearts|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that they will go in|וְיָבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb after them.|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Then I will gain honor|וְאִכָּבְדָ֤ה\rb* \rb by means of Pharaoh|בְּפַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and chariots|בְּרִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and horsemen.|וּבְפָרָשָֽׁיו׃\rb* \v 18 \rb The Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֥וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb when I am honored|בְּהִכָּבְדִ֣י\rb* \rb through Pharaoh,|בְּפַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb his chariots,|בְּרִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and his horsemen.”|וּבְפָרָשָֽׁיו׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 14:19 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb who had gone|הַהֹלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיִּסַּ֞ע\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb behind them.|מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb The pillar|עַמּ֤וּד\rb* \rb of cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb* \rb also moved|וַיִּסַּ֞ע\rb* \rb from before them|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb behind them,|מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb so that it came|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין׀\rb* \rb the camps|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵין֙\rb*\rb |מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb The cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb there in the darkness,|וְהַחֹ֔שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb but it lit up|וַיָּ֖אֶר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the night.|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*\f + \fr 14:20 \ft LXX \fqa and the night passed\f* \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb night long|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb neither camp|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb went near|קָרַ֥ב\rb* \rb the other.|זֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |זֶ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּ֨ט\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֮\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּם֒\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that night|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb drove back|וַיּ֣וֹלֶךְ\rb* \rb the sea|הַ֠יָּם\rb* \rb with a strong|עַזָּה֙\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֤ים\rb* \rb wind|בְּר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb that turned|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb into dry land.|לֶחָרָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb So the waters|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb were divided,|וַיִּבָּקְע֖וּ\rb* \v 22 \rb and the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb on dry ground,|בַּיַּבָּשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb with walls|חֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb of water|וְהַמַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb on their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb right|מִֽימִינָ֖ם\rb* \rb and on their left.|וּמִשְּׂמֹאלָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb And the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb chased after them—|וַיִּרְדְּפ֤וּ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb horses,|ס֣וּס\rb* \rb chariots,|רִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and horsemen—|וּפָרָשָׁ֑יו\rb* \rb and followed|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea.|הַיָּֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb At morning|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb watch,|בְּאַשְׁמֹ֣רֶת\rb* \rb however,|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb looked down|וַיַּשְׁקֵ֤ף\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the army|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from the pillar|בְּעַמּ֥וּד\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb and cloud,|וְעָנָ֑ן\rb* \rb and He threw their camp into confusion.|וַיָּ֕הָם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 25 \rb He caused their chariot|מַרְכְּבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb wheels|אֹפַ֣ן\rb* \rb to wobble,|וַיָּ֗סַר\rb*\f + \fr 14:25 \ft Or \fqa to swerve \ft or \fqa to come off \ft or \fqa to bind\ft ; see also SP, LXX, and Syriac.\f*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb so that they had difficulty|בִּכְבֵדֻ֑ת\rb* \rb driving.|וַֽיְנַהֲגֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb “Let us flee|אָנ֙וּסָה֙\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Israelites,”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the Egyptians,|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb “for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is fighting|נִלְחָ֥ם\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against Egypt!”|בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Stretch out|נְטֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb so that the waters|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb may flow back|וְיָשֻׁ֤בוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and|עַל־\rb* \rb their chariots|רִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and horsemen.”|פָּרָשָֽׁיו׃\rb* \v 27 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיֵּט֩\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּ֗ם\rb* \rb and at daybreak|לִפְנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֜ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֨שָׁב\rb* \rb to its normal state.|לְאֵ֣יתָנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb As the Egyptians|וּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb were retreating,|נָסִ֣ים\rb*\rb |לִקְרָאת֑וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb swept them|וַיְנַעֵ֧ר\rb* \rb into|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea.|הַיָּֽם׃\rb* \v 28 \rb The waters|הַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb flowed back|וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb and covered|וַיְכַסּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the chariots|הָרֶ֙כֶב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and horsemen—|הַפָּ֣רָשִׁ֔ים\rb*  \rb the entire|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb army|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb that had chased|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb the Israelites|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the sea.|בַּיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb Not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb of them|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb survived.|נִשְׁאַ֥ר\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb But the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb had walked|הָלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb through|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb on dry ground,|בַיַּבָּשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb with walls|חֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb of water|וְהַמַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb on their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb right|מִֽימִינָ֖ם\rb* \rb and on their left.|וּמִשְּׂמֹאלָֽם\rb* \v 30 \rb That|הַה֛וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb saved|וַיּ֨וֹשַׁע\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Egyptians,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb dead|מֵ֖ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the shore.|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּֽם׃\rb* \v 31 \rb When Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb power|הַיָּ֣ד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had exercised|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb over the Egyptians,|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּֽירְא֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and believed|וַיַּֽאֲמִ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb in Him|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in His servant|עַבְדּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb Moses.|וּבְמֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*
\c 15
\s1 The Song at the Sea
\r \ref Judges 5:1–31|JDG 5:1-31\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֩\rb* \rb and the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sang|יָשִֽׁיר־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֤ה\rb* \rb to the LORD:|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “I will sing|אָשִׁ֤ירָה\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He is highly exalted.|גָאֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |גָּאָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb The horse|ס֥וּס\rb* \rb and rider|וְרֹכְב֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He has thrown|רָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb into the sea.|בַיָּֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb The LORD|יָ֔הּ\rb* \rb is my strength|עָזִּ֤י\rb* \rb and my song,|וְזִמְרָת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and He has become|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb salvation.|לִֽישׁוּעָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb He is|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb my God,|אֵלִי֙\rb* \rb and I will praise Him,|וְאַנְוֵ֔הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb my father’s|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb God,|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb and I will exalt Him.|וַאֲרֹמְמֶֽנְהוּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is a warrior,|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is His name.|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb* \rb chariots|מַרְכְּבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and army|וְחֵיל֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He has cast|יָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb into the sea;|בַיָּ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb the finest|וּמִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb of his officers|שָֽׁלִשָׁ֖יו\rb*
\q2 \rb are drowned|טֻבְּע֥וּ\rb* \rb in the Red|סֽוּף׃\rb* \rb Sea.|בְיַם־\rb*\f + \fr 15:4 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\ft ; also in verse 22\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb The depths|תְּהֹמֹ֖ת\rb* \rb have covered them;|יְכַסְיֻ֑מוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb they sank|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb there|בִמְצוֹלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb like|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb a stone.|אָֽבֶן׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Your right hand,|יְמִֽינְךָ֣\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb is majestic|נֶאְדָּרִ֖י\rb* \rb in power;|בַּכֹּ֑חַ\rb*
\q1 \rb Your right hand,|יְמִֽינְךָ֥\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb has shattered|תִּרְעַ֥ץ\rb* \rb the enemy.|אוֹיֵֽב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb You overthrew|תַּהֲרֹ֣ס\rb* \rb Your adversaries|קָמֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb by Your great|וּבְרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb majesty.|גְּאוֹנְךָ֖\rb*
\q1 \rb You unleashed|תְּשַׁלַּח֙\rb* \rb Your burning wrath;|חֲרֹ֣נְךָ֔\rb*
\q2 \rb it consumed them|יֹאכְלֵ֖מוֹ\rb* \rb like stubble.|כַּקַּֽשׁ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb At the blast|וּבְר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb of Your nostrils|אַפֶּ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb the waters|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb piled up;|נֶ֣עֶרְמוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb like|כְמוֹ־\rb* \rb a wall|נֵ֖ד\rb* \rb the currents|נֹזְלִ֑ים\rb* \rb stood firm;|נִצְּב֥וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb the depths|תְהֹמֹ֖ת\rb* \rb congealed|קָֽפְא֥וּ\rb* \rb in the heart|בְּלֶב־\rb* \rb of the sea.|יָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb The enemy|אוֹיֵ֛ב\rb* \rb declared,|אָמַ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘I will pursue,|אֶרְדֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb I will overtake.|אַשִּׂ֖יג\rb*
\q1 \rb I will divide|אֲחַלֵּ֣ק\rb* \rb the spoils;|שָׁלָ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb I will gorge myself on them.|תִּמְלָאֵ֣מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb I will draw|אָרִ֣יק\rb* \rb my sword;|חַרְבִּ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb my hand|יָדִֽי׃\rb* \rb will destroy them.’|תּוֹרִישֵׁ֖מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb But You blew|נָשַׁ֥פְתָּ\rb* \rb with Your breath,|בְרוּחֲךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb and the sea|יָ֑ם\rb* \rb covered them.|כִּסָּ֣מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb They sank|צָֽלֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb like lead|כַּֽעוֹפֶ֔רֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb in the mighty|אַדִּירִֽים׃\rb* \rb waters.|בְּמַ֖יִם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb among the gods|בָּֽאֵלִם֙\rb* \rb is like You,|כָמֹ֤כָה\rb* \rb O LORD?|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb is like You—|כָּמֹ֖כָה\rb*  \rb majestic|נֶאְדָּ֣ר\rb* \rb in holiness,|בַּקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*
\q1 \rb revered|נוֹרָ֥א\rb* \rb with praises,|תְהִלֹּ֖ת\rb*
\q2 \rb performing|עֹ֥שֵׂה\rb* \rb wonders?|פֶֽלֶא׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb You stretched out|נָטִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb Your right hand,|יְמִ֣ינְךָ֔\rb*
\q2 \rb and the earth|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb swallowed them up.|תִּבְלָעֵ֖מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb With loving devotion|בְחַסְדְּךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 15:13 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb You will lead|נָחִ֥יתָ\rb*
\q2 \rb the people|עַם־\rb*\rb |ז֣וּ\rb* \rb You have redeemed;|גָּאָ֑לְתָּ\rb*
\q1 \rb with Your strength|בְעָזְּךָ֖\rb* \rb You will guide them|נֵהַ֥לְתָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your holy|קָדְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb dwelling.|נְוֵ֥ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The nations|עַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb will hear|שָֽׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb and tremble;|יִרְגָּז֑וּן\rb*
\q2 \rb anguish|חִ֣יל\rb* \rb will grip|אָחַ֔ז\rb* \rb the dwellers|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Philistia.|פְּלָֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Then|אָ֤ז\rb* \rb the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb will be dismayed;|נִבְהֲלוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb trembling|רָ֑עַד\rb* \rb will seize|יֹֽאחֲזֵ֖מוֹ\rb* \rb the leaders|אֵילֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moab;|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*
\q1 \rb those who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Canaan|כְנָֽעַן׃\rb* \rb will melt away,|נָמֹ֕גוּ\rb*\rb |כֹּ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \v 16 \rb and terror|אֵימָ֙תָה֙\rb* \rb and dread|וָפַ֔חַד\rb* \rb will fall|תִּפֹּ֨ל\rb* \rb on them.|עֲלֵיהֶ֤ם\rb*
\q1 \rb By the power|בִּגְדֹ֥ל\rb* \rb of Your arm|זְרוֹעֲךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb they will be as still|יִדְּמ֣וּ\rb* \rb as a stone|כָּאָ֑בֶן\rb*
\q1 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb pass by,|יַעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb until|עַֽד־\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb*\rb |ז֥וּ\rb* \rb You have bought|קָנִֽיתָ׃\rb* \rb pass by.|יַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb You will bring them in|תְּבִאֵ֗מוֹ\rb* \rb and plant them|וְתִטָּעֵ֙מוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb on the mountain|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Your inheritance—|נַחֲלָֽתְךָ֔\rb*
\q1 \rb the place,|מָכ֧וֹן\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb You have prepared|פָּעַ֖לְתָּ\rb* \rb for Your dwelling,|לְשִׁבְתְּךָ֛\rb*
\q2 \rb the sanctuary,|מִקְּדָ֕שׁ\rb* \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb Your hands|יָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb have established.|כּוֹנְנ֥וּ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb forever|לְעֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever!”|וָעֶֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb For when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֜ה\rb* \rb horses,|ס֨וּס\rb* \rb chariots,|בְּרִכְבּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּבְפָרָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb went|בָא֩\rb* \rb into the sea,|בַּיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought the waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb back|וַיָּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb over them.|עֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb But the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb walked|הָלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb through|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּֽם׃פ\rb* \rb on dry ground.|בַיַּבָּשָׁ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Then Miriam|מִרְיָ֨ם\rb* \rb the prophetess,|הַנְּבִיאָ֜ה\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sister,|אֲח֧וֹת\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb a tambourine|הַתֹּ֖ף\rb* \rb in her hand,|בְּיָדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb followed her|וַתֵּצֶ֤אןָ\rb* \rb with tambourines|בְּתֻפִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and dancing.|וּבִמְחֹלֹֽת׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And Miriam|מִרְיָ֑ם\rb* \rb sang back|וַתַּ֥עַן\rb* \rb to them:|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \rb “Sing|שִׁ֤ירוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He is highly exalted;|גָאֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |גָּאָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb the horse|ס֥וּס\rb* \rb and rider|וְרֹכְב֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He has thrown|רָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb into the sea.”|בַיָּֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Waters of Marah
\p \v 22 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb led|וַיַּסַּ֨ע\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb from the Red|ס֔וּף\rb* \rb Sea,|מִיַּם־\rb* \rb and they went out|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Desert|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Shur.|שׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb For three|שְׁלֹֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb they walked|וַיֵּלְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb in the desert|בַּמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb without|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb finding|מָ֥צְאוּ\rb* \rb water.|מָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 23 \rb And when they came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to Marah,|מָרָ֔תָה\rb*\f + \fr 15:23 \fqa Marah \ft means \fqa bitter\ft .\f* \rb they could|יָֽכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb drink|לִשְׁתֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb the water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb there|מִמָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb was bitter.|מָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb (That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb it was named|קָרָֽא־\rb*\rb |שְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Marah.)|מָרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb grumbled|וַיִּלֹּ֧נוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵּאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb are we to drink?”|נִּשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 25 \rb And Moses cried out|וַיִּצְעַ֣ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb showed him|וַיּוֹרֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb a log.|עֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb And when he cast it|וַיַּשְׁלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the waters,|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb they|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb were sweetened.|וַֽיִּמְתְּק֖וּ\rb*
\p \rb There|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the LORD made|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb for them|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb a statute|חֹ֥ק\rb* \rb and an ordinance,|וּמִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb He tested them,|נִסָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb saying,|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb you will listen carefully|שָׁמ֨וֹעַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמַ֜ע\rb* \rb to the voice|לְק֣וֹל׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb what is right|וְהַיָּשָׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in His eyes,|בְּעֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb and pay attention|וְהַֽאֲזַנְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to His commands,|לְמִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His statutes,|חֻקָּ֑יו\rb* \rb then I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bring|שַׂ֤מְתִּי\rb* \rb on you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb any|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb of the diseases|הַמַּֽחֲלָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I inflicted|אָשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb on the Egyptians.|בְמִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who heals you.”|רֹפְאֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Then they came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to Elim,|אֵילִ֔מָה\rb* \rb where|וְשָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb there were twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֛ה\rb* \rb springs|עֵינֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and seventy|וְשִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb palm trees,|תְּמָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb and they camped|וַיַּחֲנוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the waters.|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb*
\c 16
\s1 Manna and Quail from Heaven
\p \v 1 \rb On the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb after they had left|לְצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from Elim|מֵֽאֵילִ֔ם\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Desert|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Sin,|סִ֔ין\rb*\f + \fr 16:1 \ft The geographical name \fqa Sin \ft is related to \fqa Sinai \ft and should not be mistaken for the English word \fqa sin\ft .\f* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb Elim|אֵילִ֖ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Sinai.|סִינָ֑י\rb* \v 2 \rb And there in the desert|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֧ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb grumbled|וַיִּלִּינוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron.|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \v 3 \rb “If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb we had died|מוּתֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb by the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb hand|בְיַד־\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt!”|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb they said.|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “There we sat|בְּשִׁבְתֵּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb pots|סִ֣יר\rb* \rb of meat|הַבָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and ate|בְּאָכְלֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb our fill|לָשֹׂ֑בַע\rb* \rb of bread,|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have brought|הוֹצֵאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb desert|הַמִּדְבָּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to starve|בָּרָעָֽב׃ס\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֥ל\rb* \rb to death!”|לְהָמִ֛ית\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will rain down|מַמְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb for you.|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb Each day|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb are to go out|וְיָצָ֨א\rb* \rb and gather|וְלָֽקְטוּ֙\rb* \rb enough for that day.|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb In this way|לְמַ֧עַן\rb* \rb I will test|אֲנַסֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb or not|לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb they will follow|הֲיֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb My instructions.|בְּתוֹרָתִ֖י\rb* \v 5 \rb Then|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb on the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔י\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb when they prepare|וְהֵכִ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they bring in,|יָבִ֑יאוּ\rb* \rb it will be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb twice|מִשְׁנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb as|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb much|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb as they gather|יִלְקְט֖וּ\rb* \rb on the other days.”|י֥וֹם׀\rb*\rb |יֽוֹם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb “This evening|עֶ֕רֶב\rb* \rb you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb it was the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb who brought|הוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb and in the morning|וּבֹ֗קֶר\rb* \rb you will see|וּרְאִיתֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb glory,|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb because He has heard|בְּשָׁמְע֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your grumbling|תְּלֻנֹּתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Him.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb For who|מָ֔ה\rb* \rb are we,|וְנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you should grumble|תַלּוֹנוּ\rb* \rb against us?”|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb added,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb will give|בְּתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb meat|בָּשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb this evening|בָּעֶ֜רֶב\rb* \rb and bread|וְלֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb to fill you|לִשְׂבֹּ֔עַ\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַּבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb for He|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has heard|בִּשְׁמֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb your grumbling|תְּלֻנֹּ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb against Him.|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb Who|מָ֔ה\rb* \rb are we?|וְנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb Your grumblings|מַלִּינִ֖ם\rb* \rb are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֥ינוּ\rb*\rb |תְלֻנֹּתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said to|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb ‘Come|קִרְב֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He has heard|שָׁמַ֔ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb your grumbling.’”|תְּלֻנֹּתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb And as|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb was speaking|כְּדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb they looked|וַיִּפְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the desert,|הַמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and there|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb in a cloud|בֶּעָנָֽן׃פ\rb* \rb the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb appeared.|נִרְאָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb “I have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grumbling|תְּלוּנֹּת֮\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites.|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb Tell them,|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘At|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָֽעַרְבַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\f + \fr 16:12 \ft Hebrew \fqa Between the two evenings\f* \rb you will eat|תֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb meat,|בָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and in the morning|וּבַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb you will be filled|תִּשְׂבְּעוּ־\rb* \rb with bread.|לָ֑חֶם\rb* \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.’”|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb That evening|בָעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb quail|הַשְּׂלָ֔ו\rb* \rb came|וַתַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb and covered|וַתְּכַ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb and in the morning|וּבַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb there was|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a layer|שִׁכְבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of dew|הַטַּ֔ל\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the camp.|לַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb When the layer|שִׁכְבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of dew|הַטָּ֑ל\rb* \rb had evaporated,|וַתַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb were thin|דַּ֣ק\rb* \rb flakes|מְחֻסְפָּ֔ס\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the desert|הַמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb floor,|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb as fine|דַּ֥ק\rb* \rb as frost|כַּכְּפֹ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb When the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb saw it,|וַיִּרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb they asked|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb one|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb another,|אָחִיו֙\rb* \rb “What|מָ֣ן\rb* \rb is it?”|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb it was.|ה֑וּא\rb*
\p \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “It|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is the bread|הַלֶּ֔חֶם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to eat.|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb This|זֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has commanded:|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb ‘Each one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb is to gather|לִקְט֣וּ\rb* \rb as much|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb as|לְפִ֣י\rb* \rb he needs.|אָכְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb You may take|תִּקָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb an omer|עֹ֣מֶר\rb*\f + \fr 16:16 \fqa An omer\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* dry quarts or 2.2 liters; also in verses 18, 32, 33, and 36.\f* \rb for each|לַגֻּלְגֹּ֗לֶת\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּר֙\rb* \rb person|נַפְשֹׁ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |לַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in your tent.’”|בְּאָהֳל֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb So the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb this.|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb Some gathered|וַֽיִּלְקְט֔וּ\rb* \rb more,|הַמַּרְבֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and some less.|וְהַמַּמְעִֽיט׃\rb* \v 18 \rb When they measured it|וַיָּמֹ֣דּוּ\rb* \rb by the omer,|בָעֹ֔מֶר\rb* \rb he who gathered much|הַמַּרְבֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb had no|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb excess,|הֶעְדִּיף֙\rb* \rb and he who gathered little|וְהַמַּמְעִ֖יט\rb* \rb had no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb shortfall.|הֶחְסִ֑יר\rb*\f + \fr 16:18 \ft Cited \ref in 2|2\ref* Corinthians 8:15\f* \rb Each one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb gathered|לָקָֽטוּ׃\rb* \rb as|לְפִֽי־\rb* \rb much as he needed to eat.|אָכְל֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “No|אַל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb may keep|יוֹתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb any of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.”|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \v 20 \rb But they did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses;|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb some people|אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb left|וַיּוֹתִ֨רוּ\rb* \rb part of|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb it until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning,|בֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and it became infested|וַיָּ֥רֻם\rb* \rb with maggots|תּוֹלָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb and began to smell.|וַיִּבְאַ֑שׁ\rb* \rb So Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb was angry|וַיִּקְצֹ֥ף\rb* \rb with them.|עֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Every morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb each one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּלְקְט֤וּ\rb* \rb as much|כְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb as was needed,|אָכְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and when the sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb grew hot,|וְחַ֥ם\rb* \rb it melted away.|וְנָמָֽס׃\rb*
\s1 The Sabbath Observed
\r \ref Genesis 2:1–3|GEN 2:1-3\ref*; \ref Hebrews 4:1–11|HEB 4:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 22 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb On the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֗י\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they gathered|לָֽקְט֥וּ\rb* \rb twice|מִשְׁנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb as much food—|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb omers|הָעֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb per person|לָאֶחָ֑ד\rb*\f + \fr 16:22 \fqa 2 omers\ft is \ref approximately 4|4\ref* dry quarts or 4.4 liters per person.\f* — \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָֽעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and reported|וַיַּגִּ֖ידוּ\rb* \rb this to Moses.|לְמֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb He told them,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “This|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has said:|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Tomorrow|מָחָ֑ר\rb* \rb is to be a day of complete rest,|שַׁבָּת֧וֹן\rb* \rb a holy|קֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Sabbath|שַׁבַּת־\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb So|אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb bake|תֹּאפ֞וּ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you want to bake,|אֵפ֗וּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb boil|תְּבַשְּׁלוּ֙\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb you want to boil.|בַּשֵּׁ֔לוּ\rb* \rb Then set aside|הַנִּ֧יחוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb whatever|כָּל־\rb* \rb remains|הָ֣עֹדֵ֔ף\rb* \rb and keep it|לְמִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.’”|הַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So they set it aside|וַיַּנִּ֤יחוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded,|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and it did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb smell|הִבְאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb or|לֹא־\rb* \rb contain|הָ֥יְתָה\rb*\rb |בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb any maggots.|וְרִמָּ֖ה\rb* \v 25 \rb “Eat it today,”|אִכְלֻ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֥ת\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Today|הַיּ֕וֹם\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb find anything|תִמְצָאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the field.|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \v 26 \rb For six|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb you may gather,|תִּלְקְטֻ֑הוּ\rb* \rb but on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֛י\rb* \rb day,|וּבַיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb the Sabbath,|שַׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb it will not be there.”|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |בּֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Yet|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb went out|יָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb to gather,|לִלְקֹ֑ט\rb* \rb but they did not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb find anything.|מָצָֽאוּ׃ס\rb* \v 28 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb “How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |אָ֙נָה֙\rb* \rb will you refuse|מֵֽאַנְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb to keep|לִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֖י\rb* \rb and instructions?|וְתוֹרֹתָֽי׃\rb* \v 29 \rb Understand|רְא֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb the Sabbath;|הַשַּׁבָּת֒\rb* \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֠ן\rb* \rb on the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will give|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb for two days.|יוֹמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb everyone|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb must stay|שְׁב֣וּ׀\rb* \rb where he is;|תַּחְתָּ֗יו\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb may leave|יֵ֥צֵא\rb* \rb his place.”|מִמְּקֹמ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb So the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁבְּת֥וּ\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִֽי׃\rb* \rb day.|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\s1 The Jar of Manna
\p \v 31 \rb Now the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called the bread|וַיִּקְרְא֧וּ\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb manna.|מָ֑ן\rb*\f + \fr 16:31 \fqa Manna \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa What is it? \ft (see verse 15).\f* \rb It|וְה֗וּא\rb* \rb was white|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb like coriander|גַּד֙\rb* \rb seed|כְּזֶ֤רַע\rb* \rb and tasted|וְטַעְמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb like wafers|כְּצַפִּיחִ֥ת\rb* \rb made with honey.|בִּדְבָֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 32 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “This|זֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |מְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb has commanded:|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb ‘Keep|לְמִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb an omer|הָעֹ֙מֶר֙\rb* \rb of manna|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb for the generations to come,|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן׀\rb* \rb they may see|יִרְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bread|הַלֶּ֗חֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I fed|הֶאֱכַ֤לְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb when I brought you|בְּהוֹצִיאִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֚ח\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb jar|צִנְצֶ֣נֶת\rb* \rb and fill it|וְתֶן־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |מְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb with an omer|הָעֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb of manna.|מָ֑ן\rb* \rb Then place|וְהַנַּ֤ח\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to be preserved|לְמִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.”|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 34 \rb And Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb placed it|וַיַּנִּיחֵ֧הוּ\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֖ת\rb*\f + \fr 16:34 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \rb to be preserved|לְמִשְׁמָֽרֶת׃\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb The Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb ate|אָֽכְל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb manna|הַמָּן֙\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they came|בֹּאָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb where they could settle;|נוֹשָׁ֑בֶת\rb* \rb they ate|אָֽכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb manna|הַמָּן֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they reached|בֹּאָ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|קְצֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan.|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb* \v 36 \rb (Now an omer|וְהָעֹ֕מֶר\rb* \rb is a tenth|עֲשִׂרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of an ephah.)|הָאֵיפָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 16:36 \fqa An ephah\ft was a dry measure having the capacity of \ref about 20|20\ref* dry quarts or 22 liters.\f*\rb |הֽוּא׃פ\rb*
\c 17
\s1 Water from the Rock
\r \ref Numbers 20:1–13|NUM 20:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֨ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb left|וַ֠יִּסְעוּ\rb* \rb the Desert|מִמִּדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Sin,|סִ֛ין\rb*\f + \fr 17:1 \ft The geographical name \fqa Sin \ft is related to \fqa Sinai \ft and should not be mistaken for the English word \fqa sin\ft .\f* \rb moving from place to place|לְמַסְעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb commanded.|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb They camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb at Rephidim,|בִּרְפִידִ֔ים\rb* \rb but there was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb for the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb to drink.|לִשְׁתֹּ֥ת\rb* \v 2 \rb So the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb contended|וַיָּ֤רֶב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to drink.”|וְנִשְׁתֶּ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb “Why|מַה־\rb* \rb do you contend|תְּרִיבוּן֙\rb* \rb with me?”|עִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Why|מַה־\rb* \rb do you test|תְּנַסּ֖וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD?”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb But the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb thirsted|וַיִּצְמָ֨א\rb* \rb for water|לַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb and they grumbled|וַיָּ֥לֶן\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses:|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּה֙\rb* \rb have you brought us|הֶעֱלִיתָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt—|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*  \rb to make|לְהָמִ֥ית\rb* \rb us|אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb our children|בָּנַ֥י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and livestock|מִקְנַ֖י\rb* \rb die of thirst?”|בַּצָּמָֽא׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּצְעַ֤ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb should I do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people?|לָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb A little more|ע֥וֹד\rb*\rb |מְעַ֖ט\rb* \rb and they will stone me!”|וּסְקָלֻֽנִי׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Walk on|עֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and take|וְקַ֥ח\rb* \rb some of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb with you.|אִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Take along|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb the staff|וּמַטְּךָ֗\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you struck|הִכִּ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Nile,|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and go.|וְהָלָֽכְתָּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I will stand|עֹמֵד֩\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֥ם׀\rb* \rb before|לְפָנֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb you|עַֽל־\rb* \rb by the rock|הַצּוּר֮\rb* \rb at Horeb.|בְּחֹרֵב֒\rb*\f + \fr 17:6 \fqa Horeb \ft is another name for Sinai.\f* \rb And when you strike|וְהִכִּ֣יתָ\rb* \rb the rock,|בַצּ֗וּר\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will come out|וְיָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb for the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb to drink.”|וְשָׁתָ֣ה\rb*
\p \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb this|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb He named|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb Massah|מַסָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 17:7 \fqa Massah \ft means \fqa testing\ft .\f* \rb and Meribah|וּמְרִיבָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 17:7 \fqa Meribah \ft means \fqa quarreling\ft .\f* \rb because|עַל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb quarreled,|רִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb and because|וְעַ֨ל\rb* \rb they tested|נַסֹּתָ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Is|הֲיֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb among us|בְּקִרְבֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb not?”|אָֽיִן׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Defeat of the Amalekites
\p \v 8 \rb After this, the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיִּלָּ֥חֶם\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb at Rephidim.|בִּרְפִידִֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joshua,|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb “Choose|בְּחַר־\rb*\rb |לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb some of our men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and go out|וְצֵ֖א\rb* \rb to fight|הִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb the Amalekites.|בַּעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb Tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb will stand|נִצָּב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the hilltop|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |הַגִּבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb with the staff|וּמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb in my hand.”|בְּיָדִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had instructed|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and fought|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against the Amalekites,|בַּעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb while Moses,|וּמֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and Hur|וְח֔וּר\rb* \rb went up|עָל֖וּ\rb* \rb to the top|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of the hill.|הַגִּבְעָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb As long as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb held up|יָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb his hands,|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb prevailed;|וְגָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb but when|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he lowered|יָנִ֛יחַ\rb* \rb them,|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amalek|עֲמָלֵֽק׃\rb* \rb prevailed.|וְגָבַ֥ר\rb* \v 12 \rb When Moses’|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb hands|וִידֵ֤י\rb* \rb grew heavy,|כְּבֵדִ֔ים\rb* \rb they took|וַיִּקְחוּ־\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֛בֶן\rb* \rb and put|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb it under him,|תַחְתָּ֖יו\rb* \rb and he sat|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb on it.|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb Then Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb and Hur|וְח֜וּר\rb* \rb held|תָּֽמְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb his hands up,|בְיָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb one|מִזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb on each|אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb side,|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb so that his hands|יָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb remained|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb steady|אֱמוּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb went down.|בֹּ֥א\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb overwhelmed|וַיַּחֲלֹ֧שׁ\rb* \rb Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֥ק\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his army|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb with the sword.|חָֽרֶב׃פ\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Write this|כְּתֹ֨ב\rb*\rb |זֹ֤את\rb* \rb on a scroll|בַּסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb as a reminder|זִכָּרוֹן֙\rb* \rb and recite|וְשִׂ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb it to Joshua,|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will utterly blot out|מָחֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶמְחֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the memory|זֵ֣כֶר\rb* \rb of Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֔ק\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven.”|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb and named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb it|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb Is My Banner.|נִסִּֽי׃\rb*\f + \fr 17:15 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Nissi\f* \v 16 \rb “Indeed,”|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “a hand|יָד֙\rb* \rb was lifted up toward|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כֵּ֣ס\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יָ֔הּ\rb* \rb The LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will war|מִלְחָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb against Amalek|בַּֽעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb from generation|מִדֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb to generation.”|דֹּֽר׃פ\rb*
\c 18
\s1 The Visit of Jethro
\p \v 1 \rb Now Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Jethro,|יִתְר֨וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 18:1 \ft Moses’ father-in-law \fqa Jethro \ft was also called \fqa Reuel\ft ; see \ref Exodus 2:18|EXO 2:18\ref*.\f* \rb the priest|כֹהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and His people|עַמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Israel,|וּלְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and how|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had brought|הוֹצִ֧יא\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb After|אַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had sent back|שִׁלּוּחֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb his wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Zipporah,|צִפֹּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb his|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Jethro|יִתְרוֹ֙\rb* \rb had received her,|וַיִּקַּ֗ח\rb* \v 3 \rb along with|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb her two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons.|בָנֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb One|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb son|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb was named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Gershom,|גֵּֽרְשֹׁ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 18:3 \fqa Gershom \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa sojourner\ft .\f* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Moses had said,|אָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “I have been|הָיִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb in a foreign|נָכְרִיָּֽה׃\rb* \rb land.”|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \v 4 \rb The other son|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Eliezer,|אֱלִיעֶ֑זֶר\rb*\f + \fr 18:4 \fqa Eliezer \ft means \fqa God is my helper\ft .\f* \rb for Moses had said,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb “The God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb was my helper|בְּעֶזְרִ֔י\rb* \rb and delivered me|וַיַּצִּלֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb from the sword|מֵחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of Pharaoh.”|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Moses’ father-in-law|חֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb Jethro,|יִתְר֨וֹ\rb* \rb along with Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and sons,|וּבָנָ֥יו\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the desert,|הַמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb was encamped|חֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb at the mountain|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 6 \rb He sent word|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “I,|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb your father-in-law|חֹתֶנְךָ֥\rb* \rb Jethro,|יִתְר֖וֹ\rb* \rb am coming|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb you with your wife|וְאִ֨שְׁתְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and her|עִמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb sons.”|בָנֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb went out to meet|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb his father-in-law|חֹֽתְנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֙חוּ֙\rb* \rb and kissed|וַיִּשַּׁק־\rb* \rb him.|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb They greeted|וַיִּשְׁאֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb each|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb other|לְרֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb into the tent.|הָאֹֽהֱלָה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb recounted|וַיְסַפֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to his father-in-law|לְחֹ֣תְנ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and the Egyptians|וּלְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb for|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb sake,|אוֹדֹ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the hardships|הַתְּלָאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had encountered|מְצָאָ֣תַם\rb* \rb along the way,|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and how the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had delivered them.|וַיַּצִּלֵ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And Jethro|יִתְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּ֣חַדְּ\rb* \rb over|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the good things|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for Israel,|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had rescued|הִצִּיל֖וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Egyptians.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Jethro|יִתְרוֹ֒\rb* \rb declared,|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb “Blessed be|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has delivered|הִצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וּמִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb and of Pharaoh,|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb has delivered|הִצִּיל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the Egyptians.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is greater|גָד֥וֹל\rb* \rb than all other|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb gods,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He did this|בַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb when they|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb treated Israel with arrogance.”|זָד֖וּ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb Jethro|יִתְר֨וֹ\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and sacrifices|וּזְבָחִ֖ים\rb* \rb to God,|לֵֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb with all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכָל־\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֛חֶם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\s1 Jethro Advises Moses
\r \ref Deuteronomy 1:9–18|DEU 1:9-18\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb took his seat|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb to judge|לִשְׁפֹּ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and they stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֤ד\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 14 \rb When his|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was doing|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for the people,|לָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb he asked,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb doing|עֹשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb for the people?|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb Why|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb sit|יוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb alone as judge,|לְבַדֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb standing|נִצָּ֥ב\rb* \rb around|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּ֥קֶר\rb* \rb till|עַד־\rb* \rb evening?”|עָֽרֶב׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of God,”|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |לְחֹתְנ֑וֹ\rb* \v 16 \rb “Whenever|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb a dispute,|דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb it is brought|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb to judge|וְשָׁ֣פַטְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb one man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and another,|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and I make known|וְהוֹדַעְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to them|אֶת־\rb* \rb the statutes|חֻקֵּ֥י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb laws|תּוֹרֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of God.”|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb But Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb “What|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb doing|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb good.|טוֹב֙\rb* \v 18 \rb Surely|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb will wear yourselves out,|נָבֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |תִּבֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the task|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is too heavy|כָבֵ֤ד\rb* \rb for you.|מִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb You cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb handle|עֲשֹׂ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it alone.|לְבַדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Now|עַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb listen to me;|שְׁמַ֤ע\rb*\rb |בְּקֹלִי֙\rb* \rb I will give you some advice,|אִיעָ֣צְךָ֔\rb* \rb and may God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb with you.|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb must be|הֱיֵ֧ה\rb* \rb the people’s representative|לָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb before|מ֚וּל\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבֵאתָ֥\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their causes|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Him.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Teach|וְהִזְהַרְתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb the statutes|הַחֻקִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and laws,|הַתּוֹרֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and show|וְהוֹדַעְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to live|יֵ֣לְכוּ\rb*\rb |בָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the work|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they must do.|יַעֲשֽׂוּן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Furthermore,|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb select|תֶחֱזֶ֣ה\rb* \rb capable|חַ֜יִל\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb from among|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the people—|הָ֠עָם\rb*  \rb God-fearing,|יִרְאֵ֧י\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb trustworthy men|אֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb who are averse|שֹׂ֣נְאֵי\rb* \rb to dishonest gain.|בָ֑צַע\rb* \rb Appoint them|וְשַׂמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb over the people|עֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb as leaders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of thousands,|אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds,|מֵא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of fifties,|חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb and of tens.|עֲשָׂרֹֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Have these men judge|וְשָׁפְט֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb at all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb times.|עֵת֒\rb* \rb Then|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb they can bring|יָבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb major|הַגָּדֹל֙\rb* \rb issue,|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb but all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb minor|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb cases|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb they can judge|יִשְׁפְּטוּ־\rb* \rb on their own,|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb so that your load may be lightened|וְהָקֵל֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb as they share|וְנָשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb it with you.|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb If|אִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you follow|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb advice|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb so directs you,|וְצִוְּךָ֣\rb* \rb then you will be able|וְיָֽכָלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb to endure,|עֲמֹ֑ד\rb* \rb and|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb can go|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb home|מְקֹמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in peace.”|בְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to his father-in-law|חֹתְנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he said.|אָמָֽר׃\rb* \v 25 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb chose|וַיִּבְחַ֨ר\rb* \rb capable|חַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and made|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb heads|רָאשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb as leaders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of thousands,|אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds,|מֵא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of fifties,|חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb and of tens.|עֲשָׂרֹֽת׃\rb* \v 26 \rb And they judged|וְשָׁפְט֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb at all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb times;|עֵ֑ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they would bring|יְבִיא֣וּן\rb* \rb the difficult|הַקָּשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb cases|הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb but any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb minor|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb issue|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb they would judge|יִשְׁפּוּט֥וּ\rb* \rb themselves.|הֵֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb his father-in-law on his way,|חֹתְנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and Jethro returned|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own land.|אַרְצֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\c 19
\s1 Israel at Mount Sinai
\p \v 1 \rb In the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb on the same|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day of the month|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\f + \fr 19:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa In the third month, on the same day\ft ; that is, two months after leaving Egypt; see \ref Numbers 33:3|NUM 33:3\ref*.\f* \rb that the Israelites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had left|לְצֵ֥את\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb they came|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to the Wilderness|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Sinai.|סִינָֽי׃\rb* \v 2 \rb After they had set out|וַיִּסְע֣וּ\rb* \rb from Rephidim,|מֵרְפִידִ֗ים\rb* \rb they entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb the Wilderness|מִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sinai,|סִינַ֔י\rb*\rb |וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb camped|וַיִּֽחַן־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb in front of|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb the mountain.|הָהָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb went up|עָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֣ר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb*\rb |תֹאמַר֙\rb* \rb you are to tell|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb and explain|וְתַגֵּ֖יד\rb* \rb to the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 4 \rb ‘You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have seen for yourselves|רְאִיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I did|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb to Egypt,|לְמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and how I carried|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you on|עַל־\rb* \rb eagles’|נְשָׁרִ֔ים\rb* \rb wings|כַּנְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb and brought|וָאָבִ֥א\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to Myself.|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will indeed obey|שָׁמ֤וֹעַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb My voice|בְּקֹלִ֔י\rb* \rb and keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant,|בְּרִיתִ֑י\rb* \rb you will be|וִהְיִ֨יתֶם\rb* \rb My|לִ֤י\rb* \rb treasured possession|סְגֻלָּה֙\rb* \rb out of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations—|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb*  \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb is Mine.|לִ֖י\rb* \v 6 \rb And unto Me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֧ם\rb* \rb shall be|תִּהְיוּ־\rb* \rb a kingdom|מַמְלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb of priests|כֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and a holy|קָד֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb nation.’|וְג֣וֹי\rb* \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to speak|תְּדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites.”|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb and summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb the elders|לְזִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and set|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb them|אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had commanded him.|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb* \v 8 \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעֲנ֨וּ\rb* \rb together,|יַחְדָּו֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “We will do|נַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken.”|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*
\p \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּ֧שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb back to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb will come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb you in a dense|בְּעַ֣ב\rb* \rb cloud,|הֶֽעָנָן֒\rb* \rb so that|בַּעֲב֞וּר\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb when I speak|בְּדַבְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb with you,|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb they will always|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb put their trust|יַאֲמִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb in you.”|בְּךָ֖\rb*
\p \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb relayed|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb what the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and consecrate them|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֥ם\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb and tomorrow.|וּמָחָ֑ר\rb* \rb They must wash|וְכִבְּס֖וּ\rb* \rb their clothes|שִׂמְלֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb and be|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb prepared|נְכֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb by the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb day,|לַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will come down|יֵרֵ֧ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינָֽי׃\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb And you are to set up a boundary|וְהִגְבַּלְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb around the mountain|סָבִ֣יב\rb* \rb and tell them,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Be careful|הִשָּׁמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb not to go up|עֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָ֖ר\rb* \rb or touch|וּנְגֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb its base.|בְּקָצֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb the mountain|בָּהָ֖ר\rb* \rb shall surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb hand|יָ֗ד\rb* \rb shall touch|תִגַּ֨ע\rb* \rb him,|בּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he shall surely be stoned|סָק֤וֹל\rb*\rb |יִסָּקֵל֙\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb shot|יָרֹ֣ה\rb* \rb with arrows—|יִיָּרֶ֔ה\rb*  \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb beast,|בְּהֵמָ֥ה\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb live.’|יִחְיֶ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 19:13 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 12:20|HEB 12:20\ref*\f*
\p \rb Only when the ram’s horn|הַיֹּבֵ֔ל\rb* \rb sounds a long blast|בִּמְשֹׁךְ֙\rb* \rb may they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb approach|יַעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb the mountain.|בָהָֽר׃\rb*\f + \fr 19:13 \ft Or \fqa may they go up on the mountain\f*”
\p \v 14 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֧רֶד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb he consecrated them,|וַיְקַדֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and they washed|וַֽיְכַבְּס֖וּ\rb* \rb their clothes.|שִׂמְלֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb “Be|הֱי֥וּ\rb* \rb prepared|נְכֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the third|לִשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb day,”|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb draw near|תִּגְּשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a woman.”|אִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*
\s1 The LORD Visits Sinai
\p \v 16 \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֜י\rb* \rb day,|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb when morning|הַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb came,|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb there was|בִּֽהְיֹ֣ת\rb* \rb thunder|קֹלֹ֨ת\rb* \rb and lightning.|וּבְרָקִ֜ים\rb* \rb A thick|כָּבֵד֙\rb* \rb cloud|וְעָנָ֤ן\rb* \rb was upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and a very loud|חָזָ֣ק\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb blast|וְקֹ֥ל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn went out,|שֹׁפָ֖ר\rb* \rb so that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb trembled.|וַיֶּחֱרַ֥ד\rb* \v 17 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb with God,|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and they stood|וַיִּֽתְיַצְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb at the foot|בְּתַחְתִּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the mountain.|הָהָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Mount|וְהַ֤ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַי֙\rb* \rb was completely|כֻּלּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb enveloped in smoke,|עָשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb because|מִ֠פְּנֵי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had descended|יָרַ֥ד\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb in fire.|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb And the smoke|עֲשָׁנוֹ֙\rb* \rb rose|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb like the smoke|כְּעֶ֣שֶׁן\rb* \rb of a furnace,|הַכִּבְשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb mountain|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb quaked|וַיֶּחֱרַ֥ד\rb* \rb violently.|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \v 19 \rb And as|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn|הַשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb grew louder|הוֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְחָזֵ֣ק\rb* \rb and louder,|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb spoke|יְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb and God|וְהָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb answered him|יַעֲנֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb in the thunder.|בְקֽוֹל׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb descended|וַיֵּ֧רֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the top|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֖י\rb* \rb and|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Moses|לְמֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the summit.|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb So Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb went up,|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \v 21 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Go down|רֵ֖ד\rb* \rb and warn|הָעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb the people|בָּעָ֑ם\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to break through|יֶהֶרְס֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֔וֹת\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb lest many|רָֽב׃\rb* \rb of them|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb perish.|וְנָפַ֥ל\rb* \v 22 \rb Even|וְגַ֧ם\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb who approach|הַנִּגָּשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb must consecrate themselves,|יִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb will break out|יִפְרֹ֥ץ\rb* \rb against them.”|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb “The people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb come up|לַעֲלֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai,|סִינָ֑י\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb solemnly warned|הַעֵדֹ֤תָה\rb* \rb us,|בָּ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Put a boundary around|הַגְבֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb and set it apart as holy.’”|וְקִדַּשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb “Go|לֶךְ־\rb* \rb down|רֵ֔ד\rb* \rb and bring|וְעָלִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb with|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb you.|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb But the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and the people|וְהָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb must not|אַל־\rb* \rb break through|יֶֽהֶרְס֛וּ\rb* \rb to come up|לַעֲלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb He will break out|יִפְרָץ־\rb* \rb against them.”|בָּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\c 20
\s1 The Ten Commandments
\r \ref Deuteronomy 5:6–21|DEU 5:6-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb* \rb words:|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb “I|אָֽנֹכִ֖י֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑֔יךָ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצֵאתִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֣֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִיֽ֑ם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 3 \rb You|לְךָ֛֩\rb* \rb shall have|יִהְיֶֽה־\rb* \rb no|לֹֽ֣א\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖֜ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥֨ים\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb Me.|פָּנָֽ֗יַ׃\rb*\f + \fr 20:3 \ft Or \fqa besides Me\f*
\li1 \v 4 \rb You shall not|לֹֽ֣א\rb* \rb make|תַֽעֲשֶׂ֨ה־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֥֣\rb* \rb an idol|פֶ֣֙סֶל֙׀\rb* \rb in the form|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of anything|תְּמוּנָ֡֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר֣\rb* \rb in the heavens|בַּשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙׀\rb* \rb above,|מִמַּ֡֔עַל\rb*\rb |וַֽאֲשֶׁ֥ר֩\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֖֨רֶץ\rb* \rb below,|מִתַָּ֑֜חַת\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥֣ר\rb* \rb or in the waters|בַּמַּ֖֣יִם׀\rb* \rb beneath.|מִתַּ֥֣חַת\rb*\rb |לָאָֽ֗רֶץ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bow down|תִשְׁתַּחְוֶ֥֣ה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם֮\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb worship them;|תָעָבְדֵ֑ם֒\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I,|אָֽנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb am a jealous|קַנָּ֔א\rb* \rb God,|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb visiting|פֹּ֠קֵד\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֨ן\rb* \rb of the fathers|אָבֹ֧ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their children|בָּנִ֛ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the third|שִׁלֵּשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and fourth generations|רִבֵּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb of those who hate Me,|לְשֹׂנְאָֽ֑י׃\rb* \v 6 \rb but showing|וְעֹ֥֤שֶׂה\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֖֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to a thousand generations|לַאֲלָפִ֑֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 20:6 \ft Or \fqa to thousands\f* \rb of those who love Me|לְאֹהֲבַ֖י\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb My commandments.|מִצְוֺתָֽי׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb take|תִשָּׂ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in vain,|לַשָּׁ֑וְא\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb leave anyone unpunished|יְנַקֶּה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb takes|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in vain.|לַשָּֽׁוְא׃פ\rb*
\li1 \v 8 \rb Remember|זָכ֛וֹר֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֖֜ת\rb* \rb day|י֥֨וֹם\rb* \rb by keeping it holy.|לְקַדְּשֽׁ֗וֹ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Six|שֵׁ֤֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים֙\rb* \rb you shall labor|תַּֽעֲבֹ֔ד֮\rb* \rb and do|וְעָשִׂ֖֣יתָ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your work,|מְלַאכְתֶּֽךָ֒׃\rb* \v 10 \rb but the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔֜י\rb* \rb day|וְי֙וֹם֙\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֖֣ת׀\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑֗יךָ\rb* \rb on which you must not|לֹֽ֣א־\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֶׂ֣֨ה\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb work—|מְלָאכָ֡֜ה\rb* \rb neither you,|אַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb nor your son|וּבִנְךָֽ֣־\rb* \rb or daughter,|וּ֠בִתֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb nor your manservant|עַבְדְּךָ֤֨\rb* \rb or maidservant|וַאֲמָֽתְךָ֜֙\rb* \rb or livestock,|וּבְהֶמְתֶּ֔֗ךָ\rb* \rb nor the foreigner|וְגֵרְךָ֖֙\rb* \rb within|אֲשֶׁ֥֣ר\rb* \rb your gates.|בִּשְׁעָרֶֽ֔יךָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb in six|שֵֽׁשֶׁת־\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the sea|הַיָּם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is in them,|בָּ֔ם\rb* \rb but on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb He rested.|וַיָּ֖נַח\rb* \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|בֵּרַ֧ךְ\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb and set it apart as holy.|וַֽיְקַדְּשֵֽׁהוּ׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 12 \rb Honor|כַּבֵּ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and mother,|אִמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb may be long|יַאֲרִכ֣וּן\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 20:12 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 15:4|MAT 15:4\ref*, Matthew 19:19, Mark 7:10, Luke 18:20, and Ephesians 6:2–3\f*
\li1 \v 13 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥֖א\rb* \rb murder.|תִּֿרְצָֽ֖ח׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 20:13 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:21|MAT 5:21\ref*, Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11\f*
\li1 \v 14 \rb You shall not|לֹ֣֖א\rb* \rb commit adultery.|תִּֿנְאָֽ֑ף׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 20:14 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:27|MAT 5:27\ref*, Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11\f*
\li1 \v 15 \rb You shall not|לֹ֣֖א\rb* \rb steal.|תִּֿגְנֹֽ֔ב׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 20:15 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 19:18|MAT 19:18\ref*, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, and Romans 13:9\f*
\li1 \v 16 \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bear|תַעֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb false|שָֽׁקֶר׃ס\rb* \rb witness|עֵ֥ד\rb* \rb against your neighbor.|בְרֵעֲךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 20:16 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 19:18|MAT 19:18\ref*, Mark 10:19, and Luke 18:20\f*
\li1 \v 17 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb covet|תַחְמֹ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 20:17 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 7:7|ROM 7:7\ref* and Romans 13:9\f* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb house.|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb covet|תַחְמֹ֞ד\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb wife,|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb or his manservant|וְעַבְדּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb or maidservant,|וַאֲמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb or his ox|וְשׁוֹר֣וֹ\rb* \rb or donkey,|וַחֲמֹר֔וֹ\rb* \rb or anything|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belongs to your neighbor.”|לְרֵעֶֽךָ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Moses Comforts the People
\r \ref Deuteronomy 5:22–33|DEU 5:22-33\ref*; \ref Hebrews 12:18–29|HEB 12:18-29\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb When all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֩\rb* \rb witnessed|רֹאִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the thunder|הַקּוֹלֹ֜ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and lightning,|הַלַּפִּידִ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the sounding|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn,|הַשֹּׁפָ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the mountain|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb enveloped in smoke,|עָשֵׁ֑ן\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb they trembled|וַיָּנֻ֔עוּ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb at a distance.|מֵֽרָחֹֽק׃\rb* \v 19 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּר־\rb* \rb to us|עִמָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb yourself|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and we will listen,”|וְנִשְׁמָ֑עָה\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “But do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb let God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb speak|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to us,|עִמָּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb we will die.”|נָמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,”|תִּירָאוּ֒\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָעָם֮\rb* \rb “For|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb to|לְבַֽעֲבוּר֙\rb* \rb test you,|נַסּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that|וּבַעֲב֗וּר\rb*\rb |תִּהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb the fear of Him|יִרְאָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb may be before|עַל־\rb* \rb you,|פְּנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to keep|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you from sinning.”|תֶחֱטָֽאוּ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb at a distance|מֵרָחֹ֑ק\rb* \rb as Moses|וּמֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb approached|נִגַּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the thick darkness|הָֽעֲרָפֶ֔ל\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb God was.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*
\s1 Idolatry Forbidden
\r \ref 1 Corinthians 10:14–22|1CO 10:14-22\ref*)
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb you are to tell|תֹאמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites:|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb ‘You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have seen for yourselves|רְאִיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven.|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \v 23 \rb You are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to make|תַעֲשׂ֖וּן\rb* \rb any gods|אֱלֹ֤הֵי\rb* \rb alongside Me;|אִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to make|תַעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb gods|וֵאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb or gold.|זָהָ֔ב\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb You are to make|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for Me|לִּי֒\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of earth,|אֲדָמָה֮\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְזָבַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עֹלֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and peace offerings,|שְׁלָמֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sheep and goats|צֹֽאנְךָ֖\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and cattle.|בְּקָרֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb In every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I cause My name|שְׁמִ֔י\rb* \rb to be remembered,|אַזְכִּ֣יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will come|אָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and bless you.|וּבֵרַכְתִּֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Now if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you make|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb of stones|אֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb for Me,|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb you must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb build|תִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb it|אֶתְהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb with stones shaped by tools;|גָּזִ֑ית\rb* \rb for if|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb you use|הֵנַ֥פְתָּ\rb* \rb a chisel|חַרְבְּךָ֛\rb* \rb on it,|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb you will defile it.|וַתְּחַֽלְלֶֽהָ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb And you must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb go up|תַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb My altar|מִזְבְּחִ֑י\rb* \rb on steps,|בְמַעֲלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb lest|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb your nakedness|עֶרְוָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb be exposed|תִגָּלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on it.’|עָלָֽיו׃פ\rb*[’’]
\c 21
\s1 Hebrew Servants
\r \ref Deuteronomy 15:12–18|DEU 15:12-18\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to set|תָּשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb before them:|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you buy|תִקְנֶה֙\rb* \rb a Hebrew|עִבְרִ֔י\rb* \rb servant,|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb he is to serve you|יַעֲבֹ֑ד\rb* \rb for six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb But in the seventh year,|וּבַ֨שְּׁבִעִ֔ת\rb* \rb he shall go|יֵצֵ֥א\rb* \rb free|לַֽחָפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb without paying anything.|חִנָּֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he arrived alone,|יָבֹ֖א\rb*\rb |בְּגַפּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb he is to leave alone;|יֵצֵ֑א\rb*\rb |בְּגַפּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb*\rb |בַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb arrived with a wife,|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb she|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb is to leave|וְיָצְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb with him.|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb gives|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and she bears|וְיָלְדָה־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb daughters,|בָנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and her children|וִילָדֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb shall belong to|תִּהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb her master,|לַֽאדֹנֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and only the man|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb shall go free.|יֵצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |בְגַפּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the servant|הָעֶ֔בֶד\rb* \rb declares,|אָמֹ֤ר\rb*\rb |יֹאמַר֙\rb* \rb ‘I love|אָהַ֙בְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and my wife|אִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and children;|בָּנָ֑י\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb want to go|אֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb free,’|חָפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \v 6 \rb then his master|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb is to bring him|וְהִגִּישׁ֤וֹ\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the judges.|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 21:6 \ft Or \fqa before God\f* \rb And he shall take him|וְהִגִּישׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb doorpost|הַמְּזוּזָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנָ֤יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and pierce|וְרָצַ֨ע\rb* \rb his ear|אָזְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb with an awl.|בַּמַּרְצֵ֔עַ\rb* \rb Then he shall serve his master|וַעֲבָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb for life.|לְעֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sells|יִמְכֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb his daughter|בִּתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb as a servant,|לְאָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb she is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to go free|תֵצֵ֖א\rb*\rb |כְּצֵ֥את\rb* \rb as the menservants do.|הָעֲבָדִֽים׃\rb* \v 8 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb she is displeasing|רָעָ֞ה\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֧י\rb* \rb of her master|אֲדֹנֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had designated her for himself,|יְעָדָ֖הּ\rb*\f + \fr 21:8 \ft Or \fqa so that he does not designate her for himself\f* \rb he must allow her to be redeemed.|וְהֶפְדָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb He has no|לֹא\rb* \rb right|יִמְשֹׁ֥ל\rb* \rb to sell her|לְמָכְרָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to foreigners,|לְעַ֥ם\rb*\rb |נָכְרִ֛י\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb since he has broken faith|בְּבִגְדוֹ־\rb* \rb with her.|בָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he chooses her|יִֽיעָדֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb for his son,|לִבְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb he must deal|יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb with her|לָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb as with|כְּמִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb a daughter.|הַבָּנ֖וֹת\rb* \v 10 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he takes|יִֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb another wife,|אַחֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb reduce|יִגְרָֽע׃\rb* \rb the food,|שְׁאֵרָ֛הּ\rb* \rb clothing,|כְּסוּתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb or marital rights of his first wife.|וְעֹנָתָ֖הּ\rb* \v 11 \rb If, however,|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb provide|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb her|לָ֑הּ\rb* \rb with these|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb three things,|שְׁלָ֨שׁ־\rb* \rb she is free to go|וְיָצְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |חִנָּ֖ם\rb* \rb without|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb monetary payment.|כָּֽסֶף׃ס\rb*
\s1 Personal Injury Laws
\p \v 12 \rb Whoever strikes|מַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb and kills|וָמֵ֖ת\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb If, however,|וַאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb lie in wait,|צָדָ֔ה\rb* \rb but God|וְהָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb allowed it to happen,|אִנָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |לְיָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb then I will appoint|וְשַׂמְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a place|מָק֔וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he may flee.|יָנ֖וּס\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb schemes|בְעָרְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and acts willfully|יָזִ֥ד\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to kill him,|לְהָרְג֣וֹ\rb* \rb you must take him|תִּקָּחֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb away from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb My altar|מִזְבְּחִ֔י\rb* \rb to be put to death.|לָמֽוּת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Whoever strikes|וּמַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb or mother|וְאִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Whoever kidnaps|וְגֹנֵ֨ב\rb* \rb another man|אִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb must be put to death,|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃ס\rb* \rb whether he sells him|וּמְכָר֛וֹ\rb* \rb or the man is found|וְנִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb in his possession.|בְיָד֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Anyone who curses|וּמְקַלֵּ֥ל\rb*\f + \fr 21:17 \ft Or \fqa dishonors \ft or \fqa reviles\f* \rb his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb or mother|וְאִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 21:17 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 15:4|MAT 15:4\ref* and Mark 7:10\f*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb are quarreling|יְרִיבֻ֣ן\rb* \rb and one|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strikes|וְהִכָּה־\rb* \rb the other|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb with a stone|בְּאֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb a fist,|בְאֶגְרֹ֑ף\rb* \rb and he does not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb but is confined|וְנָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb to bed,|לְמִשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb* \v 19 \rb then the one who struck him|הַמַּכֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb shall go unpunished,|וְנִקָּ֣ה\rb* \rb as long as|אִם־\rb* \rb the other can get up|יָק֞וּם\rb* \rb and walk around|וְהִתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb outside|בַּח֛וּץ\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb his staff.|מִשְׁעַנְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Nevertheless,|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb he must compensate|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb the man for his lost work|שִׁבְתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and see that he is completely healed.|וְרַפֹּ֥א\rb*\rb |יְרַפֵּֽא׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strikes|יַכֶּה֩\rb* \rb his manservant|עַבְדּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb maidservant|אֲמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb with a rod,|בַּשֵּׁ֔בֶט\rb* \rb and the servant dies|וּמֵ֖ת\rb* \rb by|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb his hand,|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb he shall surely be punished.|נָקֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |יִנָּקֵֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb However,|אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb the servant gets up|יַעֲמֹ֑ד\rb* \rb after a day|י֛וֹם\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb two,|יוֹמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb the owner shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be punished,|יֻקַּ֔ם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the servant is|הֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb his property.|כַסְפּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who are fighting|יִנָּצ֣וּ\rb* \rb strike|וְנָ֨גְפ֜וּ\rb* \rb a pregnant|הָרָה֙\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb and her child|יְלָדֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb is born prematurely,|וְיָצְא֣וּ\rb*\f + \fr 21:22 \ft Literally \fqa and her children come out\f* \rb but there is|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb no further|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb injury,|אָס֑וֹן\rb* \rb he shall surely be fined|עָנ֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |יֵעָנֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the woman’s|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb husband|בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb demands|יָשִׁ֤ית\rb*\rb |עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and as the court allows.|וְנָתַ֖ן\rb*\rb |בִּפְלִלִֽים׃\rb* \v 23 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb a serious injury|אָס֖וֹן\rb* \rb results,|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb then you must require|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb a life|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb a life—|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*  \v 24 \rb eye|עַ֚יִן\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb eye,|עַ֔יִן\rb* \rb tooth|שֵׁ֖ן\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb tooth,|שֵׁ֑ן\rb*\f + \fr 21:24 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:38|MAT 5:38\ref*\f* \rb hand|יָ֚ד\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb hand,|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb foot|רֶ֖גֶל\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb foot,|רָֽגֶל׃\rb* \v 25 \rb burn|כְּוִיָּה֙\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb burn,|כְּוִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wound|פֶּ֖צַע\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb wound,|פָּ֑צַע\rb* \rb and stripe|חַבּוּרָ֕ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb stripe.|חַבּוּרָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strikes|יַכֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb and blinds|וְשִֽׁחֲתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the eye|עֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of his manservant|עַבְדּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb maidservant,|אֲמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb he must let the servant go|יְשַׁלְּחֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb free|לַֽחָפְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb as compensation for|תַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |עֵינֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb the eye.|עֵ֥ין\rb* \v 27 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he knocks out|יַפִּ֑יל\rb* \rb the tooth|שֵׁ֥ן\rb* \rb of his manservant|עַבְדּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb maidservant,|אֲמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb he must let the servant go|יְשַׁלְּחֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb free|לַֽחָפְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb as compensation for|תַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |שִׁנּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb the tooth.|שֵׁ֥ן\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 21:28 \ft Or \fqa a bull\ft ; also in verses 29–36\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gores|יִגַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to death,|וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb the ox|הַשּׁ֗וֹר\rb* \rb must surely be stoned,|סָק֨וֹל\rb*\rb |יִסָּקֵ֜ל\rb* \rb and its meat|בְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb* \rb must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb be eaten.|יֵאָכֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb But the owner|וּבַ֥עַל\rb* \rb of the ox|הַשּׁ֖וֹר\rb* \rb shall not be held responsible.|נָקִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb But if|וְאִ֡ם\rb* \rb the ox|שׁוֹר֩\rb* \rb has a habit|מִתְּמֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֗ם\rb* \rb of goring,|נַגָּ֨ח\rb*\rb |ה֜וּא\rb* \rb and its owner|בִּבְעָלָיו֙\rb* \rb has been warned|וְהוּעַ֤ד\rb* \rb yet does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb restrain it,|יִשְׁמְרֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb and it kills|וְהֵמִ֥ית\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb woman,|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb then the ox|הַשּׁוֹר֙\rb* \rb must be stoned|יִסָּקֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and its owner|בְּעָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb must also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb be put to death.|יוּמָֽת׃\rb* \v 30 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb payment|כֹּ֖פֶר\rb* \rb is demanded|יוּשַׁ֣ת\rb* \rb of him instead,|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb he may redeem|פִּדְיֹ֣ן\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb by paying|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb the full|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb amount demanded|יוּשַׁ֖ת\rb* \rb of him.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb If|אוֹ־\rb* \rb the ox gores|יִגָּ֖ח\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֥ן\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a daughter,|בַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יִגָּ֑ח\rb* \rb it shall be done|יֵעָ֥שֶׂה\rb* \rb to him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb according to the same|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb rule.|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the ox|הַשּׁ֖וֹר\rb* \rb gores|יִגַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a manservant|עֶ֛בֶד\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb maidservant,|אָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb the owner must pay|יִתֵּן֙\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֗ים\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֣סֶף׀\rb*\f + \fr 21:32 \fqa \ref 30|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 12|12\ref* ounces or 342 grams of silver.\f* \rb to the master of that servant,|לַֽאדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and the ox|וְהַשּׁ֖וֹר\rb* \rb must be stoned.|יִסָּקֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb opens|יִפְתַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |בּ֗וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֠וֹ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb digs|יִכְרֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb a pit|בֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb and fails|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to cover it,|יְכַסֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb and an ox|שּׁ֖וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb a donkey|חֲמֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb falls|וְנָֽפַל־\rb* \rb into it,|שָׁ֥מָּה\rb* \v 34 \rb the owner|בַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb of the pit|הַבּוֹר֙\rb* \rb shall make restitution;|יְשַׁלֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb he must pay|יָשִׁ֣יב\rb*\rb |כֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb its owner,|לִבְעָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and the dead animal|וְהַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his.|לּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man’s|אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ox|שֽׁוֹר־\rb* \rb injures|יִגֹּ֧ף\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb ox|שׁ֥וֹר\rb* \rb and it dies,|וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb they must sell|וּמָ֨כְר֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the live|הַחַי֙\rb* \rb one|הַשּׁ֤וֹר\rb* \rb and divide|וְחָצ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the proceeds;|כַּסְפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb they also must|וְגַ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb divide|יֶֽחֱצֽוּן׃\rb* \rb the dead animal.|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \v 36 \rb But if|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb it was known|נוֹדַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb the ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb had a habit|מִתְּמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֔ם\rb* \rb of goring,|נַגָּ֥ח\rb*\rb |הוּא֙\rb* \rb yet its owner|בְּעָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb failed|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to restrain it,|יִשְׁמְרֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb he shall pay full compensation,|שַׁלֵּ֨ם\rb*\rb |יְשַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb ox|שׁוֹר֙\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb ox,|הַשּׁ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and the dead animal|וְהַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his.|לּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*[’’]
\c 22
\s1 Property Laws
\p \v 1 \rb “If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb steals|יִגְנֹֽב־\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 22:1 \ft Or \fqa a bull \ft or \fqa a cow\ft ; also in verses 4, 9, and 10\f* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a sheep|שֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and slaughters|וּטְבָח֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb sells it,|מְכָר֑וֹ\rb* \rb he must repay|יְשַׁלֵּם֙\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb oxen|בָקָ֗ר\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb*\rb |תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb an ox|הַשּׁ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבַּע־\rb* \rb sheep|הַשֶּֽׂה׃\rb* \rb for a sheep.|צֹ֖אן\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb a thief|הַגַּנָּ֖ב\rb* \rb is caught|יִמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb breaking in|בַּמַּחְתֶּ֛רֶת\rb* \rb and is beaten|וְהֻכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to death,|וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb no one|אֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb shall be guilty of bloodshed.|דָּמִֽים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb it happens after sunrise,|זָרְחָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֛מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb there is guilt for his bloodshed.|דָּמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb*
\p \rb A thief must make full restitution;|שַׁלֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |יְשַׁלֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb he has nothing,|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb he himself shall be sold|וְנִמְכַּ֖ר\rb* \rb for his theft.|בִּגְנֵבָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb If what was stolen|אִֽם־\rb*\rb |הַגְּנֵבָ֗ה\rb* \rb is actually found|הִמָּצֵא֩\rb*\rb |תִמָּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb in his possession—|בְיָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb whether ox|מִשּׁ֧וֹר\rb* \rb or|עַד־\rb* \rb donkey|חֲמ֛וֹר\rb* \rb or|עַד־\rb* \rb sheep—|שֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb he must pay back|יְשַׁלֵּֽם׃ס\rb* \rb double.|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb grazes his livestock|יַבְעֶר־\rb* \rb in a field|שָׂדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb vineyard|כֶ֔רֶם\rb* \rb and allows them|בְּעִירֹה\rb* \rb to stray|וְשִׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they graze|וּבִעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in someone else’s|אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb field,|בִּשְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb he must make restitution|יְשַׁלֵּֽם׃ס\rb* \rb from the best|מֵיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb of his own field|שָׂדֵ֛הוּ\rb*\rb |וּמֵיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb or vineyard.|כַּרְמ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb breaks out|תֵצֵ֨א\rb* \rb and spreads|וּמָצְאָ֤ה\rb* \rb to thornbushes|קֹצִים֙\rb* \rb so that it consumes|וְנֶאֱכַ֣ל\rb* \rb stacked|גָּדִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb standing grain,|הַקָּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb the whole field,|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb the one who started|הַמַּבְעִ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fire|הַבְּעֵרָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb must make full restitution.|שַׁלֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |יְשַׁלֵּ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb gives|יִתֵּן֩\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb goods|כֵלִים֙\rb* \rb for safekeeping|לִשְׁמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and they are stolen|וְגֻנַּ֖ב\rb* \rb from the neighbor’s|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb house,|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb the thief,|הַגַּנָּ֖ב\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb caught,|יִמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb must pay back|יְשַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb double.|שְׁנָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the thief|הַגַּנָּ֔ב\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb found,|יִמָּצֵא֙\rb* \rb the owner|בַּֽעַל־\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb must appear|וְנִקְרַ֥ב\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the judges|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 22:8 \ft Or \fqa before God\ft ; also in verse 9\f* \rb to determine whether|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb he has taken|שָׁלַ֛ח\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb property.|בִּמְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb In|עַֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb cases|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of illegal possession|פֶּ֡שַׁע\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb an ox,|שׁ֡וֹר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb a donkey,|חֲ֠מוֹר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb a sheep,|שֶׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb a garment,|שַׂלְמָ֜ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb or any|כָּל־\rb* \rb lost item|אֲבֵדָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb someone claims,|יֹאמַר֙\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb ‘This|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb is mine,’|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb both parties|שְׁנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb shall bring|יָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb their cases|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb before|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the judges.|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb The one whom the judges|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb find guilty|יַרְשִׁיעֻן֙\rb*\f + \fr 22:9 \ft Or \fqa whom God condemns\f* \rb must pay back|יְשַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb double|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to his neighbor.|לְרֵעֵֽהוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb gives|יִתֵּן֩\rb* \rb a donkey,|חֲמ֨וֹר\rb* \rb an ox,|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb a sheep,|שֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb or any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb other animal|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb to be cared for|לִשְׁמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb by his neighbor,|רֵעֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb but it dies|וּמֵ֛ת\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb is injured|נִשְׁבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb stolen|נִשְׁבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb while no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one is watching,|רֹאֶֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb an oath|שְׁבֻעַ֣ת\rb* \rb before the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb shall be made|תִּהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the parties|שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to determine whether|אִם־\rb* \rb or not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the man has taken|שָׁלַ֛ח\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb property.|בִּמְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb The owner|בְּעָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb must accept the oath|וְלָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb and require no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb restitution.|יְשַׁלֵּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the animal was actually|גָּנֹ֥ב\rb* \rb stolen|יִגָּנֵ֖ב\rb* \rb from the neighbor,|מֵעִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb he must make restitution|יְשַׁלֵּ֖ם\rb* \rb to the owner.|לִבְעָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the animal was torn to pieces,|טָרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |יִטָּרֵ֖ף\rb* \rb he shall bring|יְבִאֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb it as evidence;|עֵ֑ד\rb* \rb he need not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb make restitution|יְשַׁלֵּֽם׃פ\rb* \rb for the torn carcass.|הַטְּרֵפָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb borrows|יִשְׁאַ֥ל\rb* \rb an animal|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb from his neighbor|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and it is injured|וְנִשְׁבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb dies|מֵ֑ת\rb* \rb while its owner|בְּעָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb is not|אֵין־\rb* \rb present,|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb he must make full restitution.|שַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb*\rb |יְשַׁלֵּֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the owner|בְּעָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb was present,|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb restitution is required.|יְשַׁלֵּ֑ם\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the animal|ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |בָּ֖א\rb* \rb was rented,|שָׂכִ֣יר\rb* \rb the fee covers the loss.|בִּשְׂכָרֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Laws of Social Responsibility
\p \v 16 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb seduces|יְפַתֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb a virgin|בְּתוּלָ֛ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pledged in marriage|אֹרָ֖שָׂה\rb* \rb and sleeps|וְשָׁכַ֣ב\rb* \rb with her,|עִמָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb he must pay the full dowry|מָהֹ֛ר\rb*\rb |יִמְהָרֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb for her|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to be his wife.|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb absolutely refuses|מָאֵ֧ן\rb*\rb |יְמָאֵ֛ן\rb* \rb to give her|לְתִתָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb to him,|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb the man still must pay|יִשְׁקֹ֔ל\rb* \rb an amount comparable|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb to the bridal price|כְּמֹ֖הַר\rb* \rb of a virgin.|הַבְּתוּלֹֽת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb allow a sorceress|מְכַשֵּׁפָ֖ה\rb* \rb to live.|תְחַיֶּֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb lies|שֹׁכֵ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb an animal|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb If anyone sacrifices|זֹבֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb to any god|לָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb other than|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb alone,|לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb he must be set apart for destruction.|יָֽחֳרָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 22:20 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f*
\p \v 21 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb exploit|תוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb oppress|תִלְחָצֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb a foreign resident,|וְגֵ֥ר\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you yourselves were|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb foreigners|גֵרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb mistreat|תְעַנּֽוּן׃\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb widow|אַלְמָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb or orphan.|וְיָת֖וֹם\rb* \v 23 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do mistreat them,|עַנֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |תְעַנֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb and they cry out|צָעֹ֤ק\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb in distress,|יִצְעַק֙\rb* \rb I will surely hear|שָׁמֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |אֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb their cry.|צַעֲקָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 24 \rb My anger|אַפִּ֔י\rb* \rb will be kindled,|וְחָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and I will kill|וְהָרַגְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with the sword;|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb then your wives|נְשֵׁיכֶם֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb widows|אַלְמָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and your children|וּבְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will be fatherless.|יְתֹמִֽים׃פ\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you lend|תַּלְוֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֣סֶף׀\rb* \rb to one of My people|עַמִּ֗י\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb who is poor,|הֶֽעָנִי֙\rb* \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb act|תִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb as a creditor|כְּנֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb to him;|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb you are not to charge|תְשִׂימ֥וּן\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb him|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb interest.|נֶֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you take your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb cloak|שַׂלְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb as collateral,|חָבֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |תַּחְבֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb return it|תְּשִׁיבֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb by|עַד־\rb* \rb sunset,|בֹּ֥א\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \v 27 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb his cloak|הִ֤וא\rb* \rb is the only|לְבַדָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb covering|כְסוּתָה\rb* \rb he has|הִ֥וא\rb* \rb for|שִׂמְלָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb his body.|לְעֹר֑וֹ\rb* \rb What else|בַּמֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb will he sleep in?|יִשְׁכָּ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb And if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he cries out|יִצְעַ֣ק\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb I will hear,|וְשָׁמַעְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָֽנִי׃ס\rb* \rb am compassionate.|חַנּ֥וּן\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb blaspheme|תְקַלֵּ֑ל\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb or curse|תָאֹֽר׃\rb* \rb the ruler|וְנָשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb of your people.|בְעַמְּךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 22:28 \ft LXX \fqa or speak evil about the ruler of your people\ft ; cited in \ref Acts 23:5|ACT 23:5\ref*\f*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb hold back|תְאַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb offerings from your granaries|מְלֵאָתְךָ֥\rb* \rb or vats.|וְדִמְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb You are to give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb Me|לִּֽי׃\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of your sons.|בָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 30 \rb You shall do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb likewise|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb with your cattle|לְשֹׁרְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your sheep.|לְצֹאנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Let them stay|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb their mothers|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb but on the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb you are to give them|תִּתְּנוֹ־\rb* \rb to Me.|לִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb You are to be|תִּהְי֣וּן\rb* \rb My|לִ֑י\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb people.|וְאַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb the meat|וּבָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb of a mauled animal|טְרֵפָה֙\rb* \rb found in the field;|בַּשָּׂדֶ֤ה\rb* \rb you are to throw|תַּשְׁלִכ֥וּן\rb* \rb it|אֹתֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb to the dogs.|לַכֶּ֖לֶב\rb*[’’]
\c 23
\s1 Justice and Mercy
\p \v 1 \rb “You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb spread|תִשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb a false|שָׁ֑וְא\rb* \rb report.|שֵׁ֣מַע\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb join|תָּ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָֽדְךָ֙\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb by being|לִהְיֹ֖ת\rb* \rb a malicious|חָמָֽס׃ס\rb* \rb witness.|עֵ֥ד\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb follow|תִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵֽי־\rb* \rb the crowd|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in wrongdoing.|לְרָעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb When you testify|תַעֲנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb a lawsuit,|רִ֗ב\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb pervert justice|לְהַטֹּֽת׃\rb* \rb by siding|לִנְטֹ֛ת\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the crowd.|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \v 3 \rb And do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb show favoritism|תֶהְדַּ֖ר\rb* \rb to a poor man|וְדָ֕ל\rb* \rb in his lawsuit.|בְּרִיבֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you encounter|תִפְגַּ֞ע\rb* \rb your enemy’s|אֹֽיִבְךָ֛\rb* \rb stray|תֹּעֶ֑ה\rb* \rb ox|שׁ֧וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb donkey,|חֲמֹר֖וֹ\rb* \rb you must return it|הָשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |תְּשִׁיבֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb to him.|לֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you see|תִרְאֶ֞ה\rb* \rb the donkey|חֲמ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of one who hates you|שֹׂנַאֲךָ֗\rb* \rb fallen|רֹבֵץ֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb its load,|מַשָּׂא֔וֹ\rb* \rb do not|וְחָדַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb leave|מֵעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb it there;|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb you must help him|עָזֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |תַּעֲזֹ֖ב\rb* \rb with it.|עִמּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb deny|תַטֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb to the poor|אֶבְיֹנְךָ֖\rb* \rb in their lawsuits.|בְּרִיבֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Stay far away|תִּרְחָ֑ק\rb* \rb from a false|שֶׁ֖קֶר\rb* \rb accusation.|מִדְּבַר־\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb kill|תַּהֲרֹ֔ג\rb* \rb the innocent|וְנָקִ֤י\rb* \rb or the just,|וְצַדִּיק֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb acquit|אַצְדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb the guilty.|רָשָֽׁע׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb accept|תִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb a bribe,|וְשֹׁ֖חַד\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a bribe|הַשֹּׁ֙חַד֙\rb* \rb blinds|יְעַוֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb those who see|פִּקְחִ֔ים\rb* \rb and twists|וִֽיסַלֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the righteous.|צַדִּיקִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb oppress|תִלְחָ֑ץ\rb* \rb a foreign resident,|וְגֵ֖ר\rb* \rb since you|וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb yourselves know|יְדַעְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb how it feels to be foreigners;|הַגֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you were|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb foreigners|גֵרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\s1 Sabbath Laws
\r \ref Leviticus 25:1–7|LEV 25:1-7\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 15:1–6|DEU 15:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb For six|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb you are to sow|תִּזְרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your land|אַרְצֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and gather|וְאָסַפְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its produce,|תְּבוּאָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb but in the seventh year|וְהַשְּׁבִיעִ֞ת\rb* \rb you must let it rest|תִּשְׁמְטֶ֣נָּה\rb* \rb and lie fallow,|וּנְטַשְׁתָּ֗הּ\rb* \rb so that the poor|אֶבְיֹנֵ֣י\rb* \rb among your people|עַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb may eat|וְאָֽכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb from the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb and the wild animals|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb may consume|תֹּאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb what they leave.|וְיִתְרָ֕ם\rb* \rb Do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the same|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb with your vineyard|לְכַרְמְךָ֖\rb* \rb and olive grove.|לְזֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb For six|שֵׁ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb you are to do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb your work,|מַעֲשֶׂ֔יךָ\rb* \rb but on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb you must cease,|תִּשְׁבֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb your ox|שֽׁוֹרְךָ֙\rb* \rb and your donkey|וַחֲמֹרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb may rest|יָנ֗וּחַ\rb* \rb and the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of your maidservant|אֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb may be refreshed,|וְיִנָּפֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb as well as the foreign resident.|וְהַגֵּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Pay close attention|תִּשָּׁמֵ֑רוּ\rb* \rb to everything|וּבְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have said|אָמַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb to you.|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb invoke|תַזְכִּ֔ירוּ\rb* \rb the names|וְשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb of other|אֲחֵרִים֙\rb* \rb gods;|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb they must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be heard|יִשָּׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your lips.|פִּֽיךָ׃\rb*
\s1 The Three Feasts of Pilgrimage
\r \ref Leviticus 23:1–3|LEV 23:1-3\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb Three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb times|רְגָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb you are to celebrate a feast|תָּחֹ֥ג\rb* \rb to Me.|לִ֖י\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You are to keep|תִּשְׁמֹר֒\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֣ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּוֹת֮\rb*\f + \fr 23:15 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see \ref Exodus 12:14–20|EXO 12:14-20\ref*.\f* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I commanded you:|צִוִּיתִ֗ךָ\rb* \rb At the appointed time|לְמוֹעֵד֙\rb* \rb in the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib|הָֽאָבִ֔יב\rb*\f + \fr 23:15 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \rb you are to eat|תֹּאכַ֨ל\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִים֩\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb that was the month|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb you came out|יָצָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb No one|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb may appear|יֵרָא֥וּ\rb* \rb before Me|פָנַ֖י\rb* \rb empty-handed.|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb You are also to keep the Feast|וְחַ֤ג\rb* \rb of Harvest|הַקָּצִיר֙\rb*\f + \fr 23:16 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Weeks\ft (see \ref Exodus 34:22|EXO 34:22\ref*) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see \ref Acts 2:1|ACT 2:1\ref*).\f* \rb with the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the produce|מַעֲשֶׂ֔יךָ\rb* \rb from what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you sow|תִּזְרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the field.|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb And keep the Feast|וְחַ֤ג\rb* \rb of Ingathering|הָֽאָסִף֙\rb*\f + \fr 23:16 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is later called \fqa the Feast of Tabernacles \ft (or \fqa Booths \ft or \fqa Shelters\ft ).\f* \rb at the end|בְּצֵ֣את\rb* \rb of the year,|הַשָּׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb when you gather|בְּאָסְפְּךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your produce|מַעֲשֶׂ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field.|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your males|זְכ֣וּרְךָ֔\rb* \rb are to appear|יֵרָאֶה֙\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Lord|הָאָדֹ֥ן׀\rb* \rb GOD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb offer|תִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the blood|דַּם־\rb* \rb of My sacrifices|זִבְחִ֑י\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb anything leavened,|חָמֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb nor may|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb the fat|חֵֽלֶב־\rb* \rb of My feast|חַגִּ֖י\rb* \rb remain|יָלִ֥ין\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Bring|תָּבִ֕יא\rb* \rb the best|רֵאשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb of the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵי֙\rb* \rb of your soil|אַדְמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb cook|תְבַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִ֖י\rb* \rb in its mother’s|אִמּֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb milk.|בַּחֲלֵ֥ב\rb*
\s1 God’s Angel to Lead
\r \ref Deuteronomy 7:12–26|DEU 7:12-26\ref*)
\p \v 20 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb am sending|שֹׁלֵ֤חַ\rb* \rb an angel|מַלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to protect you|לִשְׁמָרְךָ֖\rb* \rb along the way|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb and to bring you|וְלַהֲבִ֣יאֲךָ֔\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have prepared.|הֲכִנֹֽתִי׃\rb* \v 21 \rb Pay attention|הִשָּׁ֧מֶר\rb* \rb to him|מִפָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and listen|וּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to his voice;|בְּקֹל֖וֹ\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb defy|תַּמֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb him,|בּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb forgive|יִשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb rebellion,|לְפִשְׁעֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb is in him.|בְּקִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will listen carefully|שָׁמֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb to his voice|בְּקֹל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and do|וְעָשִׂ֕יתָ\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I say,|אֲדַבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb I will be an enemy|אֹ֣יְבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to your enemies|וְאָֽיַבְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and a foe|וְצַרְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your foes.|צֹרְרֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb My angel|מַלְאָכִי֮\rb* \rb will go|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶיךָ֒\rb* \rb and bring you|וֶהֱבִֽיאֲךָ֗\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land of the Amorites,|הָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַ֣חִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּי֙\rb* \rb Canaanites,|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites,|וְהַיְבוּסִ֑י\rb* \rb and I will annihilate them.|וְהִכְחַדְתִּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bow down|תִשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֤ה\rb* \rb to their gods|לֵאלֹֽהֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb or serve them|תָֽעָבְדֵ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb follow|תַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb their practices.|כְּמַֽעֲשֵׂיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Instead,|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you are to demolish them|הָרֵס֙\rb*\rb |תְּהָ֣רְסֵ֔ם\rb* \rb and smash their sacred stones|מַצֵּבֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb to pieces.|וְשַׁבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |תְּשַׁבֵּ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb So you shall serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and He will bless|וּבֵרַ֥ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 23:25 \ft LXX and Vulgate \fqa I will bless\f*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמְךָ֖\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb your water.|מֵימֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb And I will take away|וַהֲסִרֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb sickness|מַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb No|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb woman in your land|בְּאַרְצֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |תִהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb will miscarry|מְשַׁכֵּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb or be barren;|וַעֲקָרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will fulfill|אֲמַלֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb the number|מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of your days.|יָמֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will send|אֲשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb My terror|אֵֽימָתִי֙\rb* \rb ahead of you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and throw into confusion|וְהַמֹּתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb nation|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you encounter.|תָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb I will make all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb turn|וְנָתַתִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and run.|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |עֹֽרֶף׃\rb* \v 28 \rb I will send|וְשָׁלַחְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hornet|הַצִּרְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb to drive|וְגֵרְשָׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Hivites|הַחִוִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֛י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Hittites|הַחִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb out of your way.|מִלְּפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb I will not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb drive them out|אֲגָרְשֶׁ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in a single|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb year;|בְּשָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb would become|תִּהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and wild|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \rb animals|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb would multiply|וְרַבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb against you.|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 30 \rb Little|מְעַ֥ט\rb* \rb by little|מְעַ֛ט\rb* \rb I will drive them out|אֲגָרְשֶׁ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb ahead of you,|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you become fruitful|תִּפְרֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and possess|וְנָחַלְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb And I will establish|וְשַׁתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your borders|גְּבֻלְךָ֗\rb* \rb from the Red|סוּף֙\rb* \rb Sea|מִיַּם־\rb*\f + \fr 23:31 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the Sea|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the Philistines,|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and from the desert|וּמִמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Euphrates.|הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*\f + \fr 23:31 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I will deliver|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb into your hand,|בְּיֶדְכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb and you will drive them out|וְגֵרַשְׁתָּ֖מוֹ\rb* \rb before you.|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 32 \rb You shall make|תִכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִֽית׃\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb or with their gods.|וְלֵאלֹֽהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 33 \rb They must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb remain|יֵשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in your land,|בְּאַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb they cause you to sin|יַחֲטִ֥יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb against Me.|לִ֑י\rb* \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb if you serve|תַעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gods,|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb it will surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵֽשׁ׃פ\rb* \rb to you.”|לְךָ֖\rb*
\c 24
\s1 The Covenant Sealed
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD said|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb “Come up|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD—|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*  \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb and Abihu,|וַאֲבִיה֔וּא\rb* \rb and seventy|וְשִׁבְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb of Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb elders—|מִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb*  \rb and you are to worship|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb at a distance.|מֵרָחֹֽק׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb shall approach|וְנִגַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb but the others|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb come near.|יִגָּ֑שׁוּ\rb* \rb And the people|וְהָעָ֕ם\rb* \rb may not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go up|יַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb with him.”|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb and told|וַיְסַפֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb the people|לָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֑ים\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb they|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb responded|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb with one|אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb voice:|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb “All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken,|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb we will do.”|נַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb wrote down|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\p \rb Early the next morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb he got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb at the base of|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb along with twelve|וּשְׁתֵּ֤ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb pillars|מַצֵּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb for the twelve|לִשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then he sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb some young men|נַעֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and they offered|וַיַּֽעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וַֽיִּזְבְּח֞וּ\rb* \rb young bulls|פָּרִֽים׃\rb* \rb as peace|שְׁלָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb offerings|זְבָחִ֧ים\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb of the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and put it|וַיָּ֖שֶׂם\rb* \rb in bowls,|בָּאַגָּנֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and the other half|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb he splattered|זָרַ֖ק\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb and read it|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb who replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “All|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb we will do,|נַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb and we will be obedient.”|וְנִשְׁמָֽע׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the blood,|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb splattered|וַיִּזְרֹ֖ק\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “This|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb is the blood|דַֽם־\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has made|כָּרַ֤ת\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in accordance with|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words.”|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 24:8 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 9:20|HEB 9:20\ref*\f*
\p \v 9 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb with Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָב֙\rb* \rb and Abihu,|וַאֲבִיה֔וּא\rb* \rb and seventy|וְשִׁבְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb and they saw|וַיִּרְא֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Under|וְתַ֣חַת\rb* \rb His feet|רַגְלָ֗יו\rb* \rb was a work|כְּמַעֲשֵׂה֙\rb* \rb like a pavement|לִבְנַ֣ת\rb* \rb made of sapphire,|הַסַּפִּ֔יר\rb*\rb |וּכְעֶ֥צֶם\rb* \rb as clear|לָטֹֽהַר׃\rb* \rb as the sky itself.|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \v 11 \rb But|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lay|שָׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb His hand|יָד֑וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the nobles|אֲצִילֵי֙\rb* \rb of Israel;|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb they saw|וַֽיֶּחֱזוּ֙\rb* \rb Him,|אֶת־\rb* \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb and drank.|וַיִּשְׁתּֽוּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Moses on the Mountain
\p \v 12 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Come up|עֲלֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb on the mountain|הָהָ֖רָה\rb* \rb and stay|וֶהְיֵה־\rb* \rb here,|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb so that I may give|וְאֶתְּנָ֨ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֜\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tablets|לֻחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of stone,|הָאֶ֗בֶן\rb* \rb with the law|וְהַתּוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb and commandments|וְהַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have written|כָּתַ֖בְתִּי\rb* \rb for their instruction.”|לְהוֹרֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb with Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb his attendant|מְשָׁרְת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb*\rb |מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountain|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb he said|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb to the elders,|הַזְּקֵנִ֤ים\rb* \rb “Wait|שְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb here|בָזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb for us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we return|נָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to you.|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and Hur|וְחוּר֙\rb* \rb are here|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb with you.|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Whoever|מִי־\rb*\rb |בַ֥עַל\rb* \rb has a dispute|דְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb can go|יִגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to them.”|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb on the mountain,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb covered it,|וַיְכַ֥ס\rb*\rb |הָהָֽר׃\rb* \v 16 \rb and the glory|כְּבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb settled|וַיִּשְׁכֹּ֤ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai.|סִינַ֔י\rb* \rb For six|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb covered it,|וַיְכַסֵּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD called|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb from within|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the cloud.|הֶעָנָֽן׃\rb* \v 17 \rb And the sight|וּמַרְאֵה֙\rb* \rb of the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was like a consuming|אֹכֶ֖לֶת\rb* \rb fire|כְּאֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb on the mountaintop|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb as he went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb and he|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb remained|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָ֔ר\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb nights.|לָֽיְלָה׃פ\rb*
\c 25
\s1 Offerings for the Tabernacle
\r \ref Exodus 35:4–9|EXO 35:4-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּר֙\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to bring|וְיִקְחוּ־\rb* \rb Me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb an offering.|תְּרוּמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb You are to receive|תִּקְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My offering|תְּרוּמָתִֽי׃\rb* \rb from every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb compels him.|יִדְּבֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \v 3 \rb This|וְזֹאת֙\rb* \rb is the offering|הַתְּרוּמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to accept|תִּקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb from them:|מֵאִתָּ֑ם\rb*
\li1 \rb gold,|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb silver,|וָכֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and bronze;|וּנְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\li1 \v 4 \rb blue,|וּתְכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn;|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb*
\li1 \rb fine linen|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and goat hair;|וְעִזִּֽים׃\rb*
\li1 \v 5 \rb ram|אֵילִ֧ם\rb* \rb skins|וְעֹרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb dyed red|מְאָדָּמִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְעֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and fine leather;|תְּחָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 25:5 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals\f*
\li1 \rb acacia|שִׁטִּֽים׃\rb* \rb wood;|וַעֲצֵ֥י\rb*
\li1 \v 6 \rb olive oil|שֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb for the light;|לַמָּאֹ֑ר\rb*
\li1 \rb spices|בְּשָׂמִים֙\rb* \rb for the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil|לְשֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and for the fragrant|הַסַּמִּֽים׃\rb* \rb incense;|וְלִקְטֹ֖רֶת\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb and onyx stones|אַבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֕הַם\rb* \rb and gemstones|וְאַבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb to be mounted|מִלֻּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb on the ephod|לָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb and breastpiece.|וְלַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And they are to make|וְעָ֥שׂוּ\rb* \rb a sanctuary|מִקְדָּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb for Me,|לִ֖י\rb* \rb so that I may dwell|וְשָׁכַנְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb among them.|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb You must make|תַּעֲשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb design|תַּבְנִ֣ית\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its furnishings|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb according to|כְּכֹ֗ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the pattern|תַּבְנִ֣ית\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb show|מַרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb you.|אוֹתְךָ֔\rb*
\s1 The Ark of the Covenant
\r \ref Exodus 37:1–5|EXO 37:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb And they are to construct|וְעָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb an ark|אֲר֖וֹן\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood,|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb two|אַמָּתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb and a half cubits|וָחֵ֜צִי\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֙צִי֙\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 25:10 \ft The ark was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long, 2.25 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (114.3 centimeters long, 68.6 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 11 \rb Overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֤\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb it with pure|טָה֔וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*\rb |תְּצַפֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb both inside|מִבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb and out,|וּמִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֧יתָ\rb*\rb |עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Cast|וְיָצַ֣קְתָּ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb for it|לּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and fasten them|וְנָ֣תַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb its four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb feet,|פַּעֲמֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb rings|טַבָּעֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb one|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb side|צַלְעוֹ֙\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּי֙\rb*\rb |טַבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the other.|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*\rb |צַלְע֖וֹ\rb* \v 13 \rb And make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb poles|בַדֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Insert|וְהֵֽבֵאתָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּים֙\rb* \rb into the rings|בַּטַּבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the sides|צַלְעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the ark,|הָאָרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb in order to carry|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it.|הָאָרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb The poles|הַבַּדִּ֑ים\rb* \rb are to remain|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb in the rings|בְּטַבְּעֹת֙\rb* \rb of the ark;|הָאָרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb they must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be removed.|יָסֻ֖רוּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb And place|וְנָתַתָּ֖\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹ֑ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 25:16 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments; also in verses 21 and 22.\f* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb you.|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\s1 The Mercy Seat
\r \ref Exodus 37:6–9|EXO 37:6-9\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb And you are to construct|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a mercy seat|כַפֹּ֖רֶת\rb*\f + \fr 25:17 \ft Or \fqa an atonement cover\ft ; here and throughout Exodus\f* \rb of pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb two|אַמָּתַ֤יִם\rb* \rb and a half cubits|וָחֵ֙צִי֙\rb* \rb long|אָרְכָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb wide.|רָחְבָּֽהּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 25:17 \ft The mercy seat was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long and 2.25 feet wide (114.3 centimeters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f* \v 18 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֛יתָ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרֻבִ֖ים\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of hammered|מִקְשָׁה֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb at the|מִשְּׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb ends|קְצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the mercy seat,|הַכַּפֹּֽרֶת׃\rb* \v 19 \rb |וַ֠עֲשֵׂה\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb cherub|כְּר֨וּב\rb* \rb on one|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb end|מִקָּצָה֙\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |וּכְרוּב־\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb on the other,|מִקָּצָ֖ה\rb* \rb all made|תַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb from one piece of gold.|קְצוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \v 20 \rb And the cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִים֩\rb* \rb are to have|וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb wings|כְנָפַ֜יִם\rb* \rb that spread|פֹּרְשֵׂ֨י\rb* \rb upward,|לְמַ֗עְלָה\rb* \rb overshadowing|סֹכְכִ֤ים\rb* \rb the mercy seat.|הַכַּפֹּ֔רֶת\rb*\rb |בְּכַנְפֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb The cherubim are to face|וּפְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb other,|אָחִ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַכְּרֻבִֽים׃\rb* \rb looking|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mercy seat.|הַכַּפֹּ֔רֶת\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Set|וְנָתַתָּ֧\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֛רֶת\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb*\rb |מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and put|תִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Testimony|הָ֣עֵדֻ֔ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb into|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the ark.|הָ֣אָרֹ֔ן\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And I will meet|וְנוֹעַדְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb with you|לְךָ֮\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֒\rb* \rb above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the mercy seat,|הַכַּפֹּ֗רֶת\rb* \rb between|מִבֵּין֙\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb are over|עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony;|הָעֵדֻ֑ת\rb*\f + \fr 25:22 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb I will speak|וְדִבַּרְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֜\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I command|אֲצַוֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb regarding|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Table of Showbread
\r \ref Exodus 37:10–16|EXO 37:10-16\ref*; \ref Leviticus 24:5–9|LEV 24:5-9\ref*)
\p \v 23 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a table|שֻׁלְחָ֖ן\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb two cubits|אַמָּתַ֤יִם\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּוֹ֙\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 25:23 \ft The table was \ref approximately 3|3\ref* feet long, 1.5 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (91.4 centimeters long, 45.7 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 24 \rb Overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 25 \rb And make|וְעָשִׂ֨יתָ\rb* \rb a rim|מִסְגֶּ֛רֶת\rb* \rb around it|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb a handbreadth wide|טֹ֖פַח\rb*\f + \fr 25:25 \fqa A handbreadth\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref*.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \rb and put|וְעָשִׂ֧יתָ\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵר־\rb* \rb on|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the rim.|לְמִסְגַּרְתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb for the table|לּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and fasten|וְנָתַתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הַטַּבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb corners|הַפֵּאֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb at its four|לְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb legs.|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 27 \rb The rings|הַטַּבָּעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb are to be|תִּהְיֶ֖יןָ\rb* \rb close|לְעֻמַּת֙\rb* \rb to the rim,|הַמִּסְגֶּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb to serve as holders|לְבָתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb for the poles|לְבַדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb used to carry|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table.|הַשֻּׁלְחָֽן׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּים֙\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold,|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb so that the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָֽן׃\rb* \rb may be carried|וְנִשָּׂא־\rb* \rb with them.|בָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֨יתָ\rb* \rb the plates|קְּעָרֹתָ֜יו\rb* \rb and dishes,|וְכַפֹּתָ֗יו\rb* \rb as well as the pitchers|וּקְשׂוֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb and bowls|וּמְנַקִּיֹּתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb for pouring drink offerings.|יֻסַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |בָּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb out of pure|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb And place|וְנָתַתָּ֧\rb* \rb the Bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of the Presence|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֛ן\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֥י\rb* \rb at all times.|תָּמִֽיד׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Lampstand
\r \ref Exodus 37:17–24|EXO 37:17-24\ref*; \ref Numbers 8:1–4|NUM 8:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 31 \rb Then you are to make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a lampstand|מְנֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of pure,|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb hammered|מִקְשָׁ֞ה\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb It|הַמְּנוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb shall be made|תֵּעָשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb of one piece,|מִמֶּ֥נָּה\rb* \rb including|יִהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb its base|יְרֵכָ֣הּ\rb* \rb and shaft,|וְקָנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb its cups,|גְּבִיעֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb and its buds|כַּפְתֹּרֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb and petals.|וּפְרָחֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb Six|וְשִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb branches|קָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb are to extend|יֹצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from the sides|מִצִּדֶּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb of the lampstand—|מְנֹרָ֗ה\rb*  \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |קְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb on one|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb side|מִצִּדָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb*\rb |קְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מְנֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the other.|הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb*\rb |מִצִּדָּ֖הּ\rb* \v 33 \rb There are to be three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb cups|גְ֠בִעִים\rb* \rb shaped like almond blossoms|מְֽשֻׁקָּדִ֞ים\rb* \rb on the first|הָאֶחָד֮\rb* \rb branch,|בַּקָּנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb each with buds|כַּפְתֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb and petals,|וָפֶרַח֒\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |גְבִעִ֗ים\rb*\rb |מְשֻׁקָּדִ֛ים\rb*\rb |כַּפְתֹּ֣ר\rb*\rb |וָפָ֑רַח\rb* \rb on the next|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb branch,|בַּקָּנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and the same|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb for all six|לְשֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb branches|הַקָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb that extend|הַיֹּצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lampstand.|הַמְּנֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb And on the lampstand|וּבַמְּנֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb there shall be four|אַרְבָּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb cups|גְבִעִ֑ים\rb* \rb shaped like almond blossoms|מְשֻׁקָּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb with buds|כַּפְתֹּרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and petals.|וּפְרָחֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 35 \rb For the six|לְשֵׁ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb branches|הַקָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb that extend|הַיֹּצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lampstand,|הַמְּנֹרָֽה׃\rb* \rb a bud|וְכַפְתֹּ֡ר\rb* \rb must be under|תַּחַת֩\rb* \rb the first pair|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of branches,|הַקָּנִים֙\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֔נָּה\rb* \rb a bud|וְכַפְתֹּר֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the second pair,|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַקָּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb* \rb and a bud|וְכַפְתֹּ֕ר\rb* \rb under|תַּחַת־\rb* \rb the third pair.|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \v 36 \rb The buds|כַּפְתֹּרֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and branches|וּקְנֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֣נָּה\rb* \rb are to be|יִהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb of one piece with the lampstand,|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb hammered|מִקְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb out of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb lamps|נֵרֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and set them up|וְהֶֽעֱלָה֙\rb* \rb on the lampstand|אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they|נֵ֣רֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb illuminate|וְהֵאִ֖יר\rb* \rb the area|עֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb front of it.|פָּנֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 38 \rb The wick trimmers|וּמַלְקָחֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb and their trays|וּמַחְתֹּתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb must be of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \v 39 \rb The lampstand|אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb utensils|הַכֵּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb shall be made|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb from|אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb a talent|כִּכָּ֛ר\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb*\f + \fr 25:39 \fqa A talent\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref*.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f*
\p \v 40 \rb See to it that|וּרְאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb you make everything|וַעֲשֵׂ֑ה\rb* \rb according to the pattern|בְּתַ֨בְנִיתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb shown|מָרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb on the mountain.|בָּהָֽר׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 25:40 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 8:5|HEB 8:5\ref*\f*[’’]
\c 26
\s1 The Ten Curtains for the Tabernacle
\r \ref Exodus 36:8–13|EXO 36:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb “You are to construct|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb the tabernacle itself|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֥ן\rb* \rb with ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֗ר\rb* \rb linen,|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb each with blue,|וּתְכֵ֤לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָן֙\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb and cherubim|כְּרֻבִ֛ים\rb* \rb skillfully|חֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb worked|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb into them.|אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Each|הָֽאַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb shall be twenty-eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ׀\rb*\rb |הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb*\f + \fr 26:2 \ft Each of the ten curtains was \ref approximately 42|42\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (12.8 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f* — \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb curtains|הַיְרִיעֹֽת׃\rb* \rb the same|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb size.|מִדָּ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Five|חֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹ֗ת\rb* \rb are to be|תִּֽהְיֶ֙יןָ֙\rb* \rb joined|חֹֽבְרֹ֔ת\rb* \rb together,|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲחֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and the other five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |יְרִיעֹת֙\rb* \rb joined|חֹֽבְרֹ֔ת\rb* \rb as well.|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲחֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלְאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of blue material|תְּכֵ֗לֶת\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the end|מִקָּצָ֖ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָה֙\rb* \rb in the first|הָאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb set,|בַּחֹבָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb and do|תַּעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵ֤ן\rb*\rb |בִּשְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb for the end|הַקִּ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb set.|בַּמַּחְבֶּ֖רֶת\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂה֮\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלָאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on one|הָאֶחָת֒\rb* \rb curtain|בַּיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלָאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on the end|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑ית\rb* \rb set,|בַּמַּחְבֶּ֣רֶת\rb* \rb so that the loops|הַלֻּ֣לָאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb line up|מַקְבִּילֹת֙\rb* \rb opposite|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb one another.|אֲחֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֕יתָ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb clasps as well,|קַרְסֵ֣י\rb* \rb and join|וְחִבַּרְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹ֜ת\rb* \rb together|אִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲחֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb with the clasps,|בַּקְּרָסִ֔ים\rb* \rb so that the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a unit.|אֶחָֽד׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Eleven Curtains of Goat Hair
\r \ref Exodus 36:14–19|EXO 36:14-19\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb You are to make|וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of goat hair|עִזִּ֔ים\rb* \rb for the tent|לְאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle—|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb eleven|עַשְׁתֵּי־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb curtains in all.|יְרִיעֹ֖ת\rb* \v 8 \rb Each|הָֽאַחַ֗ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the eleven|לְעַשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹֽת׃\rb* \rb is to be the same|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb size—|מִדָּ֣ה\rb*  \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁים֙\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ׀\rb*\rb |הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide.|וְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb*\f + \fr 26:8 \ft Each of the eleven curtains was \ref approximately 45|45\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (13.7 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f*
\p \v 9 \rb Join|וְחִבַּרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb of the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹת֙\rb* \rb into one set|לְבָ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the other six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb into another.|הַיְרִיעֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |לְבָ֑ד\rb* \rb Then fold the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔ית\rb* \rb curtain over|הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb double|וְכָפַלְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|מ֖וּל\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tent.|הָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלָאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb along|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb end|הַקִּיצֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָה֙\rb* \rb in the first set,|בַּחֹבָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלָאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb along|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the corresponding curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb set.|הַחֹבֶ֖רֶת\rb* \v 11 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֛יתָ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֑ים\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb clasps|קַרְסֵ֥י\rb* \rb and put|וְהֵבֵאתָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הַקְּרָסִים֙\rb* \rb through the loops|בַּלֻּ֣לָאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to join|וְחִבַּרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb together|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb as a unit.|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb As for the overlap|וְסֶ֙רַח֙\rb* \rb that remains|הָעֹדֵ֔ף\rb* \rb of the tent|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb curtains,|בִּירִיעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb the half|חֲצִ֤י\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָה֙\rb* \rb that is left over|הָעֹדֶ֔פֶת\rb* \rb shall hang down|תִּסְרַ֕ח\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the back|אֲחֹרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And the tent|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb curtains will be|יְרִיעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb a cubit|וְהָאַמָּ֨ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:13 \fqa A cubit\ft is \ref approximately 18|18\ref* inches or 45.7 centimeters.\f* \rb longer|בְּאֹ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb on either side,|מִזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb and the excess|בָּעֹדֵ֔ף\rb* \rb will|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb hang|סָר֜וּחַ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the sides|צִדֵּ֧י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb to cover it.|לְכַסֹּתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Also make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb a covering|מִכְסֶה֙\rb* \rb for the tent|לָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb out of ram|אֵילִ֖ם\rb* \rb skins|עֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb dyed red,|מְאָדָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and over that|מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃פ\rb* \rb a covering|וּמִכְסֵ֛ה\rb*\rb |עֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of fine leather.|תְּחָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 26:14 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals\f*
\s1 The Frames and Bases
\r \ref Exodus 36:20–34|EXO 36:20-34\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb You are to construct|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb upright|עֹמְדִֽים׃\rb* \rb frames|הַקְּרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֖ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the tabernacle.|לַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 16 \rb Each frame|הַקָּ֑רֶשׁ\rb* \rb is to be ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb and a half|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide.|רֹ֖חַב\rb*\f + \fr 26:16 \ft Each frame was \ref approximately 15|15\ref* feet long and 2.25 feet wide (4.6 meters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f*\rb |הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb*\rb |הַקֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb* \v 17 \rb Two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb tenons|יָד֗וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 26:17 \ft That is, projecting pieces of wood made for insertion into another piece; similarly in verse 19.\f* \rb must be connected|מְשֻׁלָּבֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb each|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb other|אֲחֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb for each|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb frame.|לַקֶּ֙רֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the frames|קַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb* \rb in this way.|כֵּ֣ן\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Construct|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַקְּרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb frames|קֶ֔רֶשׁ\rb* \rb for the south|נֶ֥גְבָּה\rb*\rb |תֵימָֽנָה׃\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|לַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 19 \rb with|תַּעֲשֶׂ֕ה\rb* \rb forty|וְאַרְבָּעִים֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶ֔סֶף\rb* \rb bases|אַדְנֵי־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb frames—|הַקָּ֑רֶשׁ\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb bases|אֲדָנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb for each|הָאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb frame,|הַקֶּ֤רֶשׁ\rb* \rb one under each|לִשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb tenon.|יְדֹתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |לִשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |יְדֹתָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb For the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb side|וּלְצֶ֧לַע\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb side,|לִפְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb make twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb frames|קָֽרֶשׁ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb bases—|אַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb bases|אֲדָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb each|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb frame.|הַקֶּ֣רֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb for the rear|וּֽלְיַרְכְּתֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb the west side,|יָ֑מָּה\rb* \v 23 \rb and|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb for the two back|בַּיַּרְכָתָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb corners|לִמְקֻצְעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 24 \rb |וְיִֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb coupled|תֹֽאֲמִים֮\rb* \rb together|וְיַחְדָּ֗ו\rb*\rb |יִהְי֤וּ\rb*\rb |תַמִּים֙\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb bottom|מִלְּמַטָּה֒\rb* \rb to top|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and fitted into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a single|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb ring.|הַטַּבַּ֖עַת\rb*\rb |כֵּ֚ן\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb These|לִשְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will serve as|יִהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb the two|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb corners.|הַמִּקְצֹעֹ֖ת\rb* \v 25 \rb So there are to be|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and sixteen|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb bases—|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb frame.|הַקֶּ֣רֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֕ה\rb* \rb crossbars|בְרִיחִ֖ם\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the frames|לְקַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb on one|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb side|צֶֽלַע־\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \v 27 \rb five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְרִיחִ֔ם\rb* \rb for those|לְקַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb on the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֑ית\rb* \rb side,|צֶֽלַע־\rb*\rb |הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb and five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְרִיחִ֗ם\rb* \rb for those|לְקַרְשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb on the rear|לַיַּרְכָתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb side|צֶ֣לַע\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb to the west.|יָֽמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb The central|הַתִּיכֹ֖ן\rb* \rb crossbar|וְהַבְּרִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the frames|הַקְּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb shall extend|מַבְרִ֕חַ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb one end|הַקָּצֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the other.|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַקָּצֶֽה׃\rb* \v 29 \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb Overlay|תְּצַפֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb the frames|הַקְּרָשִׁ֞ים\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb to hold|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb the crossbars.|לַבְּרִיחִ֑ם\rb* \rb Also overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crossbars|הַבְּרִיחִ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb So you are to set up|וַהֲקֵמֹתָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \rb according to the pattern|כְּמִ֨שְׁפָּט֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb shown you|הָרְאֵ֖יתָ\rb* \rb on the mountain.|בָּהָֽר׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Veil
\r \ref Exodus 36:35–36|EXO 36:35-36\ref*)
\p \v 31 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb a veil|פָרֹ֗כֶת\rb* \rb of blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb* \rb linen,|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb with cherubim|כְּרֻבִֽים׃\rb* \rb skillfully|חֹשֵׁ֛ב\rb* \rb worked|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb into it.|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \v 32 \rb Hang|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb hooks|וָוֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָה֙\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of acacia wood,|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb overlaid|מְצֻפִּ֣ים\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb and standing on|עַל־\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb silver|כָֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb bases.|אַדְנֵי־\rb* \v 33 \rb And hang|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the veil|הַפָּרֹכֶת֮\rb* \rb from|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the clasps|הַקְּרָסִים֒\rb* \rb and place|וְהֵבֵאתָ֥\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵד֑וּת\rb*\f + \fr 26:33 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\ft ; also in verse 34\f*\rb |שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb behind|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb the veil.|לַפָּרֹ֔כֶת\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb So the veil|הַפָּרֹ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb will separate|וְהִבְדִּילָ֤ה\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb from the Most Holy Place.|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 26:33 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\ft ; also in verse 34\f*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb Put|וְנָתַתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֻ֑ת\rb* \rb in the Most Holy Place.|בְּקֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 35 \rb And place|וְשַׂמְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָן֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the veil|לַפָּרֹ֔כֶת\rb*\rb |וְהַ֨שֻּׁלְחָ֔ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the north|צָפֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb side|צֶ֥לַע\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb put|תִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb the lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָה֙\rb* \rb opposite|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb the table,|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֔ן\rb* \rb on|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb the south|תֵּימָ֑נָה\rb* \rb side.|צֶ֥לַע\rb*
\s1 The Curtain for the Entrance
\r \ref Exodus 36:37–38|EXO 36:37-38\ref*)
\p \v 36 \rb For the entrance|לְפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the tent,|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb you are to make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb a curtain|מָסָךְ֙\rb* \rb embroidered|רֹקֵֽם׃\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \v 37 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of acacia wood|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb for the curtain,|לַמָּסָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֤\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb hooks,|וָוֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb and cast|וְיָצַקְתָּ֣\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃ס\rb* \rb bases|אַדְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb for them.|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*[’’]
\c 27
\s1 The Bronze Altar
\r \ref Exodus 38:1–7|EXO 38:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “You are to build|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood.|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb The altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb must be|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb square,|רָב֤וּעַ\rb* \rb five|חָמֵשׁ֩\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb long,|אֹ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb five|וְחָמֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb wide,|רֹ֗חַב\rb* \rb and three|וְשָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 27:1 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 4.5 feet high (2.3 meters in length and width, and 1.4 meters high).\f* \v 2 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb a horn|קַרְנֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb on each of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb its four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb corners,|פִּנֹּתָ֔יו\rb* \rb so that the horns|קַרְנֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb are|תִּהְיֶ֣יןָ\rb* \rb of one piece,|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb and overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb it with bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלָ֖יו\rb* \rb of bronze—|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*  \rb its pots|סִּֽירֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb for removing ashes,|לְדַשְּׁנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb its shovels,|וְיָעָיו֙\rb* \rb its sprinkling bowls,|וּמִזְרְקֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb its meat forks,|וּמִזְלְגֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and its firepans.|וּמַחְתֹּתָ֑יו\rb* \v 4 \rb Construct|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb for it|לּוֹ֙\rb* \rb a grate|מִכְבָּ֔ר\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb mesh,|רֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb and make a|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb*\rb |אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb ring|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb at|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb each of the four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb corners|קְצוֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the mesh.|הָרֶ֗שֶׁת\rb* \v 5 \rb Set|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the grate|אֹתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb beneath|מִלְּמָ֑טָּה\rb*\rb |תַּ֛חַת\rb* \rb the ledge|כַּרְכֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb of the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb so that the mesh|הָרֶ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb comes|וְהָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb halfway|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb up|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Additionally, make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb poles|בַדִּים֙\rb*\rb |בַּדֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb and overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb The poles|בַּדָּ֖יו\rb* \rb are to be inserted|וְהוּבָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the rings|בַּטַּבָּעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb so that the poles|הַבַּדִּ֗ים\rb* \rb are|וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֛י\rb* \rb sides|צַלְעֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb when it is carried.|בִּשְׂאֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Construct|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the altar|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb with boards|לֻחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb so that it is hollow.|נְב֥וּב\rb* \rb It is to be made|יַעֲשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you were shown|הֶרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתְךָ֛\rb* \rb on the mountain.|בָּהָ֖ר\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*
\s1 The Courtyard
\r \ref Exodus 38:9–20|EXO 38:9-20\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֕יתָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb a courtyard|חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb for the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \rb On the south|נֶֽגֶב־\rb*\rb |תֵּ֠ימָנָה\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the courtyard|לֶחָצֵ֜ר\rb* \rb make curtains|קְלָעִ֨ים\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֗ר\rb* \rb linen,|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb cubits|בָֽאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 27:9 \fqa \ref 100|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 150|150\ref* feet or 45.7 meters; also in verse 11.\f* \rb on one|הָאֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb side,|לַפֵּאָ֖ה\rb* \v 10 \rb with twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb posts|וְעַמֻּדָ֣יו\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb bases,|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb hooks|וָוֵ֧י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on the posts.|הָעַמֻּדִ֛ים\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Likewise|וְכֵ֨ן\rb* \rb there are to be curtains|קְלָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the north|צָפוֹן֙\rb* \rb side,|לִפְאַ֤ת\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵ֣אָה\rb* \rb cubits|אֹ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb long,|בָּאֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb with twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֗ים\rb* \rb posts|וְעַמְדּוּ\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb bases,|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and with silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb hooks|וָוֵ֧י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on the posts.|הָֽעַמֻּדִ֛ים\rb* \v 12 \rb The curtains|קְלָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the west|יָ֔ם\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַת־\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb shall be fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb wide,|וְרֹ֤חַב\rb*\f + \fr 27:12 \fqa \ref 50|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref* feet or 22.9 meters; also in verse 13.\f* \rb with ten|עֲשָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמֻּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and ten|עֲשָׂרָֽה׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb The east|קֵ֥דְמָה\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the courtyard,|הֶֽחָצֵ֗ר\rb* \rb toward the sunrise,|מִזְרָ֖חָה\rb* \rb is to be fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide.|וְרֹ֣חַב\rb* \v 14 \rb Make the curtains|קְלָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb on one side|לַכָּתֵ֑ף\rb* \rb fifteen|וַחֲמֵ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits long,|אַמָּ֛ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:14 \fqa \ref 15|5\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 22|22\ref*.5 feet or 6.9 meters; also in verse 15.\f* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמֻּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb bases,|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 15 \rb and the curtains|קְלָעִ֑ים\rb* \rb on the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֔ית\rb* \rb side|וְלַכָּתֵף֙\rb* \rb fifteen cubits long,|חְמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמֻּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb The gate|וּלְשַׁ֨עַר\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵ֜ר\rb* \rb shall be twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits long,|אַמָּ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:16 \fqa \ref 20|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 30|30\ref* feet or 9.1 meters.\f* \rb with a curtain|מָסָ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb embroidered|רֹקֵ֑ם\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֨לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֜ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֧עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֛י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֖ר\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb It shall have four|אַרְבָּעָ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמֻּֽדֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבָּעָֽה׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the posts|עַמּוּדֵ֨י\rb* \rb around|סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵ֤ר\rb* \rb shall have silver bands,|מְחֻשָּׁקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb hooks,|וָוֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 18 \rb The entire|בַּחֲמִשִּׁ֗ים\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵר֩\rb* \rb shall be a hundred|מֵאָ֨ה\rb* \rb cubits|בָֽאַמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb and fifty cubits|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb wide,|וְרֹ֣חַב׀\rb*\f + \fr 27:18 \ft The courtyard was \ref approximately 150|150\ref* feet long and 75 feet wide (45.7 meters long and 22.9 meters wide).\f* \rb with curtains of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb* \rb linen|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high,|וְקֹמָ֛ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:18 \fqa 5 cubits\ft is \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet or 2.3 meters.\f* \rb and with bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 19 \rb All|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the utensils|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb for every|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb use,|עֲבֹדָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb including all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its tent pegs|יְתֵדֹתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the tent pegs|יִתְדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the courtyard,|הֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb* \rb shall be made of bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Oil for the Lamps
\r \ref Leviticus 24:1–4|LEV 24:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 20 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb are to command|תְּצַוֶּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to bring|וְיִקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb pure|זָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb of pressed|כָּתִ֖ית\rb* \rb olives|זַ֥יִת\rb* \rb for the light,|לַמָּא֑וֹר\rb* \rb to keep the lamps|נֵ֖ר\rb* \rb burning|לְהַעֲלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb continually.|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb In the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵד֩\rb* \rb outside|מִח֨וּץ\rb* \rb the veil|לַפָּרֹ֜כֶת\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in front of|עַל־\rb* \rb the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֗ת\rb*\f + \fr 27:21 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb are to tend|יַעֲרֹךְ֩\rb* \rb the lamps|אֹת֨וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb from evening|מֵעֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.|בֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb This is to be a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹ֣רֹתָ֔ם\rb*[’’]
\c 28
\s1 Garments for the Priests
\p \v 1 \rb “Next,|וְאַתָּ֡ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have your brother|אָחִ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb brought|הַקְרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֛וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb along with|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*\rb |אַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Nadab,|נָדָ֧ב\rb* \rb Abihu,|וַאֲבִיה֛וּא\rb* \rb Eleazar,|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb and Ithamar,|וְאִיתָמָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אַהֲרֹ֕ן\rb* \rb to serve Me as priests.|לְכַהֲנוֹ־\rb* \v 2 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb garments|בִגְדֵי־\rb* \rb for your brother|אָחִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Aaron,|לְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb to give him glory|לְכָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb and splendor.|וּלְתִפְאָֽרֶת׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb You|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb are to instruct|תְּדַבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the skilled craftsmen,|חַכְמֵי־\rb*\rb |לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have filled|מִלֵּאתִ֖יו\rb* \rb with a spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of wisdom,|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb to make|וְעָשׂ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֧י\rb* \rb for Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb consecration,|לְקַדְּשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb so that he may serve Me as priest.|לְכַהֲנוֹ־\rb*\rb |לִֽי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb These|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb are the garments|הַבְּגָדִ֜ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they shall make:|יַעֲשׂ֗וּ\rb* \rb a breastpiece,|חֹ֤שֶׁן\rb* \rb an ephod,|וְאֵפוֹד֙\rb* \rb a robe,|וּמְעִ֔יל\rb* \rb a woven|תַּשְׁבֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb tunic,|וּכְתֹ֥נֶת\rb* \rb a turban,|מִצְנֶ֣פֶת\rb* \rb and a sash.|וְאַבְנֵ֑ט\rb* \rb They are to make|וְעָשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb these holy|קֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb garments|בִגְדֵי־\rb* \rb for your brother|אָחִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb and his sons,|וּלְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb so that they may serve Me as priests.|לְכַהֲנוֹ־\rb* \v 5 \rb They|וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb shall use|יִקְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gold,|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb blue,|הַתְּכֵ֖לֶת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb purple,|הָֽאַרְגָּמָ֑ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|תּוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and fine linen.|הַשֵּֽׁשׁ׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Ephod
\r \ref Exodus 39:1–7|EXO 39:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 6 \rb They are to make|וְעָשׂ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֑ד\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֖ר\rb* \rb linen|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb embroidered|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |חֹשֵֽׁב׃\rb* \rb with gold,|זָ֠הָב\rb* \rb and with blue,|תְּכֵ֨לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֜ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn.|תּוֹלַ֧עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֛י\rb* \v 7 \rb It shall have|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֧י\rb* \rb shoulder pieces|כְתֵפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb attached|חֹֽבְרֹ֗ת\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of its corners,|קְצוֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb so it can be fastened.|וְחֻבָּֽר׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And the skillfully woven waistband|וְחֵ֤שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb the ephod|אֲפֻדָּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb must be|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb of one piece,|מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb of the same workmanship—|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֖הוּ\rb*  \rb with gold,|זָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and with finely spun|מָשְׁזָֽר׃\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Take|וְלָ֣קַחְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb onyx|שֹׁ֑הַם\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵי־\rb* \rb and engrave|וּפִתַּחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb six|שִׁשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb of their names|מִשְּׁמֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb stone|הָאֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb and the remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb six|הַשִּׁשָּׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֞וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the other,|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb*\rb |הָאֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb in the order of their birth.|כְּתוֹלְדֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb Engrave|תְּפַתַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb on the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb the way a gem|אֶבֶן֒\rb* \rb cutter|חָרַשׁ֮\rb* \rb engraves|פִּתּוּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb a seal.|חֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb Then mount|מֻסַבֹּ֛ת\rb* \rb the stones|אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb in gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb filigree settings.|מִשְׁבְּצ֥וֹת\rb* \v 12 \rb Fasten|וְשַׂמְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the shoulder pieces|כִּתְפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָֽאֵפֹ֔ד\rb* \rb as memorial|זִכָּרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the sons|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to bear|וְנָשָׂא֩\rb* \rb their names|שְׁמוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb shoulders|כְתֵפָ֖יו\rb* \rb as a memorial|לְזִכָּרֹֽן׃ס\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Fashion|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \rb filigree settings|מִשְׁבְּצֹ֖ת\rb* \v 14 \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb chains|שַׁרְשְׁרֹת֙\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֔וֹר\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb made|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of braided|מִגְבָּלֹ֛ת\rb* \rb cord|עֲבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb work;|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and attach|וְנָתַתָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָעֲבֹתֹ֖ת\rb* \rb chains|שַׁרְשְׁרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the settings.|הַֽמִּשְׁבְּצֹֽת׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Breastpiece
\r \ref Exodus 39:8–21|EXO 39:8-21\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb a breastpiece|חֹ֤שֶׁן\rb* \rb of judgment|מִשְׁפָּט֙\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb with the same workmanship|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |חֹשֵׁ֔ב\rb*\rb |כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb as the ephod.|אֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb Construct|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb it|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb with gold,|זָ֠הָב\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֨לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֜ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֧עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֛י\rb* \rb and with finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֖ר\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \v 16 \rb It must be|יִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb square|רָב֥וּעַ\rb* \rb when folded over double,|כָּפ֑וּל\rb* \rb a span|זֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and a span|וְזֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb wide.|רָחְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 28:16 \ft The breastpiece, when folded over, was \ref approximately 9|9\ref* inches or 22.9 centimeters in both length and width.\f*
\p \v 17 \rb And mount|וּמִלֵּאתָ֥\rb* \rb on it|בוֹ֙\rb* \rb a setting|מִלֻּ֣אַת\rb* \rb of gemstones,|אֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of stones:|אָ֑בֶן\rb*\f + \fr 28:17 \ft The precise identification of some of these gemstones is uncertain.\f*
\li1 \rb In the first|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb row there shall be|ט֗וּר\rb*\rb |הַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a ruby,|אֹ֤דֶם\rb* \rb a topaz,|פִּטְדָה֙\rb* \rb and an emerald;|וּבָרֶ֔קֶת\rb*
\li1 \v 18 \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb row|וְהַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a turquoise,|נֹ֥פֶךְ\rb* \rb a sapphire,|סַפִּ֖יר\rb* \rb and a diamond;|וְיָהֲלֹֽם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 19 \rb in the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb row|וְהַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a jacinth,|לֶ֥שֶׁם\rb* \rb an agate,|שְׁב֖וֹ\rb* \rb and an amethyst;|וְאַחְלָֽמָה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 20 \rb and in the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb row|וְהַטּוּר֙\rb* \rb a beryl,|תַּרְשִׁ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb an onyx,|וְשֹׁ֖הַם\rb* \rb and a jasper.|וְיָשְׁפֵ֑ה\rb*\rb |מְשֻׁבָּצִ֥ים\rb*
\p \rb Mount these stones|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb in gold|זָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb filigree settings.|בְּמִלּוּאֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb The twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb stones|וְ֠הָאֲבָנִים\rb* \rb are|תִּֽהְיֶ֜יןָ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb correspond to the names|שְׁמֹ֧ת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |תִּֽהְיֶ֕יןָ\rb* \rb engraved|פִּתּוּחֵ֤י\rb* \rb like a seal|חוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the name|שְׁמֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of one of the twelve|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb tribes.|שָֽׁבֶט׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb For the breastpiece,|הַחֹ֛שֶׁן\rb*\rb |שַֽׁרְשֹׁ֥ת\rb* \rb make|וְעָשִׂ֧יתָ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb braided chains|גַּבְלֻ֖ת\rb*\rb |עֲבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb like cords|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \v 23 \rb You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הַחֹ֔שֶׁן\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb and fasten|וְנָתַתָּ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb*\rb |הַטַּבָּע֔וֹת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb corners|קְצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece.|הַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb* \v 24 \rb Then fasten|וְנָתַתָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb chains|עֲבֹתֹ֣ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb gold rings|הַטַּבָּעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the corners|קְצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece,|הַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb* \v 25 \rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb and fasten|תִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb the other|שְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb ends|קְצוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb chains|הָעֲבֹתֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb filigree settings,|הַֽמִּשְׁבְּצ֑וֹת\rb* \rb attaching them|וְנָתַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the shoulder pieces|כִּתְפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front.|מ֥וּל\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֗יתָ\rb* \rb two more|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb and attach|וְשַׂמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the other two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb corners|קְצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece,|הַחֹ֑שֶׁן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the inside|בָּֽיְתָה׃\rb* \rb edge|שְׂפָת֕וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb next to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ephod.|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂיתָ֮\rb* \rb two additional|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb gold|זָהָב֒\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb and attach|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֡ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the bottom|מִלְּמַ֙טָּה֙\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁתֵּי֩\rb* \rb shoulder pieces|כִתְפ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the ephod,|הָאֵפ֤וֹד\rb* \rb on its front,|מִמּ֣וּל\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb near|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb its seam|מֶחְבַּרְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb just above|מִמַּ֕עַל\rb* \rb its woven waistband.|לְחֵ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |הָאֵפֽוֹד׃\rb* \v 28 \rb The rings|מִטַּבְּעֹתוֹ\rb* \rb of the breastpiece|הַ֠חֹשֶׁן\rb* \rb shall be tied|וְיִרְכְּס֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the rings|טַבְּעֹ֤ת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹד֙\rb* \rb with a cord|בִּפְתִ֣יל\rb* \rb of blue yarn,|תְּכֵ֔לֶת\rb* \rb so that the breastpiece|הַחֹ֔שֶׁן\rb* \rb is|לִֽהְי֖וֹת\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the waistband|חֵ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפ֑וֹד\rb* \rb and does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb swing out|יִזַּ֣ח\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the ephod.|הָאֵפֽוֹד׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Whenever Aaron enters|בְּבֹא֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Holy Place,|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb he|אַ֠הֲרֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall bear|וְנָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb on the breastpiece|בְּחֹ֧שֶׁן\rb* \rb of judgment,|הַמִּשְׁפָּ֛ט\rb* \rb as a continual|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb reminder|לְזִכָּרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb And place|וְנָתַתָּ֞\rb* \rb the Urim|הָאוּרִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Thummim|הַתֻּמִּ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 28:30 \ft Literally \fqa Lights and Perfections\f* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the breastpiece|חֹ֣שֶׁן\rb* \rb of judgment,|הַמִּשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they will also be|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb whenever he comes|בְּבֹא֖וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Aaron|אַ֠הֲרֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will continually|תָּמִֽיד׃ס\rb* \rb carry|וְנָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb the judgment|מִשְׁפַּ֨ט\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\s1 Additional Priestly Garments
\r \ref Exodus 39:22–31|EXO 39:22-31\ref*)
\p \v 31 \rb You are to make|וְעָשִׂ֛יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|מְעִ֥יל\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb entirely|כְּלִ֥יל\rb* \rb of blue cloth,|תְּכֵֽלֶת׃\rb* \v 32 \rb with|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb an opening|פִֽי־\rb* \rb at its top|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the center.|בְּתוֹכ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Around the opening|סָבִ֜יב\rb* \rb shall be|יִֽהְיֶה֩\rb* \rb a woven|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹרֵ֗ג\rb* \rb collar|שָׂפָ֡ה\rb* \rb with an opening|לְפִ֨יו\rb* \rb like that|כְּפִ֥י\rb* \rb of a garment,|תַחְרָ֛א\rb*\f + \fr 28:32 \ft The meaning of the Hebrew word is uncertain; possibly \fqa a coat of mail\ft .\f* \rb so that|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb it|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb tear.|יִקָּרֵֽעַ׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb pomegranates|רִמֹּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of blue,|תְּכֵ֤לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָן֙\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn|וְתוֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |שׁוּלָ֖יו\rb* \rb all the way around the lower|סָבִ֑יב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb hem,|שׁוּלָ֗יו\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb bells|וּפַעֲמֹנֵ֥י\rb* \rb between|בְּתוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb them,|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 34 \rb alternating|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb bells|פַּעֲמֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and pomegranates|וְרִמּ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |פַּֽעֲמֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |זָהָ֖ב\rb*\rb |וְרִמּ֑וֹן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb around the lower hem|שׁוּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the robe.|הַמְּעִ֖יל\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb must wear the robe|עַֽל־\rb* \rb whenever he ministers,|לְשָׁרֵ֑ת\rb* \rb and its sound|ק֠וֹלוֹ\rb* \rb will be heard|וְנִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb when he enters|בְּבֹא֨וֹ\rb* \rb or exits|וּבְצֵאת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb so that he will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die.|יָמֽוּת׃ס\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb You are to make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a plate|צִּ֖יץ\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and engrave|וּפִתַּחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb as|פִּתּוּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb on a seal:|חֹתָ֔ם\rb*
\pc \rb HOLY|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb TO THE LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 28:36 \ft That is, \fqa the LORD\f*
\p \v 37 \rb Fasten|וְשַׂמְתָּ֤\rb* \rb to it|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb a blue|תְּכֵ֔לֶת\rb* \rb cord|פְּתִ֣יל\rb* \rb to mount it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the turban;|הַמִּצְנָ֑פֶת\rb* \rb it shall be|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|מ֥וּל\rb*\rb |פְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the turban.|הַמִּצְנֶ֖פֶת\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \v 38 \rb And it will be worn|וְהָיָה֮\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֒\rb* \rb forehead,|מֵ֣צַח\rb* \rb so that he|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb may bear|וְנָשָׂ֨א\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of the holy things|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb consecrate|יַקְדִּ֙ישׁוּ֙\rb* \rb with regard to all|לְכָֽל־\rb* \rb their holy|קָדְשֵׁיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb gifts.|מַתְּנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb It shall always|תָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his forehead,|מִצְחוֹ֙\rb* \rb so that they may be acceptable|לְרָצ֥וֹן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb You are to weave|וְשִׁבַּצְתָּ֙\rb* \rb the tunic|הַכְּתֹ֣נֶת\rb* \rb with fine linen,|שֵׁ֔שׁ\rb* \rb make|וְעָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb the turban|מִצְנֶ֣פֶת\rb* \rb of fine linen,|שֵׁ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and fashion|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb an embroidered|רֹקֵֽם׃\rb* \rb sash.|וְאַבְנֵ֥ט\rb* \v 40 \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb tunics,|כֻתֳּנֹ֔ת\rb* \rb sashes,|אַבְנֵטִ֑ים\rb* \rb and headbands|וּמִגְבָּעוֹת֙\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb sons,|וְלִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb to give|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb glory|לְכָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb and splendor.|וּלְתִפְאָֽרֶת׃\rb*
\p \v 41 \rb After you put|וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ֤\rb* \rb these garments|אֹתָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on your brother|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and his sons,|בָּנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb anoint|וּמָשַׁחְתָּ֨\rb* \rb them,|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb ordain|וּמִלֵּאתָ֧\rb* \rb them,|אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb and consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb so that they may serve Me as priests.|וְכִהֲנ֥וּ\rb*
\p \v 42 \rb Make|וַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb linen|בָ֔ד\rb* \rb undergarments|מִכְנְסֵי־\rb* \rb to cover|לְכַסּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb bare|עֶרְוָ֑ה\rb* \rb flesh,|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb extending|יִהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb from waist|מִמָּתְנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb thigh.|יְרֵכַ֖יִם\rb* \v 43 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֜יו\rb* \rb must wear them|וְהָיוּ֩\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb whenever they enter|בְּבֹאָ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֗ד\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb approach|בְגִשְׁתָּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb in the Holy Place,|בַּקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb so that they will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb incur|יִשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb guilt|עָוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb and die.|וָמֵ֑תוּ\rb* \rb This is to be a permanent|עוֹלָ֛ם\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for Aaron|אַחֲרָֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb and his descendants.|וּלְזַרְע֥וֹ\rb*[’’]
\c 29
\s1 Consecration of the Priests
\r \ref Leviticus 8:1–13|LEV 8:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “Now this|וְזֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֜ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb you are to do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to consecrate|לְקַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Aaron and his sons|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to serve Me as priests:|לְכַהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Take|לְ֠קַח\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֧ד\rb* \rb young|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֛ר\rb* \rb bull|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb and two|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb rams|וְאֵילִ֥ם\rb* \rb without blemish,|תְּמִימִֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb along with unleavened|מַצּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb bread,|וְלֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb unleavened|מַצֹּת֙\rb* \rb cakes|וְחַלֹּ֤ת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with oil,|בַּשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb* \rb and unleavened|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb wafers|וּרְקִיקֵ֥י\rb* \rb anointed|מְשֻׁחִ֣ים\rb* \rb with oil.|בַּשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb Make|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb out of fine wheat|חִטִּ֖ים\rb* \rb flour,|סֹ֥לֶת\rb* \v 3 \rb put|וְנָתַתָּ֤\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb basket,|סַ֣ל\rb* \rb and present|וְהִקְרַבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the basket,|בַּסָּ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb along with the bull|הַפָּ֔ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb rams.|הָאֵילִֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb present|תַּקְרִ֔יב\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb and wash|וְרָחַצְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with water.|בַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the garments|הַבְּגָדִ֗ים\rb* \rb and clothe|וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the tunic,|הַכֻּתֹּ֔נֶת\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the robe|מְעִ֣יל\rb* \rb of the ephod,|הָאֵפֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the ephod itself,|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the breastplate.|הַחֹ֑שֶׁן\rb* \rb Fasten|וְאָפַדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֹֽד׃\rb* \rb on him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb with its woven waistband.|בְּחֵ֖שֶׁב\rb* \v 6 \rb Put|וְשַׂמְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the turban|הַמִּצְנֶ֖פֶת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and attach|וְנָתַתָּ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb diadem|נֵ֥זֶר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the turban.|הַמִּצְנָֽפֶת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then take|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and anoint him|וּמָשַׁחְתָּ֖\rb* \rb by pouring|וְיָצַקְתָּ֖\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head.|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Present|תַּקְרִ֑יב\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb as well|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and clothe them|וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb with tunics.|כֻּתֳּנֹֽת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Wrap|וְחָגַרְתָּ֩\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֨ם\rb* \rb the sashes|אַבְנֵ֜ט\rb* \rb around Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb and tie|וְחָבַשְׁתָּ֤\rb* \rb headbands|מִגְבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb on them.|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb The priesthood|כְּהֻנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb theirs|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb by a permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb statute.|לְחֻקַּ֣ת\rb* \rb In this way you are to ordain|וּמִלֵּאתָ֥\rb*\rb |יַֽד־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְיַד־\rb* \rb and his sons.|בָּנָֽיו׃\rb*
\s1 The Order of the Sacrifices
\r \ref Leviticus 8:22–36|LEV 8:22-36\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb You are to present|וְהִקְרַבְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb at the front|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to lay|וְסָמַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its|הַפָּֽר׃\rb* \rb head.|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \v 11 \rb And you shall slaughter|וְשָׁחַטְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Take some|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֙\rb* \rb of the blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb of the bull|הַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and put|וְנָתַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb with your finger;|בְּאֶצְבָּעֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb then pour out|תִּשְׁפֹּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the blood|הַדָּ֣ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Take|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֗\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵלֶב֮\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּרֶב֒\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver,|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֖לֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb and burn them|וְהִקְטַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb on the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb burn|תִּשְׂרֹ֣ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of the bull|הַפָּר֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its hide|עֹר֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and dung|פִּרְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp;|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb it is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb a sin offering.|חַטָּ֖את\rb*\f + \fr 29:14 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\ft ; also in verse 36\f*
\p \v 15 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Take|תִּקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb of the rams,|הָאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall lay|וְסָ֨מְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its|הָאָֽיִל׃\rb* \rb head.|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \v 16 \rb You are to slaughter|וְשָׁחַטְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ram,|הָאָ֑יִל\rb* \rb take|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its blood,|דָּמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and splatter|וְזָרַקְתָּ֥\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \v 17 \rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb Cut|תְּנַתֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb into pieces,|לִנְתָחָ֑יו\rb* \rb wash|וְרָחַצְתָּ֤\rb* \rb the entrails|קִרְבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and legs,|וּכְרָעָ֔יו\rb* \rb and place them|וְנָתַתָּ֥\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb and other pieces.|נְתָחָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \v 18 \rb Then burn|וְהִקְטַרְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb ram|הָאַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb on the altar;|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|עֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיח֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb aroma,|רֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Take|וְלָ֣קַחְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb ram,|הָאַ֣יִל\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to lay|וְסָמַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its|הָאָֽיִל׃\rb* \rb head.|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \v 20 \rb Slaughter|וְשָׁחַטְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ram,|הָאַ֗יִל\rb* \rb take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb some of its blood,|מִדָּמוֹ֙\rb* \rb and put|וְנָֽתַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the right earlobes|תְּנוּךְ֩\rb*\rb |אֹ֨זֶן\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his sons,|בָּנָיו֙\rb*\rb |הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb*\rb |תְּנ֨וּךְ\rb*\rb |אֹ֤זֶן\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the thumbs|בֹּ֤הֶן\rb* \rb of their right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb hands,|יָדָם֙\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the big toes|בֹּ֥הֶן\rb* \rb of their right|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb feet.|רַגְלָ֖ם\rb* \rb Splatter|וְזָרַקְתָּ֧\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the remaining blood|הַדָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \v 21 \rb And take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֞\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּחַ֮\rb* \rb and some of the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָה֒\rb* \rb oil|וּמִשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזֵּיתָ֤\rb* \rb it on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb and his garments,|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb as well as on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and their garments.|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb Then he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb and his garments|וּבְגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb will be consecrated,|וְקָדַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb as well as his sons|בָנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and their|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb garments.|וּבִגְדֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בָנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֨לֶב\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ram,|הָ֠אַיִל\rb* \rb the fat tail,|וְהָֽאַלְיָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֣לֶב׀\rb* \rb covering|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails,|הַקֶּ֗רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the lobe|יֹתֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb of the liver,|הַכָּבֵד֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֗ת\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them,|עֲלֵהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the right|הַיָּמִ֑ין\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb (since|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb this|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is a ram|אֵ֥יל\rb* \rb for ordination),|מִלֻּאִ֖ים\rb* \v 23 \rb along with one|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb loaf|וְכִכַּ֨ר\rb* \rb of bread,|לֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb cake|וַֽחַלַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb made with oil,|שֶׁ֛מֶן\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb wafer|וְרָקִ֣יק\rb* \rb from the basket|מִסַּל֙\rb* \rb of unleavened bread|הַמַּצּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 24 \rb Put|וְשַׂמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb all these|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the hands|כַּפֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |כַּפֵּ֣י\rb* \rb and his sons|בָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and wave|וְהֵנַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb as a wave offering.|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \v 25 \rb Then take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָ֔ם\rb* \rb and burn them|וְהִקְטַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חָה\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיח֙וֹחַ֙\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֤יחַ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the breast|הֶֽחָזֶ֗ה\rb* \rb of the ram|מֵאֵ֤יל\rb* \rb of Aaron’s|לְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb ordination|הַמִּלֻּאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and wave|וְהֵנַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb it|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as a wave offering,|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb and it will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb portion.|לְמָנָֽה׃\rb* \v 27 \rb Consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb for Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וּמֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and his sons|לְבָנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb the breast|חֲזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is waved|הוּנַ֖ף\rb* \rb and the thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb of the heave offering|הַתְּרוּמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is lifted up|הוּרָ֑ם\rb* \rb from the ram|מֵאֵיל֙\rb* \rb of ordination.|הַמִּלֻּאִ֔ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \v 28 \rb This will belong to|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֜יו\rb* \rb as a regular|עוֹלָ֗ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb portion|לְחָק־\rb* \rb from the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is the heave offering|תְרוּמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb will make|וּתְרוּמָ֞ה\rb*\rb |תְּרוּמָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb from their peace offerings.|שַׁלְמֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |מִזִּבְחֵ֣י\rb*
