\s1 Food for the Priests
\p \v 31 \rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb You are to take|תִּקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb the ram|אֵ֥יל\rb* \rb of ordination|הַמִּלֻּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb and boil|וּבִשַּׁלְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its flesh|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \rb in a holy|קָדֹֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb place.|בְּמָקֹ֥ם\rb* \v 32 \rb At the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to eat|וְאָכַ֨ל\rb* \rb the meat|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the bread|הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the basket.|בַּסָּ֑ל\rb* \v 33 \rb They must eat|וְאָכְל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb those things by which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb atonement was made|כֻּפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb for their ordination|לְמַלֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and consecration.|לְקַדֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb But no|לֹא־\rb* \rb outsider|וְזָ֥ר\rb* \rb may eat them,|יֹאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb these|הֵֽם׃\rb* \rb things are sacred.|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \v 34 \rb And if|וְֽאִם־\rb* \rb any of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the meat|מִבְּשַׂ֧ר\rb* \rb of ordination|הַמִּלֻּאִ֛ים\rb* \rb or any bread|הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb is left|יִוָּתֵ֞ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the morning,|הַבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb you are to burn up|וְשָׂרַפְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the remainder.|הַנּוֹתָר֙\rb* \rb It must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be eaten,|יֵאָכֵ֖ל\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb it|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is sacred.|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb This is what|כָּ֔כָה\rb* \rb you are to do|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb for Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָיו֙\rb* \rb based on all|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb you,|אֹתָ֑כָה\rb* \rb taking seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb to ordain|תְּמַלֵּ֥א\rb* \rb them.|יָדָֽם׃\rb* \v 36 \rb Sacrifice|תַּעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb a bull|וּפַ֨ר\rb* \rb as a sin offering|חַטָּ֜את\rb* \rb each day|לַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb atonement.|הַכִּפֻּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb Purify|וְחִטֵּאתָ֙\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb by making atonement|בְּכַפֶּרְךָ֖\rb*\rb |עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb for it,|עַל־\rb* \rb and anoint|וּמָֽשַׁחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to consecrate it.|לְקַדְּשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb you shall make atonement|תְּכַפֵּר֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb and consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֖\rb* \rb it.|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb Then the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb most holy;|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָֽדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb whatever|כָּל־\rb* \rb touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb the altar|בַּמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb will be holy.|יִקְדָּֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Daily Offerings
\r \ref Numbers 28:1–8|NUM 28:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 38 \rb This|וְזֶ֕ה\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to offer|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb regularly|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb each day:|לַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֧ים\rb* \rb that are a year old.|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \v 39 \rb Offer|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb lamb|הַכֶּ֥בֶשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the morning|בַבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*\rb |הַכֶּ֣בֶשׂ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb twilight.|הָעַרְבָּֽיִם׃\rb*\f + \fr 29:39 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings\ft ; also in verse 41\f* \v 40 \rb With the first|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb lamb|לַכֶּ֖בֶשׂ\rb* \rb offer a tenth of an ephah|וְעִשָּׂרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb of fine flour,|סֹ֜לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 29:40 \fqa A tenth of an ephah\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb mixed|בָּל֨וּל\rb* \rb with a quarter|רֶ֣בַע\rb* \rb hin|הַהִ֔ין\rb* \rb of oil|בְּשֶׁ֤מֶן\rb* \rb from pressed olives,|כָּתִית֙\rb*\f + \fr 29:40 \ft Hebrew \fqa a quarter hin of pressed oil\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.97 quarts or 0.92 liters\f* \rb and a drink offering|וְנֵ֕סֶךְ\rb* \rb of a quarter|רְבִעִ֥ית\rb* \rb hin|הַהִ֖ין\rb* \rb of wine.|יָ֑יִן\rb* \v 41 \rb And|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb offer|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb lamb|הַכֶּ֣בֶשׂ\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָעַרְבָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb with|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb the same|לָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb grain offering|כְּמִנְחַ֨ת\rb* \rb and drink offering|וּכְנִסְכָּהּ֙\rb* \rb as in the morning,|הַבֹּ֤קֶר\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb aroma,|לְרֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 42 \rb For the generations to come,|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this burnt offering|עֹלַ֤ת\rb* \rb shall be made regularly|תָּמִיד֙\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I will meet|אִוָּעֵ֤ד\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you.|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 43 \rb I will also meet|וְנֹעַדְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb with the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and that place will be consecrated|וְנִקְדַּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb by My glory.|בִּכְבֹדִֽי׃\rb* \v 44 \rb So I will consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and I will consecrate|אֲקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb to serve Me as priests.|לְכַהֵ֥ן\rb*
\s1 God Will Dwell among the People
\p \v 45 \rb Then I will dwell|וְשָׁ֣כַנְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and be|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God.|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \v 46 \rb And they will know|וְיָדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb their God,|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought them out|הוֹצֵ֧אתִי\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb so that I might dwell|לְשָׁכְנִ֣י\rb* \rb among them.|בְתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb their God.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*[’’]
\c 30
\s1 The Altar of Incense
\r \ref Exodus 37:25–29|EXO 37:25-29\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “You are also to make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֖ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the burning|מִקְטַ֣ר\rb* \rb of incense.|קְטֹ֑רֶת\rb* \v 2 \rb It is to be|יִהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb square,|רָב֣וּעַ\rb* \rb a cubit|אַמָּ֨ה\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֤ה\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and two cubits|וְאַמָּתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָת֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 30:2 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 3 feet high (45.7 centimeters in length and width, and 91.4 centimeters high).\f* \rb Its horns|קַרְנֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb must be of one piece.|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \v 3 \rb Overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֨\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb with pure|טָה֗וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb the top|גַּגּ֧וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|סָבִ֖יב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the sides|קִירֹתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and horns,|קַרְנֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 4 \rb And make|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb*\rb |לּ֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּי֩\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֜ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֨ת\rb* \rb below|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the molding|לְזֵר֗וֹ\rb*\rb |עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |צַלְעֹתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb opposite sides|צִדָּ֑יו\rb* \rb to|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb hold|לְבָתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb the poles|לְבַדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb used to carry it.|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בָּהֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlay|וְצִפִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Place|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the altar|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the veil|הַפָּרֹ֔כֶת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is before|עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֻ֑ת\rb*\f + \fr 30:6 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\ft ; also in verse 26\f*— \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֗רֶת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb is over|עַל־\rb* \rb the Testimony—|הָ֣עֵדֻ֔ת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I will meet|אִוָּעֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with you.|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb is to burn|וְהִקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb fragrant|סַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֣רֶת\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֛יו\rb*\rb |יַקְטִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb every morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb when he tends|בְּהֵיטִיב֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lamps.|הַנֵּרֹ֖ת\rb* \v 8 \rb When Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sets up|וּבְהַעֲלֹ֨ת\rb* \rb the lamps|הַנֵּרֹ֛ת\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb twilight,|הָעֲרְבַּ֖יִם\rb*\f + \fr 30:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings\f* \rb he must burn|יַקְטִירֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb the incense|קְטֹ֧רֶת\rb* \rb perpetually|תָּמִ֛יד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb On this altar|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb offer|תַעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb unauthorized|זָרָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 30:9 \ft Or \fqa strange\f* \rb incense|קְטֹ֥רֶת\rb* \rb or a burnt offering|וְעֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb or grain offering;|וּמִנְחָ֑ה\rb* \rb nor are you|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to pour|תִסְּכ֖וּ\rb* \rb a drink offering|וְנֵ֕סֶךְ\rb* \rb on it.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Once|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb shall make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns of the altar.|קַרְנֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb Throughout your generations|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb he shall make atonement|יְכַפֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb annually|אַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |בַּשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb with the blood|מִדַּ֞ם\rb* \rb of the sin offering|חַטַּ֣את\rb*\f + \fr 30:10 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\f* \rb of atonement.|הַכִּפֻּרִ֗ים\rb* \rb The altar is|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb most|קֹֽדֶשׁ־\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Census Offering
\r \ref 2 Samuel 24:1–9|2SA 24:1-9\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 21:1–6|1CH 21:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb “When|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you take a census|תִשָּׂ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb to number them,|לִפְקֻדֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb must pay|וְנָ֨תְנ֜וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb a ransom|כֹּ֧פֶר\rb* \rb for his life|נַפְשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb when he is counted.|בִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb plague|נֶ֖גֶף\rb* \rb will come|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb upon them|בָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb when they are numbered.|בִּפְקֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb |זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who crosses|הָעֹבֵר֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb to those counted|הַפְּקֻדִ֔ים\rb* \rb must pay|יִתְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb a half|מַחֲצִ֥ית\rb* \rb shekel,|הַשֶּׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 30:13 \fqa A half shekel\ft is \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.2 ounces or 5.7 grams; also in verse 15.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb which weighs|הַשֶּׁ֔קֶל\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb gerahs.|גֵּרָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 30:13 \fqa \ref 20|0\ref* gerahs\ft is equivalent to one shekel \ref (approximately 0|0\ref*.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f* \rb This half|מַחֲצִ֣ית\rb* \rb shekel|הַשֶּׁ֔קֶל\rb* \rb is an offering|תְּרוּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Everyone|כֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb twenty years|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb who crosses|הָעֹבֵר֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |הַפְּקֻדִ֔ים\rb* \rb must give|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb this offering|תְּרוּמַ֥ת\rb* \rb to the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 15 \rb In making|לָתֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to atone|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your lives,|נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb the rich|הֶֽעָשִׁ֣יר\rb* \rb shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb give more|יַרְבֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb than a half|מִֽמַּחֲצִ֖ית\rb* \rb shekel,|הַשָּׁ֑קֶל\rb* \rb nor shall|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the poor|וְהַדַּל֙\rb* \rb give less.|יַמְעִ֔יט\rb* \v 16 \rb Take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the atonement|הַכִּפֻּרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb from the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and use|וְנָתַתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb it for|עַל־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb It will serve as|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb a memorial|לְזִכָּרוֹן֙\rb* \rb for the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your lives.”|נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Bronze Basin
\r \ref Exodus 38:8|EXO 38:8\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 18 \rb “You are to make|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹ֛שֶׁת\rb* \rb basin|כִּיּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb with a bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb stand|וְכַנּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb for washing.|לְרָחְצָ֑ה\rb* \rb Set|וְנָתַתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb it between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵד֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb and put|וְנָתַתָּ֥\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb in it,|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \v 19 \rb with which|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb are to wash|וְרָחֲצ֛וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and feet.|רַגְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 20 \rb Whenever they enter|בְּבֹאָ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֧הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֛ד\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb approach|בְגִשְׁתָּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֔ת\rb* \rb by presenting|לְהַקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb they must wash|יִרְחֲצוּ־\rb* \rb with water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb so that they will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die.|יָמֻ֑תוּ\rb* \v 21 \rb Thus they are to wash|וְרָחֲצ֛וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and feet|וְרַגְלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb so that they will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die;|יָמֻ֑תוּ\rb* \rb this shall be|וְהָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb a permanent|עוֹלָ֛ם\rb* \rb statute|חָק־\rb* \rb for Aaron and his descendants|וּלְזַרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb for the generations to come.”|לְדֹרֹתָֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Anointing Oil
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 23 \rb |וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb “Take|קַח־\rb* \rb the finest|רֹאשׁ֒\rb* \rb spices:|בְּשָׂמִ֣ים\rb* \rb 500 shekels|חֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb of liquid|דְּרוֹר֙\rb* \rb myrrh,|מָר־\rb*\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 500|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 12|12\ref*.6 pounds or 5.7 kilograms of myrrh.\f* \rb half that amount|מַחֲצִית֖וֹ\rb* \rb (250 shekels)|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb of fragrant|בֶּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb cinnamon,|וְקִנְּמָן־\rb*\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 250|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref*.3 pounds or 2.9 kilograms of cinnamon.\f* \rb 250 shekels|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb of fragrant|בֹ֖שֶׂם\rb* \rb cane,|וּקְנֵה־\rb*\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 250|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref*.3 pounds or 2.9 kilograms of cane.\f* \v 24 \rb 500 shekels|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb of cassia|וְקִדָּ֕ה\rb*\f + \fr 30:24 \fqa \ref 500|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 12|12\ref*.6 pounds or 5.7 kilograms of cassia.\f* — \rb all according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel—|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb*  \rb and a hin|הִֽין׃\rb* \rb of olive|זַ֖יִת\rb* \rb oil.|וְשֶׁ֥מֶן\rb*\f + \fr 30:24 \fqa A hin\ft is \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.97 gallons or 3.67 liters of olive oil.\f* \v 25 \rb Prepare|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb from these a sacred|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb anointing|מִשְׁחַת־\rb* \rb oil,|שֶׁ֚מֶן\rb* \rb a fragrant blend,|רֹ֥קַח\rb*\rb |מִרְקַ֖חַת\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of a perfumer;|רֹקֵ֑חַ\rb* \rb it will be|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb anointing|מִשְׁחַת־\rb* \rb oil.|שֶׁ֥מֶן\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Use this oil to anoint|וּמָשַׁחְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻֽת׃\rb* \v 27 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָן֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of incense,|הַקְּטֹֽרֶת׃\rb* \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the basin|הַכִּיֹּ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its stand.|כַּנּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 29 \rb You are to consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb so that they will be|וְהָי֖וּ\rb* \rb most|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy.|קָֽדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb Whatever|כָּל־\rb* \rb touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb shall be holy.|יִקְדָּֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 30 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Anoint|תִּמְשָׁ֑ח\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb and consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to serve Me as priests.|לְכַהֵ֥ן\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb And you are to tell|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb ‘This|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb My|לִ֖י\rb* \rb sacred|קֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb* \rb anointing|מִשְׁחַת־\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֠מֶן\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 32 \rb It must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be used to anoint|יִיסָ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb an ordinary man,|אָדָם֙\rb*\rb |בְּשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb and you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb make|תַעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb anything like it|כָּמֹ֑הוּ\rb* \rb with the same formula.|וּבְמַ֨תְכֻּנְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb It|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is holy,|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb and it must be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 33 \rb Anyone|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb mixes perfume|יִרְקַ֣ח\rb* \rb like it|כָּמֹ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb or puts|יִתֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb an outsider|זָ֑ר\rb* \rb shall be cut off|וְנִכְרַ֖ת\rb* \rb from his people.’”|מֵעַמָּֽיו׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Incense
\p \v 34 \rb The LORD also|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb “Take|קַח־\rb* \rb fragrant spices—|סַמִּ֗ים\rb*  \rb gum resin,|נָטָ֤ף׀\rb* \rb onycha,|וּשְׁחֵ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb galbanum,|וְחֶלְבְּנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |סַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and pure|זַכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb frankincense—|וּלְבֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb |יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb in equal measures,|בַּ֥ד\rb*\rb |בְּבַ֖ד\rb* \v 35 \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb a fragrant blend of incense,|קְטֹ֔רֶת\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the work of a perfumer,|רוֹקֵ֑חַ\rb* \rb seasoned with salt,|מְמֻלָּ֖ח\rb* \rb pure|טָה֥וֹר\rb* \rb and holy.|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \v 36 \rb Grind|וְשָֽׁחַקְתָּ֣\rb* \rb some of it|מִמֶּנָּה֮\rb* \rb into fine powder|הָדֵק֒\rb* \rb and place|וְנָתַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb it|מִמֶּ֜נָּה\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the Testimony|הָעֵדֻת֙\rb*\f + \fr 30:36 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I will meet|אִוָּעֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with you.|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb It shall be|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 37 \rb You are never to use|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb this formula|בְּמַ֨תְכֻּנְתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb to make|תַעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb incense|וְהַקְּטֹ֙רֶת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for yourselves;|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb you shall regard it as holy|קֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 38 \rb Anyone|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb makes|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb something like|כָמ֖וֹהָ\rb* \rb it to enjoy|לְהָרִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb its fragrance|בָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb shall be cut off|וְנִכְרַ֖ת\rb* \rb from his people.”|מֵעַמָּֽיו׃ס\rb*
\c 31
\s1 Bezalel and Oholiab
\r \ref Exodus 35:30–35|EXO 35:30-35\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “See,|רְאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb I have called|קָרָ֣אתִֽי\rb* \rb by name|בְשֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Bezalel|בְּצַלְאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uri,|אוּרִ֥י\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hur,|ח֖וּר\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And I have filled|וָאֲמַלֵּ֥א\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God,|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb with skill,|בְּחָכְמָ֛ה\rb* \rb ability,|וּבִתְבוּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וּבְדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb in all kinds|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb of craftsmanship,|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb to design|לַחְשֹׁ֖ב\rb* \rb artistic|מַחֲשָׁבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb works|לַעֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb* \rb in gold,|בַּזָּהָ֥ב\rb* \rb silver,|וּבַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and bronze,|וּבַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \v 5 \rb to cut|וּבַחֲרֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb gemstones|אֶ֛בֶן\rb* \rb for settings,|לְמַלֹּ֖את\rb* \rb and to carve|וּבַחֲרֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb wood,|עֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb so that he may be a master|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb craft.|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Moreover, I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb have selected|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb Oholiab|אָהֳלִיאָ֞ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahisamach,|אֲחִֽיסָמָךְ֙\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Dan,|דָ֔ן\rb* \rb as his assistant.|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb*
\p \rb I have also given|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb skill|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the craftsmen,|חֲכַם־\rb*\rb |לֵ֖ב\rb*\rb |וּבְלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb that they may fashion|וְעָשׂ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you:|צִוִּיתִֽךָ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֗ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָֽאָרֹן֙\rb* \rb of the Testimony|לָֽעֵדֻ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 31:7 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֖רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb upon it,|עָלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the other furnishings|כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tent—|הָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb* \v 8 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its utensils,|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the pure|הַטְּהֹרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb gold lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of incense,|הַקְּטֹֽרֶת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the basin|הַכִּיּ֖וֹר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its stand—|כַּנּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb as well as|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the woven|הַשְּׂרָ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb garments,|בִּגְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb both the holy|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb for Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb for his sons|בָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to serve as priests,|לְכַהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 11 \rb in addition to|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֧מֶן\rb* \rb and fragrant|הַסַּמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֥רֶת\rb* \rb for the Holy Place.|לַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb They are to make them|יַעֲשֽׂוּ׃פ\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have commanded you.”|צִוִּיתִ֖ךָ\rb*
\s1 The Sign of the Sabbath
\r \ref Numbers 15:32–36|NUM 15:32-36\ref*)
\p \v 12 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb |וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Surely|אַ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you must keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֑רוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths,|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this|הִ֜וא\rb* \rb will be a sign|א֨וֹת\rb* \rb between Me|וּבֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and you|בֵּינִ֤י\rb* \rb for the generations to come,|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that you may know|לָדַ֕עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies you.|מְקַדִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath,|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb is holy|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to you.|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Anyone who profanes it|מְחַֽלְלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֔ת\rb*\rb |כִּ֗י\rb* \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb does|הָעֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb any work|מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb on that day|בָהּ֙\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖וא\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb his people.|עַמֶּֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb For six|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֮\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָה֒\rb* \rb may be done,|יֵעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb but the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֧ת\rb* \rb of complete rest,|שַׁבָּת֛וֹן\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb does|הָעֹשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb any work|מְלָאכָ֛ה\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must keep|וְשָׁמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb the Sabbath,|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb celebrating|לַעֲשׂ֧וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַשַּׁבָּ֛ת\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתָ֖ם\rb* \v 17 \rb It|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb is a sign|א֥וֹת\rb* \rb between Me|בֵּינִ֗י\rb*\rb |וּבֵין֙\rb* \rb and the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb forever;|לְעֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb in six|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb but on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb He rested|שָׁבַ֖ת\rb* \rb and was refreshed.’”|וַיִּנָּפַֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Moses Receives the Tablets
\p \v 18 \rb When the LORD had finished|כְּכַלֹּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb with Moses|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai,|סִינַ֔י\rb* \rb He gave|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֑ת\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of stone|אֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb inscribed|כְּתֻבִ֖ים\rb* \rb by the finger|בְּאֶצְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb of God.|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\c 32
\s1 The Golden Calf
\r \ref Deuteronomy 9:7–29|DEU 9:7-29\ref*; \ref Acts 7:39–43|ACT 7:39-43\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now when the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was delayed|בֹשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb in coming down|לָרֶ֣דֶת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb they|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקָּהֵ֨ל\rb* \rb around|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Come,|ק֣וּם׀\rb* \rb make|עֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb will go|יֵֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb before us.|לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb As for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb brought us up|הֶֽעֱלָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb we do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb what|מֶה־\rb* \rb has happened|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb to him!”|לֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:1 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:40|ACT 7:40\ref*\f*
\p \v 2 \rb So Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Take off|פָּֽרְקוּ֙\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb earrings|נִזְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb are on|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your wives|נְשֵׁיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבְנֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and bring them|וְהָבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb to me.”|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took off|וַיִּתְפָּֽרְקוּ֙\rb* \rb their gold|הַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb earrings|נִזְמֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיָּבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron.|אַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \v 4 \rb He took the gold|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb from their hands,|מִיָּדָ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וַיָּ֤צַר\rb* \rb with an engraving tool|בַּחֶ֔רֶט\rb* \rb he fashioned|וַֽיַּעֲשֵׂ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb into a molten|מַסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb calf.|עֵ֣גֶל\rb* \rb And they said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “These,|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb are your gods,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb brought you up|הֶעֱל֖וּךָ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt!”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb When Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb saw this,|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb before the calf|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and proclaimed:|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |אַֽהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “Tomorrow|מָחָֽר׃\rb* \rb shall be a feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So the next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb they arose,|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֙ימוּ֙\rb* \rb offered|וַיַּעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings,|עֹלֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and presented|וַיַּגִּ֖שׁוּ\rb* \rb peace offerings.|שְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb And the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb sat down|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb to eat|לֶֽאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְשָׁת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and got up|וַיָּקֻ֖מוּ\rb* \rb to indulge in revelry.|לְצַחֵֽק׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 32:6 \ft Or \fqa to play\ft ; cited \ref in 1|1\ref* Corinthians 10:7\f*
\p \v 7 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb “Go down at once,|לֶךְ־\rb*\rb |רֵ֕ד\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb your people,|עַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you brought up|הֶעֱלֵ֖יתָ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb have corrupted themselves.|שִׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \v 8 \rb How quickly they have|מַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb turned aside|סָ֣רוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I commanded them!|צִוִּיתִ֔ם\rb* \rb They have made|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb a molten|מַסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb calf|עֵ֖גֶל\rb* \rb and have bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּֽחֲווּ־\rb* \rb to it.|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb They have sacrificed|וַיִּזְבְּחוּ־\rb* \rb to it|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb ‘These,|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb are your gods,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb brought you up|הֶֽעֱל֖וּךָ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.’”|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb “I have seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb and they|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb are indeed|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֖רֶף\rb* \rb people.|עַם־\rb* \v 10 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb leave Me|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb alone,|הַנִּ֣יחָה\rb* \rb so that My anger|אַפִּ֥י\rb* \rb may burn|וְיִֽחַר־\rb* \rb against them|בָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and consume them.|וַאֲכַלֵּ֑ם\rb* \rb Then I will make|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb into a great|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb nation.”|לְג֥וֹי\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sought the favor|וַיְחַ֣ל\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God,|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb why|לָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb does Your anger|אַפְּךָ֙\rb* \rb burn|יֶחֱרֶ֤ה\rb* \rb against Your people,|בְּעַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb You brought|הוֹצֵ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb with great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb power|בְּכֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb and a mighty|חֲזָקָֽה׃\rb* \rb hand?|וּבְיָ֥ד\rb* \v 12 \rb Why|לָמָּה֩\rb* \rb should the Egyptians declare,|יֹאמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘He brought them out|הֽוֹצִיאָם֙\rb* \rb with evil intent,|בְּרָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb to kill|לַהֲרֹ֤ג\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb in the mountains|בֶּֽהָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and wipe them|וּ֨לְכַלֹּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth’?|הָֽאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb Turn|שׁ֚וּב\rb* \rb from Your fierce|מֵחֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb anger|אַפֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and relent|וְהִנָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb from doing|עַל־\rb* \rb harm|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Your people.|לְעַמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Remember|זְכֹ֡ר\rb* \rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָם֩\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֨ק\rb* \rb and Israel,|וּלְיִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb to|לָהֶם֮\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You swore|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְתָּ\rb* \rb by Your very self|בָּךְ֒\rb* \rb when You declared,|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘I will make your descendants|זַרְעֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as numerous|אַרְבֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֖י\rb* \rb in the sky,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and I will give|אֶתֵּן֙\rb* \rb your descendants|לְזַרְעֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֜את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have promised,|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb and it shall be their inheritance|וְנָחֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb forever.’”|לְעֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb relented|וַיִּנָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb the calamity|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had threatened|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb to bring|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb on His people.|לְעַמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּ֜פֶן\rb* \rb and went down|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb with the two|וּשְׁנֵ֛י\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֻ֖ת\rb* \rb in his hands.|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*\rb |לֻחֹ֗ת\rb* \rb They were inscribed|כְּתֻבִים֙\rb* \rb on both|מִשְּׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sides,|עֶבְרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |כְּתֻבִֽים׃\rb* \rb front|מִזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and back.|וּמִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \v 16 \rb The tablets|וְהַ֨לֻּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb were the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of God,|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb and the writing|וְהַמִּכְתָּ֗ב\rb* \rb was the writing|מִכְתַּ֤ב\rb* \rb of God,|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb engraved|חָר֖וּת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tablets.|הַלֻּחֹֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb When Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֧ע\rb* \rb the sound|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb shouting,|בְּרֵעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “The sound|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb is in the camp.”|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb But Moses replied:|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb “It is neither|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the cry|קוֹל֙\rb*\rb |עֲנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of victory|גְּבוּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb nor|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the cry|ק֖וֹל\rb*\rb |עֲנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of defeat;|חֲלוּשָׁ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb hear|שֹׁמֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of singing!”|עַנּ֔וֹת\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb |וַֽיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Moses approached|קָרַב֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the calf|הָעֵ֖גֶל\rb* \rb and the dancing,|וּמְחֹלֹ֑ת\rb* \rb he|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb with anger|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb the tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb out of his hands,|מִיָּדוֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shattering|וַיְשַׁבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb at the base of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the mountain.|הָהָֽר׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the calf|הָעֵ֨גֶל\rb* \rb they had made,|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb burned it|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֣ף\rb* \rb in the fire,|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb ground it|וַיִּטְחַ֖ן\rb* \rb to|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb powder,|דָּ֑ק\rb* \rb and scattered the powder|וַיִּ֙זֶר֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the water.|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb Then he forced|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to drink|וַיַּ֖שְׁקְ\rb* \rb it.|אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb “What|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb did this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb do|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to you,”|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have led them|הֵבֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb into|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb so great|גְדֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb a sin?”|חֲטָאָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be enraged,|יִ֥חַר\rb*\rb |אַ֖ף\rb* \rb my lord,”|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb yourself know|יָדַ֣עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb are intent on evil.|בְרָ֖ע\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \v 23 \rb They told|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb ‘Make|עֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will go|יֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb before us.|לְפָנֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb As for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb brought us up|הֶֽעֱלָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb we do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb what|מֶה־\rb* \rb has happened|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb to him!’|לֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So I said|וָאֹמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to them,|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb ‘Whoever|לְמִ֣י\rb* \rb has gold,|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb let him take it off,’|הִתְפָּרָ֖קוּ\rb* \rb and they gave it|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb to me.|לִ֑י\rb* \rb And when I threw it|וָאַשְׁלִכֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb into the fire,|בָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb out came|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb calf!”|הָעֵ֥גֶל\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb that the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb were out of control,|פָרֻ֖עַ\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb had let them run wild|פְרָעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and become a laughingstock|לְשִׁמְצָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 32:25 \ft Or \fqa and become an object of derision\f* \rb to their enemies.|בְּקָמֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb at the entrance|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb to the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Whoever|מִ֥י\rb* \rb is for the LORD,|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb come to me.”|אֵלָ֑י\rb*
\p \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Levites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵוִֽי׃\rb* \rb gathered|וַיֵּאָסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb around him.|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb He told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Each of you men|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb is to fasten|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb his sword|חַרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his side,|יְרֵכ֑וֹ\rb* \rb go back and forth|עִבְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |וָשׁ֜וּבוּ\rb* \rb through the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb from gate|מִשַּׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to gate,|לָשַׁ֙עַר֙\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and slay|וְהִרְג֧וּ\rb* \rb his brother,|אָחִ֛יו\rb*\rb |וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his friend,|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and his neighbor.’”|קְרֹבֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb The Levites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֖י\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb as Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb commanded,|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb and that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb about three|כִּשְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אַלְפֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb fell dead.|וַיִּפֹּ֤ל\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Afterward, Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you have been ordained|מִלְא֨וּ\rb*\f + \fr 32:29 \ft Or \fqa have ordained yourselves\f* \rb for service|יֶדְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb since|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb each man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb went against his son|בִּבְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and his brother;|וּבְאָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb so the LORD has bestowed|וְלָתֵ֧ת\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָֽה׃\rb* \rb on you|עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb this day.”|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb have committed|חֲטָאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a great|גְדֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb sin.|חֲטָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb I will go up|אֶֽעֱלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb perhaps|אוּלַ֥י\rb* \rb I can make atonement|אֲכַפְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb your sin.”|חַטַּאתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Oh,|אָ֣נָּ֗א\rb* \rb what a great|גְדֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb sin|חֲטָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb have committed!|חָטָ֞א\rb* \rb They have made|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \rb for themselves.|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 32 \rb Yet now,|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb You would only forgive|תִּשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb their sin....|חַטָּאתָ֑ם\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb not,|אַ֕יִן\rb* \rb please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb blot me|מְחֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb out of the book|מִֽסִּפְרְךָ֖\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have written.”|כָּתָֽבְתָּ׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb “Whoever|מִ֚י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has sinned|חָֽטָא־\rb* \rb against Me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb I will blot out|אֶמְחֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb of My book.|מִסִּפְרִֽי׃\rb* \v 34 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb go,|לֵ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb lead|נְחֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb to the place|אֶ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I described.|דִּבַּ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb My angel|מַלְאָכִ֖י\rb* \rb shall go|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before you.|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb But on the day|וּבְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb I settle accounts,|פָּקְדִ֔י\rb* \rb I will punish them|וּפָקַדְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for their sin.”|חַטָּאתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent a plague|וַיִּגֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb on the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb because of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had done|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the calf|הָעֵ֔גֶל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹֽן׃ס\rb* \rb had made.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*
\c 33
\s1 The Command to Leave Sinai
\r \ref Deuteronomy 1:1–8|DEU 1:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb “Leave|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb this place,|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and the people|וְהָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you brought up|הֶֽעֱלִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and go to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I promised|נִ֠שְׁבַּעְתִּי\rb* \rb to Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֨ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb and Jacob|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb when I said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘I will give it|אֶתְּנֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb to your descendants.’|לְזַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \v 2 \rb And I will send|וְשָׁלַחְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb an angel|מַלְאָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb before you,|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and I will drive out|וְגֵֽרַשְׁתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites,|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb Amorites,|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַֽחִתִּי֙\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites.|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Go up to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey.|וּדְבָ֑שׁ\rb* \rb But|כִּי֩\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb go|אֶֽעֱלֶ֜ה\rb* \rb with you,|בְּקִרְבְּךָ֗\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb are a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֙רֶף֙\rb* \rb people;|עַם־\rb* \rb otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I might destroy|אֲכֶלְךָ֖\rb* \rb you on the way.”|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb When the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb bad|הָרָ֛ע\rb* \rb news,|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb they went into mourning,|וַיִּתְאַבָּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb put on|שָׁ֛תוּ\rb* \rb any of his jewelry.|עֶדְי֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 5 \rb For the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb had said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb ‘You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֔רֶף\rb* \rb people.|עַם־\rb* \rb If I should go|אֶֽעֱלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with you|בְקִרְבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb for a single|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb moment,|רֶ֧גַע\rb* \rb I would destroy you.|וְכִלִּיתִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb take off|הוֹרֵ֤ד\rb* \rb your jewelry,|עֶדְיְךָ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and I will decide|וְאֵדְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb what|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb to do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb with you.’”|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stripped themselves|וַיִּֽתְנַצְּל֧וּ\rb* \rb of their jewelry|עֶדְיָ֖ם\rb* \rb from Mount|מֵהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Horeb onward.|חוֹרֵֽב׃\rb*\f + \fr 33:6 \ft That is, from Mount Sinai onward, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
\s1 The Tent of Meeting
\p \v 7 \rb Now Moses|וּמֹשֶׁה֩\rb* \rb used to take|יִקַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֜הֶל\rb* \rb and pitch|וְנָֽטָה־\rb* \rb it|ל֣וֹ׀\rb*\rb |מִח֣וּץ\rb*\rb |לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb at a distance|הַרְחֵק֙\rb* \rb outside|מִן־\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb He called|וְקָ֥רָא\rb* \rb it|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb and|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb inquiring of|מְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb would go|יֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the camp.|לַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then,|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb whenever Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb went out|כְּצֵ֤את\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent,|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְנִ֨צְּב֔וּ\rb* \rb would stand|יָק֙וּמוּ֙\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb at the entrances|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to their own tents|אָהֳל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and watch|וְהִבִּ֙יטוּ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he entered|בֹּא֖וֹ\rb* \rb the tent.|הָאֹֽהֱלָה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb As|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb entered|כְּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb the tent,|הָאֹ֔הֱלָה\rb* \rb the pillar|עַמּ֣וּד\rb* \rb of cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb would come down|יֵרֵד֙\rb* \rb and remain|וְעָמַ֖ד\rb* \rb at the entrance,|פֶּ֣תַח\rb*\rb |הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb and the LORD would speak|וְדִבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וְרָאָ֤ה\rb* \rb the pillar|עַמּ֣וּד\rb* \rb of cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the tent,|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb they|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb* \rb would stand up|וְקָ֤ם\rb* \rb and worship,|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוּ֔וּ\rb* \rb each one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to his own tent.|אָהֳלֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Thus the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb would speak|וְדִבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb face,|פָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his friend.|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb Then Moses would return|וְשָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb but his young|נַ֔עַר\rb* \rb assistant|וּמְשָׁ֨רְת֜וֹ\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נוּן֙\rb* \rb would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave|יָמִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the tent.|הָאֹֽהֶל׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Promise of God’s Presence
\p \v 12 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb “Look,|רְ֠אֵה\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb have been telling me,|אֹמֵ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb ‘Lead|הַ֚עַל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people up,’|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but You|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb let me know|הֽוֹדַעְתַּ֔נִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You will send|תִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb with me.|עִמִּ֑י\rb* \rb Yet You|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb have said,|אָמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘I know|יְדַעְתִּ֣יךָֽ\rb* \rb you by name,|בְשֵׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and you have|וְגַם־\rb* \rb found|מָצָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in My sight.’|בְּעֵינָֽי׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb indeed|נָא֩\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֜ן\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb please|נָא֙\rb* \rb let me know|הוֹדִעֵ֤נִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your ways,|דְּרָכֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb that I may know You|וְאֵדָ֣עֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb and find|אֶמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in Your sight.|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Remember|וּרְאֵ֕ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb is Your people.”|עַמְּךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb And the LORD answered,|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “My Presence|פָּנַ֥י\rb* \rb will go with you,|יֵלֵ֖כוּ\rb* \rb and I will give you rest.”|וַהֲנִחֹ֥תִי\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb Your Presence|פָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb does not|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb go with us,”|הֹלְכִ֔ים\rb* \rb Moses replied,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb lead us up|תַּעֲלֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from here.|מִזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb For how then|וּבַמֶּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb can it be known|יִוָּדַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֵפ֗וֹא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Your people|וְעַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb unless|הֲל֖וֹא\rb* \rb You go|בְּלֶכְתְּךָ֣\rb* \rb with us?|עִמָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb How else will we|אֲנִ֣י\rb*\rb |וְעַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb be distinguished|וְנִפְלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּ֨ל־\rb* \rb the other people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth?”|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb very|גַּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb you have asked,|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have found|מָצָ֤אתָ\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in My sight,|בְּעֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb and I know|וָאֵדָעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb you by name.”|בְּשֵֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Moses said,|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb show me|הַרְאֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb Your glory.”|כְּבֹדֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb will cause all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My goodness|טוּבִי֙\rb* \rb to pass|אַעֲבִ֤יר\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb you,”|פָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb the LORD replied,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “and I will proclaim|וְקָרָ֧אתִֽי\rb* \rb My name—|בְשֵׁ֛ם\rb*  \rb the LORD—|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*  \rb in your presence.|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb I will have mercy|וְחַנֹּתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have mercy,|אָחֹ֔ן\rb* \rb and I will have compassion|וְרִחַמְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have compassion.”|אֲרַחֵֽם׃\rb*\f + \fr 33:19 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 9:15|ROM 9:15\ref*\f*
\p \v 20 \rb But He added,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “You cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My face,|פָּנָ֑י\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb can see Me|יִרְאַ֥נִי\rb* \rb and live.”|וָחָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb continued,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “There|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb is a place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb near Me|אִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb where you are to stand|וְנִצַּבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb a rock,|הַצּֽוּר׃\rb* \v 22 \rb and when|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb My glory|כְּבֹדִ֔י\rb* \rb passes by,|בַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb I will put you|וְשַׂמְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in a cleft|בְּנִקְרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the rock|הַצּ֑וּר\rb* \rb and cover you|וְשַׂכֹּתִ֥י\rb* \rb with My hand|כַפִּ֛י\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I have passed by.|עָבְרִֽי׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Then I will take My hand|כַּפִּ֔י\rb* \rb away,|וַהֲסִרֹתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and you will see|וְרָאִ֖יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My back;|אֲחֹרָ֑י\rb* \rb but My face|וּפָנַ֖י\rb* \rb must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be seen.”|יֵרָאֽוּ׃ס\rb*
\c 34
\s1 New Stone Tablets
\r \ref Deuteronomy 10:1–11|DEU 10:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Chisel out|פְּסָל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb stone|אֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb like the originals,|כָּרִאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb and I will write|וְכָתַבְתִּי֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|הַלֻּחֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were|הָי֛וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the first|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb tablets,|הַלֻּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you broke.|שִׁבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Be|וֶהְיֵ֥ה\rb* \rb ready|נָכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb in the morning,|לַבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb and come up|וְעָלִ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb on Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to present yourself|וְנִצַּבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb before Me|לִ֛י\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountaintop.|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָהָֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb may go up|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you;|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in fact,|וְגַם־\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb may be seen|יֵרָ֖א\rb* \rb anywhere|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb on the mountain—|הָהָ֑ר\rb*  \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֤אן\rb* \rb or herds|וְהַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb may graze|יִרְע֔וּ\rb* \rb in front of|אֶל־\rb*\rb |מ֖וּל\rb* \rb the|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb mountain.”|הָהָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb chiseled out|וַיִּפְסֹ֡ל\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb stone|אֲבָנִ֜ים\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֨ת\rb* \rb like the originals.|כָּרִאשֹׁנִ֗ים\rb* \rb He rose early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb and taking|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb stone|אֲבָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb in his hands,|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb he went up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֔י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb had commanded him.|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb descended|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb in a cloud,|בֶּֽעָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb stood|וַיִּתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and proclaimed|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb His name,|בְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb passed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֨ר\rb* \rb in front of|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|פָּנָיו֮\rb* \rb and called out:|וַיִּקְרָא֒\rb*
\q1 \rb “The LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb God,|אֵ֥ל\rb*
\q2 \rb is compassionate|רַח֖וּם\rb* \rb and gracious,|וְחַנּ֑וּן\rb*
\q1 \rb slow|אֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to anger,|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb abounding|וְרַב־\rb* \rb in loving devotion|חֶ֥סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness,|וֶאֱמֶֽת׀\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb maintaining|נֹצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to a thousand generations,|לָאֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 34:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa to thousands\f*
\q2 \rb forgiving|נֹשֵׂ֥א\rb* \rb iniquity,|עָוֺ֛ן\rb* \rb transgression,|וָפֶ֖שַׁע\rb* \rb and sin.|וְחַטָּאָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb Yet He will by no means|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |וְנַקֵּה֙\rb* \rb leave the guilty unpunished;|יְנַקֶּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb He will visit|פֹּקֵ֣ד׀\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of the fathers|אָב֗וֹת\rb*
\q1 \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their children|בָּנִים֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb grandchildren|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָנִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the third|שִׁלֵּשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and fourth generations.”|רִבֵּעִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb immediately|וַיְמַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb bowed down|וַיִּקֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb and worshiped.|וַיִּשְׁתָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “O Lord,”|אֲדֹנָ֔י\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb* \rb “if|אִם־\rb* \rb I have indeed found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb my Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb please|נָא֩\rb* \rb go|יֵֽלֶךְ־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb with us.|בְּקִרְבֵּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb Although|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb this|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֙רֶף֙\rb* \rb people,|עַם־\rb* \rb forgive|וְסָלַחְתָּ֛\rb* \rb our iniquity|לַעֲוֺנֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb and sin,|וּלְחַטָּאתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and take us as Your inheritance.”|וּנְחַלְתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*
\s1 The LORD Renews the Covenant
\r \ref 2 Corinthians 3:7–18|2CO 3:7-18\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb And the LORD said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֮\rb* \rb am making|כֹּרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb a covenant.|בְּרִית֒\rb* \rb Before|נֶ֤גֶד\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb your people|עַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb I will perform|אֶעֱשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb wonders|נִפְלָאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb have never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been done|נִבְרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb in any|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb nation|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb in all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb the world.|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָ֠עָם\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb among whom you live|בְקִרְבּ֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb will see|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb work,|מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it is|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb an awesome thing|נוֹרָ֣א\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am doing|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb with you.|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Observe|שְׁמָ֨ר־\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb command you|מְצַוְּךָ֣\rb* \rb this day.|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֧י\rb* \rb I will drive out|גֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Canaanites,|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb Hittites,|וְהַחִתִּי֙\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites.|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to make|תִּכְרֹ֤ת\rb* \rb a treaty|בְּרִית֙\rb*\f + \fr 34:12 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft .\f* \rb with the inhabitants|לְיוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are entering,|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb they become|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in your midst.|בְּקִרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Rather,|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you must tear down|תִּתֹּצ֔וּן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their altars,|מִזְבְּחֹתָם֙\rb* \rb smash|תְּשַׁבֵּר֑וּן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their sacred stones,|מַצֵּבֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and chop down|תִּכְרֹתֽוּן׃\rb* \rb their Asherah poles.|אֲשֵׁרָ֖יו\rb* \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb worship|תִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb any other|אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb god,|לְאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb whose name is|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Jealous,|קַנָּ֣א\rb* \rb is a jealous|קַנָּ֖א\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb God.|אֵ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Do not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb make|תִּכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb with the inhabitants|לְיוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb for when they prostitute themselves|וְזָנ֣וּ׀\rb* \rb to|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְזָבְחוּ֙\rb* \rb to them,|לֵאלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb they will invite|וְקָרָ֣א\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb and you will eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb their sacrifices.|מִזִּבְחֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb And when you take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb some of their daughters|מִבְּנֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb as brides for your sons,|לְבָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb their daughters|בְנֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb will prostitute themselves|וְזָנ֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb and cause your sons|בָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to do the same.|וְהִזְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb You shall make|תַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb molten|מַסֵּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb for yourselves.|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You are to keep|תִּשְׁמֹר֒\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֣ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread.|הַמַּצּוֹת֮\rb*\f + \fr 34:18 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see \ref Exodus 12:14–20|EXO 12:14-20\ref*.\f* \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֜ים\rb* \rb at the appointed time|לְמוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb in the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib,|הָאָבִ֑יב\rb*\f + \fr 34:18 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April; twice in this verse.\f* \rb you are to eat|תֹּאכַ֤ל\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּוֹת֙\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I commanded you.|צִוִּיתִ֔ךָ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb in the month|בְּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib|הָֽאָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb you came out|יָצָ֖אתָ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb The first offspring|פֶּ֥טֶר\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb womb|רֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb belongs to Me,|לִ֑י\rb* \rb including all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|פֶּ֖טֶר\rb* \rb males|תִּזָּכָ֔ר\rb* \rb among your livestock,|מִקְנְךָ֙\rb* \rb whether cattle|שׁ֥וֹר\rb* \rb or sheep.|וָשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \v 20 \rb You must redeem|תִּפְדֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb the firstborn|וּפֶ֤טֶר\rb* \rb of a donkey|חֲמוֹר֙\rb* \rb with a lamb;|בְשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb redeem it,|תִפְדֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb you are to break its neck.|וַעֲרַפְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb You must redeem|תִּפְדֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֤וֹר\rb* \rb of your sons.|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb No|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb one shall appear|יֵרָא֥וּ\rb* \rb before Me|פָנַ֖י\rb* \rb empty-handed.|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Six|שֵׁ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb you shall labor,|תַּעֲבֹ֔ד\rb* \rb but on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb you shall rest;|תִּשְׁבֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb even in the seasons of plowing|בֶּחָרִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and harvesting,|וּבַקָּצִ֖יר\rb* \rb you must rest.|תִּשְׁבֹּֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb are to celebrate|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the Feast|וְחַ֤ג\rb* \rb of Weeks|שָׁבֻעֹת֙\rb*\f + \fr 34:22 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Harvest\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref*) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see \ref Acts 2:1|ACT 2:1\ref*).\f* \rb with the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the wheat|חִטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb harvest,|קְצִ֣יר\rb* \rb and the Feast|וְחַג֙\rb* \rb of Ingathering|הָֽאָסִ֔יף\rb*\f + \fr 34:22 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is later called \fqa the Feast of Tabernacles \ft (or \fqa Booths \ft or \fqa Shelters\ft ).\f* \rb at the turn|תְּקוּפַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the year.|הַשָּׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your males|זְכ֣וּרְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to appear|יֵרָאֶה֙\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb the Lord|הָֽאָדֹ֥ן׀\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 24 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will drive out|אוֹרִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and enlarge|וְהִרְחַבְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your borders,|גְּבוּלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb will covet|יַחְמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb your land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb when you go up|בַּעֲלֹֽתְךָ֗\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb to appear|לֵרָאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb offer|תִשְׁחַ֥ט\rb* \rb the blood|דַּם־\rb* \rb of a sacrifice to Me|זִבְחִ֑י\rb* \rb along with|עַל־\rb* \rb anything leavened,|חָמֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb and do not let|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb any of the sacrifice|זֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb from the Passover|הַפָּֽסַח׃\rb* \rb Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb remain|יָלִ֣ין\rb* \rb until morning.|לַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Bring|תָּבִ֕יא\rb* \rb the best|רֵאשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb of the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵי֙\rb* \rb of your soil|אַדְמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb cook|תְבַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִ֖י\rb* \rb in its mother’s|אִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb milk.”|בַּחֲלֵ֥ב\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Write down|כְּתָב־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words,|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb for|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb in accordance with|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb I have made|כָּרַ֧תִּי\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb with|אִתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb you and with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb So Moses was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb nights|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb without|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eating|אָכַ֔ל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֚חֶם\rb* \rb or drinking|שָׁתָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb water.|וּמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb He wrote on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb of the covenant—|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb*  \rb the Ten|עֲשֶׂ֖רֶת\rb* \rb Commandments.|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 34:28 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Ten Words\f*
\p \v 29 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb came down|בְּרֶ֤דֶת\rb* \rb from Mount|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֔י\rb* \rb with the two|וּשְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֤ת\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָֽעֵדֻת֙\rb* \rb in his|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb hands,|בְּיַד־\rb*\rb |בְּרִדְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb he|וּמֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb was unaware|יָדַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |ע֥וֹר\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb had become radiant|קָרַ֛ן\rb* \rb from speaking|בְּדַבְּר֥וֹ\rb* \rb with the LORD.|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 30 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked at|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and behold,|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb was radiant.|קָרַ֖ן\rb* \rb And they were afraid|וַיִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb to approach|מִגֶּ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb him.|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to them;|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb so Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the leaders|הַנְּשִׂאִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the congregation|בָּעֵדָ֑ה\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֧בוּ\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb and Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 32 \rb And after|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵ֥ן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb came near,|נִגְּשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb and Moses commanded|וַיְצַוֵּ֕ם\rb* \rb them|אֵת֩\rb* \rb to do everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb had told him|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai.|סִינָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֣ל\rb* \rb speaking|מִדַּבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb with them,|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb he put|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb a veil|מַסְוֶֽה׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his face.|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \v 34 \rb But whenever Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb went in|וּבְבֹ֨א\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with Him,|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb he would remove|יָסִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the veil|הַמַּסְוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he came out.|צֵאת֑וֹ\rb* \rb And when he came out,|וְיָצָ֗א\rb* \rb he would tell|וְדִבֶּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had been commanded,|יְצֻוֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 35 \rb and the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would see|וְרָא֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb was radiant.|קָרַ֔ן\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹר\rb* \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb would put the veil|הַמַּסְוֶה֙\rb* \rb back|וְהֵשִׁ֨יב\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb his face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he went in|בֹּא֖וֹ\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with the LORD.|אִתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\c 35
\s1 The Sabbath
\p \v 1 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיַּקְהֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֛ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the things|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you to do:|לַעֲשֹׂ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb For six|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֮\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָה֒\rb* \rb may be done,|תֵּעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb but the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb holy day,|קֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb* \rb a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּת֖וֹן\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb does|הָעֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb any work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb on that day|ב֛וֹ\rb* \rb must be put to death.|יוּמָֽת׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb light|תְבַעֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb in any|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of your dwellings|מֹשְׁבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃פ\rb* \rb day.”|בְּי֖וֹם\rb*
\s1 Offerings for the Tabernacle
\r \ref Exodus 25:1–9|EXO 25:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Moses also|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “This|זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb has commanded:|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \v 5 \rb Take|קְח֨וּ\rb* \rb from among you|מֵֽאִתְּכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb an offering|תְּרוּמָה֙\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb Let everyone|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb whose heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb is willing|נְדִ֣יב\rb* \rb bring|יְבִיאֶ֕הָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb an offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD:|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\li1 \rb gold,|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb silver,|וָכֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and bronze;|וּנְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\li1 \v 6 \rb blue,|וּתְכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn;|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb*
\li1 \rb fine linen|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and goat hair;|וְעִזִּֽים׃\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb ram|אֵילִ֧ם\rb* \rb skins|וְעֹרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb dyed red|מְאָדָּמִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְעֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and fine leather;|תְּחָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 35:7 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals; also in verse 23\f*
\li1 \rb acacia|שִׂטִּֽים׃\rb* \rb wood;|וַעֲצֵ֥י\rb*
\li1 \v 8 \rb olive oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb for the light;|לַמָּא֑וֹר\rb*
\li1 \rb spices|וּבְשָׂמִים֙\rb* \rb for the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil|לְשֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and for the fragrant|הַסַּמִּֽים׃\rb* \rb incense;|וְלִקְטֹ֖רֶת\rb*
\li1 \v 9 \rb and onyx stones|וְאַ֨בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֔הַם\rb* \rb and gemstones|וְאַבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb to be mounted|מִלֻּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb on the ephod|לָאֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb and breastpiece.|וְלַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb*
\s1 The Skilled Craftsmen
\p \v 10 \rb Let every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb skilled craftsman|חֲכַם־\rb*\rb |לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb among you|בָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and make|וְיַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has commanded:|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*
\li1 \v 11 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַ֨מִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb with its tent|אָהֳל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and covering,|מִכְסֵ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its clasps|קְרָסָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and frames,|קְרָשָׁ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its crossbars,|בְּרִיחָ֕ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb posts,|עַמֻּדָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and bases;|אֲדָנָֽיו׃\rb*
\li1 \v 12 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its poles|בַּדָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and mercy seat,|הַכַּפֹּ֑רֶת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the veil|פָּרֹ֥כֶת\rb* \rb to shield it;|הַמָּסָֽךְ׃\rb*
\li1 \v 13 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֥ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its poles,|בַּדָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils,|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the Bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of the Presence;|הַפָּנִֽים׃\rb*
