\s1 The People Offer Gifts
\p \v 20 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיֵּֽצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb heart|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb stirred him|נְשָׂא֣וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְכֹ֡ל\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb spirit|רוּח֜וֹ\rb* \rb prompted|נָדְבָ֨ה\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb* \rb and brought|הֵ֠בִיאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an offering|תְּרוּמַ֨ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb for the work|לִמְלֶ֨אכֶת\rb* \rb on the Tent|אֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵד֙\rb* \rb for all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb its services,|עֲבֹ֣דָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and for the holy|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb garments.|וּלְבִגְדֵ֖י\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So all|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb who had willing|נְדִ֣יב\rb* \rb hearts,|לֵ֗ב\rb* \rb both men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and|עַל־\rb* \rb women,|הַנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb and brought|הֵ֠בִיאוּ\rb* \rb brooches|חָ֣ח\rb* \rb and earrings,|וָנֶ֜זֶם\rb* \rb rings|וְטַבַּ֤עַת\rb* \rb and necklaces,|וְכוּמָז֙\rb* \rb and all kinds|כָּל־\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb jewelry.|כְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb And they all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb presented|הֵנִ֛יף\rb* \rb their gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפַ֥ת\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Everyone|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |נִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb had|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb or scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb or fine linen,|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb goat hair,|וְעִזִּ֑ים\rb* \rb ram|אֵילִ֧ם\rb* \rb skins|וְעֹרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb dyed red,|מְאָדָּמִ֛ים\rb* \rb or articles of fine leather,|תְּחָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְעֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb brought them.|הֵבִֽיאוּ׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who could present|מֵרִ֗ים\rb* \rb an offering|תְּר֤וּמַת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb or bronze|וּנְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֕יאוּ\rb* \rb it|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb as a contribution|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Also, everyone|וְכֹ֡ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb had|נִמְצָ֨א\rb*\rb |אִתּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb acacia|שִׁטִּ֛ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb for any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb part|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb of the service|הָעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought it.|הֵבִֽיאוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb skilled|חַכְמַת־\rb*\rb |לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb spun|טָו֑וּ\rb* \rb with her hands|בְּיָדֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb and brought|וַיָּבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb what she had spun:|מַטְוֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb blue,|הַתְּכֵ֙לֶת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb purple,|הָֽאַרְגָּמָ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb or scarlet yarn,|תּוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or fine linen.|הַשֵּֽׁשׁ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the skilled women|הַ֨נָּשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |בְּחָכְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb hearts|לִבָּ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖נָה\rb* \rb were stirred|נָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb spun|טָו֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the goat hair.|הָעִזִּֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb The leaders|וְהַנְּשִׂאִ֣ם\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֔יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb onyx|הַשֹּׁ֔הַם\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and gemstones|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to mount|הַמִּלֻּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb on the ephod|לָאֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb and breastpiece,|וְלַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb* \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb as well as spices|הַבֹּ֖שֶׂם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and olive oil|הַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb for the light,|לְמָא֕וֹר\rb* \rb for the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil,|וּלְשֶׁ֙מֶן֙\rb* \rb and for the fragrant|הַסַּמִּֽים׃\rb* \rb incense.|וְלִקְטֹ֖רֶת\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and women|וְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb hearts|לִבָּם֮\rb* \rb prompted|נָדַ֣ב\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֒\rb* \rb brought|לְהָבִיא֙\rb* \rb a freewill offering|נְדָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*\rb |הֵבִ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded them|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb to do.|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb*
\s1 Bezalel and Oholiab
\r \ref Exodus 31:1–11|EXO 31:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 30 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb “See,|רְא֛וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has called|קָרָ֥א\rb* \rb by name|בְּשֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Bezalel|בְּצַלְאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uri,|אוּרִ֥י\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hur,|ח֖וּר\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 31 \rb And He has filled|וַיְמַלֵּ֥א\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God,|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb with skill,|בְּחָכְמָ֛ה\rb* \rb ability,|בִּתְבוּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וּבְדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb in all kinds|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb of craftsmanship,|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \v 32 \rb to design|וְלַחְשֹׁ֖ב\rb* \rb artistic|מַֽחַשָׁבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb works|לַעֲשֹׂ֛ת\rb* \rb in gold,|בַּזָּהָ֥ב\rb* \rb silver,|וּבַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and bronze,|וּבַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \v 33 \rb to cut|וּבַחֲרֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb gemstones|אֶ֛בֶן\rb* \rb for settings,|לְמַלֹּ֖את\rb* \rb and to carve|וּבַחֲרֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb wood,|עֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb so that he may be a master|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb artistic|מַחֲשָֽׁבֶת׃\rb* \rb craft.|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb And the LORD|בְּלִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb both him|ה֕וּא\rb* \rb and Oholiab|וְאָֽהֳלִיאָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahisamach,|אֲחִיסָמָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Dan,|דָֽן׃\rb* \rb the ability to teach others.|וּלְהוֹרֹ֖ת\rb* \v 35 \rb He has filled|מִלֵּ֨א\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb with skill|חָכְמַת־\rb*\rb |לֵ֗ב\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂוֹת֮\rb* \rb all kinds|כָּל־\rb* \rb of work|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb as engravers,|חָרָ֣שׁ׀\rb* \rb designers,|וְחֹשֵׁב֒\rb* \rb embroiderers|וְרֹקֵ֞ם\rb* \rb in blue,|בַּתְּכֵ֣לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וּבָֽאַרְגָּמָ֗ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn|בְּתוֹלַ֧עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֛י\rb* \rb and fine linen,|וּבַשֵּׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb and as weavers—|וְאֹרֵ֑ג\rb*  \rb as artistic designers|עֹשֵׂי֙\rb*\rb |וְחֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb*\rb |מַחֲשָׁבֹֽת׃\rb* \rb of every kind|כָּל־\rb* \rb of craft.|מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb*[’’]
\c 36
\s1 The People Bring More than Enough
\p \v 1 \rb “So Bezalel,|בְצַלְאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb Oholiab,|וְאָהֳלִיאָ֜ב\rb* \rb and every|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb skilled|חֲכַם־\rb*\rb |לֵ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb person|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb are to carry out|וְעָשָׂה֩\rb* \rb everything|לְכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֖ה\rb* \rb by the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb who|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb them|בָּהֵ֔מָּה\rb* \rb skill|חָכְמָ֤ה\rb* \rb and ability|וּתְבוּנָה֙\rb* \rb to know|לָדַ֣עַת\rb* \rb how to perform|לַעֲשֹׂ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֖אכֶת\rb* \rb of constructing|עֲבֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb the sanctuary.”|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Bezalel,|בְּצַלְאֵ֘ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Oholiab,|אָֽהֳלִיאָב֒\rb*\rb |וְאֶל֙\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb skilled|חֲכַם־\rb*\rb |לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb person|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |בְּלִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had gifted—|נָתַ֧ן\rb*\rb |חָכְמָ֖ה\rb*  \rb everyone|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb stirred him|נְשָׂא֣וֹ\rb* \rb to come|לְקָרְבָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and do|לַעֲשֹׂ֥ת\rb* \rb the work.|הַמְּלָאכָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb They received|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb* \rb from|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the contributions|הַתְּרוּמָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb had brought|הֵבִ֜יאוּ\rb* \rb to carry out|לִמְלֶ֛אכֶת\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of constructing|לַעֲשֹׂ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the sanctuary.|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb*
\p \rb Meanwhile, the people|וְ֠הֵם\rb* \rb continued to bring|הֵבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֥יו\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb freewill offerings|נְדָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb morning|בַּבֹּ֥קֶר\rb* \rb after morning,|בַּבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \v 4 \rb so that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the skilled craftsmen|הַ֣חֲכָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were doing|הָעֹשִׂ֕ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb on the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb left|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb their work|מִמְּלַאכְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הֵ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |עֹשִֽׂים׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “The people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb are bringing|לְהָבִ֑יא\rb* \rb more|מַרְבִּ֥ים\rb* \rb than enough|מִדֵּ֤י\rb* \rb for doing|הָֽעֲבֹדָה֙\rb* \rb the work|לַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb us|אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb to do.”|לַעֲשֹׂ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb After Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had given an order,|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb they sent|וַיַּעֲבִ֨ירוּ\rb* \rb a proclamation|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb throughout the camp:|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶה֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “No|אַל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or woman|וְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb should make|יַעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb anything|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb else|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb as an offering|לִתְרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb for the sanctuary.”|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb So the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb were restrained|וַיִּכָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb from bringing more,|מֵהָבִֽיא׃\rb* \v 7 \rb since what they already had|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb was more|וְהוֹתֵֽר׃ס\rb* \rb than enough|דַיָּ֛ם\rb* \rb to perform|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb the work.|וְהַמְּלָאכָ֗ה\rb*
\s1 The Ten Curtains for the Tabernacle
\r \ref Exodus 26:1–6|EXO 26:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the skilled craftsmen|חֲכַם־\rb*\rb |לֵ֜ב\rb* \rb among the workmen|וַיַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|בְּעֹשֵׂ֧י\rb* \rb the ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb for the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb They were made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֗ר\rb* \rb linen,|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb as well as blue,|וּתְכֵ֤לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָן֙\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb with cherubim|כְּרֻבִ֛ים\rb* \rb skillfully|חֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb worked into them.|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \v 9 \rb Each|הָֽאַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb was twenty-eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֜רֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide;|וְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb*\f + \fr 36:9 \ft Each of the ten curtains was \ref approximately 42|42\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (12.8 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹֽת׃\rb* \rb were the same|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb size.|מִדָּ֥ה\rb* \v 10 \rb And he joined|וַיְחַבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb together,|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb and the other five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |יְרִיעֹת֙\rb* \rb he joined|חִבַּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb as well.|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶחָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb He made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלְאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of blue material|תְּכֵ֗לֶת\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the end|מִקָּצָ֖ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָה֙\rb* \rb in the first|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb set,|בַּמַּחְבָּ֑רֶת\rb* \rb and also|עָשָׂה֙\rb*\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb*\rb |בִּשְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb on the end|הַקִּ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb set.|בַּמַּחְבֶּ֖רֶת\rb* \v 12 \rb He made|עָשָׂה֮\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻלָאֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on one|הָאֶחָת֒\rb* \rb curtain|בַּיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻלָאֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb on the end|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑ית\rb* \rb set,|בַּמַּחְבֶּ֣רֶת\rb* \rb so that the loops|הַלֻּ֣לָאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb lined up|מַקְבִּילֹת֙\rb* \rb opposite|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb another.|אֶחָֽת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb clasps|קַרְסֵ֣י\rb* \rb to join|וַיְחַבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the curtains|הַיְרִעֹ֜ת\rb* \rb together,|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |אַחַת֙\rb*\rb |בַּקְּרָסִ֔ים\rb* \rb so that the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a unit.|אֶחָֽד׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Eleven Curtains of Goat Hair
\r \ref Exodus 26:7–14|EXO 26:7-14\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb He then made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of goat hair|עִזִּ֔ים\rb* \rb for the tent|לְאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle—|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb*  \rb eleven|עַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb in all.|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Each|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the eleven|לְעַשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb curtains|יְרִיעֹֽת׃\rb* \rb was the same|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb size—|מִדָּ֣ה\rb* \rb |הָאַחַ֗ת\rb*\rb |הַיְרִיעָ֣ה\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁים֙\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb wide.|רֹ֖חַב\rb*\f + \fr 36:15 \ft Each of the eleven curtains was \ref approximately 45|45\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (13.7 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f* \v 16 \rb He joined|וַיְחַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the curtains|הַיְרִיעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb into one set|לְבָ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the other|הַיְרִיעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb into another.|לְבָֽד׃\rb* \v 17 \rb He made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֗ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻֽלָאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb along|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the end|הַקִּיצֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the first set,|בַּמַּחְבָּ֑רֶת\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb loops|לֻלָאֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the edge|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the corresponding curtain|הַיְרִיעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb set.|הַחֹבֶ֖רֶת\rb* \v 18 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֑ים\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb clasps|קַרְסֵ֥י\rb* \rb to join the tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb*\rb |לִֽהְיֹ֥ת\rb* \rb together|לְחַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as a unit.|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Additionally, he made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb for the tent|לָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb a covering|מִכְסֶה֙\rb* \rb of ram|אֵלִ֖ים\rb* \rb skins|עֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb dyed red,|מְאָדָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and over that|מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃ס\rb* \rb a covering|וּמִכְסֵ֛ה\rb*\rb |עֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of fine leather.|תְּחָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 36:19 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals\f*
\s1 The Frames and Bases
\r \ref Exodus 26:15–30|EXO 26:15-30\ref*)
\p \v 20 \rb Next, he constructed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb upright|עֹמְדִֽים׃\rb* \rb frames|הַקְּרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֖ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the tabernacle.|לַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 21 \rb Each frame|הַקָּ֑רֶשׁ\rb* \rb was ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמֹּ֖ות\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb and a half|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide.|רֹ֖חַב\rb*\f + \fr 36:21 \ft Each frame was \ref approximately 15|15\ref* feet long and 2.25 feet wide (4.6 meters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f* \rb |הַקֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb*\v 22 \rb Two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb tenons|יָדֹ֗ת\rb*\f + \fr 36:22 \ft That is, projecting pieces of wood made for insertion into another piece; similarly in verse 24.\f* \rb were connected|מְשֻׁלָּבֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb each|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb other|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb for each|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb frame.|לַקֶּ֙רֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb He made|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the frames|קַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb* \rb in this way.|כֵּ֣ן\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb He constructed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַקְּרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb for the south|נֶ֥גֶב\rb*\rb |תֵּימָֽנָה׃\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|לַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 24 \rb with|עָשָׂ֕ה\rb* \rb forty|וְאַרְבָּעִים֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶ֔סֶף\rb* \rb bases|אַדְנֵי־\rb* \rb to put under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb frames—|הַקְּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb bases|אֲדָנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb for each frame,|הַקֶּ֤רֶשׁ\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |לִשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |יְדֹתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֛ים\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb*\rb |הַקֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |לִשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb tenon.|יְדֹתָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb For the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb side|וּלְצֶ֧לַע\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb side,|לִפְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb he made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 26 \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb bases—|אַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb bases|אֲדָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֚חַת\rb*\rb |הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |הַקֶּ֣רֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb frame.|הַקֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb He made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb for the rear|וּֽלְיַרְכְּתֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb the west side,|יָ֑מָּה\rb* \v 28 \rb and|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb for the two back|בַּיַּרְכָתָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb corners|לִמְקֻצְעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \v 29 \rb |וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb coupled together|תוֹאֲמִם֮\rb* \rb from bottom|מִלְּמַטָּה֒\rb*\rb |וְיַחְדָּ֗ו\rb*\rb |יִהְי֤וּ\rb*\rb |תַמִּים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb top|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and fitted into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a single|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb ring.|הַטַּבַּ֖עַת\rb* \rb He made|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb both|לִשְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |לִשְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb corners|הַמִּקְצֹעֹֽת׃\rb* \rb in this way.|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \v 30 \rb So there were|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb frames|קְרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and sixteen|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb bases—|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*  \rb two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִים֙\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲדָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb frame.|הַקֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֕ה\rb* \rb crossbars|בְּרִיחֵ֖י\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the frames|לְקַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb on one|הָאֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb side|צֶֽלַע־\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \v 32 \rb five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְרִיחִ֔ם\rb* \rb for those|לְקַרְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb on the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֑ית\rb* \rb side,|צֶֽלַע־\rb*\rb |הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb and five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |בְרִיחִם֙\rb* \rb for those|לְקַרְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb on the rear side|לַיַּרְכָתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb to the west.|יָֽמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb He made|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the central|הַתִּיכֹ֑ן\rb* \rb crossbar|הַבְּרִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb to run through|לִבְרֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb the center|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the frames,|הַקְּרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb one end|הַקָּצֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the other.|הַקָּצֶֽה׃\rb* \v 34 \rb And|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb he overlaid|צִפָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the frames|הַקְּרָשִׁ֞ים\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and made|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to hold|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb the crossbars.|לַבְּרִיחִ֑ם\rb* \rb He also overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crossbars|הַבְּרִיחִ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\s1 The Veil
\r \ref Exodus 26:31–35|EXO 26:31-35\ref*)
\p \v 35 \rb Next, he made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the veil|הַפָּרֹ֔כֶת\rb* \rb of blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb* \rb linen,|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb with cherubim|כְּרֻבִֽים׃\rb* \rb skillfully|חֹשֵׁ֛ב\rb* \rb worked into it.|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָה֙\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of acacia wood|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb for it|לָ֗הּ\rb* \rb and overlaid them|וַיְצַפֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb with gold,|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb along with gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb hooks;|וָוֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and he cast|וַיִּצֹ֣ק\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb silver|כָֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb bases|אַדְנֵי־\rb* \rb for the posts.|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*
\s1 The Curtain for the Entrance
\r \ref Exodus 26:36–37|EXO 26:36-37\ref*)
\p \v 37 \rb For the entrance|לְפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the tent,|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a curtain|מָסָךְ֙\rb* \rb embroidered|רֹקֵֽם׃\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb linen,|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \v 38 \rb together with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדָ֤יו\rb* \rb and their hooks.|וָ֣וֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \rb He overlaid|וְצִפָּ֧ה\rb* \rb the tops|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of the posts and their bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold,|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb and their five|חֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb bases|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb were bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃פ\rb*
\c 37
\s1 Constructing the Ark
\r \ref Exodus 25:10–16|EXO 25:10-16\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Bezalel went on|בְּצַלְאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to construct|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood,|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb two|אַמָּתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb and a half cubits|וָחֵ֜צִי\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֙צִי֙\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 37:1 \ft The ark was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long, 2.25 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (114.3 centimeters long, 68.6 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 2 \rb He overlaid|וַיְצַפֵּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb it with pure|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb both inside|מִבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb and out,|וּמִח֑וּץ\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And he cast|וַיִּצֹ֣ק\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb for|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb its four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb feet,|פַּעֲמֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb rings|טַבָּעֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb one|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb side|צַלְעוֹ֙\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּי֙\rb*\rb |טַבָּע֔וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the other.|הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*\rb |צַלְע֖וֹ\rb* \v 4 \rb Then he made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb poles|בַּדֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \v 5 \rb He inserted|וַיָּבֵ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּים֙\rb* \rb into the rings|בַּטַּבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the sides|צַלְעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the ark|הָאָרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb in order to carry|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it.|הָאָרֹֽן׃\rb*
\s1 The Mercy Seat
\r \ref Exodus 25:17–22|EXO 25:17-22\ref*)
\p \v 6 \rb He constructed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a mercy seat|כַּפֹּ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb two|אַמָּתַ֤יִם\rb* \rb and a half cubits|וָחֵ֙צִי֙\rb* \rb long|אָרְכָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb wide.|רָחְבָּֽהּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 37:6 \ft The mercy seat was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long and 2.25 feet wide (114.3 centimeters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f* \v 7 \rb He made|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb cherubim|כְרֻבִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of hammered|מִקְשָׁה֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb at the|מִשְּׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb ends|קְצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the mercy seat,|הַכַּפֹּֽרֶת׃\rb* \v 8 \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb cherub|כְּרוּב־\rb* \rb on one|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb end|מִקָּצָה֙\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |וּכְרוּב־\rb* \rb on the other,|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |מִקָּצָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הַכַּפֹּ֛רֶת\rb* \rb all made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִשְּׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb from one piece of gold.|קִצְווֹתוֹ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb |וַיִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb And the cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִים֩\rb* \rb had wings|כְנָפַ֜יִם\rb* \rb that spread|פֹּרְשֵׂ֨י\rb* \rb upward,|לְמַ֗עְלָה\rb* \rb overshadowing|סֹֽכְכִ֤ים\rb* \rb the mercy seat.|הַכַּפֹּ֔רֶת\rb*\rb |בְּכַנְפֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb The cherubim faced|וּפְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb other,|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb looking toward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַכְּרֻבִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb the mercy seat.|הַכַּפֹּ֔רֶת\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb*
\s1 The Table of Showbread
\r \ref Exodus 25:23–30|EXO 25:23-30\ref*; \ref Leviticus 24:5–9|LEV 24:5-9\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֖ן\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb two cubits|אַמָּתַ֤יִם\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּוֹ֙\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and a half|וָחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 37:10 \ft The table was \ref approximately 3|3\ref* feet long, 1.5 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (91.4 centimeters long, 45.7 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 11 \rb He overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And he made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb a rim|מִסְגֶּ֛רֶת\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb it|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a handbreadth wide|טֹ֖פַח\rb*\f + \fr 37:12 \fqa A handbreadth\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref*.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \rb and put|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb molding|זֵר־\rb* \rb on|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the rim.|לְמִסְגַּרְתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb He cast|וַיִּצֹ֣ק\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb for the table|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and fastened|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הַטַּבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb corners|הַפֵּאֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb at its four|לְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb legs.|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 14 \rb The rings|הַטַּבָּעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb were placed|הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb close|לְעֻמַּת֙\rb* \rb to the rim,|הַמִּסְגֶּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb to serve as holders|בָּתִּים֙\rb* \rb for the poles|לַבַּדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb used to carry|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table.|הַשֻּׁלְחָֽן׃\rb* \v 15 \rb He made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּים֙\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for carrying|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָֽן׃\rb* \rb and overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָ֑ב\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the utensils|הַכֵּלִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃פ\rb* \rb gold:|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb its plates|קְעָרֹתָ֤יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and dishes,|כַּפֹּתָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb as well as its bowls|מְנַקִּיֹּתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and pitchers|הַקְּשָׂוֺ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb for pouring drink offerings.|יֻסַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |בָּהֵ֑ן\rb*
\s1 The Lampstand
\r \ref Exodus 25:31–40|EXO 25:31-40\ref*; \ref Numbers 8:1–4|NUM 8:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb Then he made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb out of pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb hammered|מִקְשָׁ֞ה\rb* \rb gold,|זָהָ֣ב\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמְּנֹרָה֙\rb* \rb all of one piece:|מִמֶּ֥נָּה\rb*\rb |הָיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb its base|יְרֵכָ֣הּ\rb* \rb and shaft,|וְקָנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb its cups,|גְּבִיעֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb and its buds|כַּפְתֹּרֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb and petals.|וּפְרָחֶ֖יהָ\rb* \v 18 \rb Six|וְשִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb branches|קָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb extended|יֹצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from the sides,|מִצִּדֶּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |קְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מְנֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb on one|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb side|מִצִּדָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb*\rb |קְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מְנֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the other.|הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb*\rb |מִצִּדָּ֖הּ\rb* \v 19 \rb There were three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb cups|גְ֠בִעִים\rb* \rb shaped like almond blossoms|מְֽשֻׁקָּדִ֞ים\rb* \rb on the first|הָאֶחָד֮\rb* \rb branch,|בַּקָּנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb each with buds|כַּפְתֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb and petals,|וָפֶרַח֒\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |גְבִעִ֗ים\rb*\rb |מְשֻׁקָּדִ֛ים\rb*\rb |כַּפְתֹּ֣ר\rb*\rb |וָפָ֑רַח\rb* \rb on the next|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb branch,|בְּקָנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and the same|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb for all six|לְשֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb branches|הַקָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb that extended|הַיֹּצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lampstand.|הַמְּנֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And on the lampstand|וּבַמְּנֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb were four|אַרְבָּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb cups|גְבִעִ֑ים\rb* \rb shaped like almond blossoms|מְשֻׁ֨קָּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb with buds|כַּפְתֹּרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and petals.|וּפְרָחֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb A bud|וְכַפְתֹּ֡ר\rb* \rb was under|תַּחַת֩\rb* \rb the first pair|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of branches|הַקָּנִ֜ים\rb* \rb that extended|הַיֹּצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from the lampstand,|מִמֶּ֗נָּה\rb* \rb a bud|וְכַפְתֹּר֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the second pair,|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֔נָּה\rb*\rb |הַקָּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb* \rb and a bud|וְכַפְתֹּ֕ר\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb the third pair.|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |לְשֵׁ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*\rb |הַקָּנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \v 22 \rb The buds|כַּפְתֹּרֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and branches|וּקְנֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb were|הָי֑וּ\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb of one piece with the lampstand,|מִמֶּ֣נָּה\rb*\rb |אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb hammered|מִקְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb out of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its seven|שִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb lamps,|נֵרֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb its wick trimmers,|וּמַלְקָחֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb and trays|וּמַחְתֹּתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \v 24 \rb He made|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the lampstand|אֹתָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלֶֽיהָ׃פ\rb* \rb from a talent|כִּכָּ֛ר\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֥ב\rb*\f + \fr 37:24 \fqa A talent\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref*.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f*
\s1 The Altar of Incense
\r \ref Exodus 30:1–10|EXO 30:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 25 \rb He made|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹ֖רֶת\rb* \rb out of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood.|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb It was square,|רָב֗וּעַ\rb* \rb a cubit|אַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּוֹ֩\rb* \rb a cubit|וְאַמָּ֨ה\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and two cubits|וְאַמָּתַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb high.|קֹֽמָת֔וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 37:25 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 3 feet high (45.7 centimeters in length and width, and 91.4 centimeters high).\f* \rb Its horns|קַרְנֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb were|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb of one piece.|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \v 26 \rb And he overlaid|וַיְצַ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb with pure|טָה֗וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb the top|גַּגּ֧וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the sides|קִירֹתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and horns.|קַרְנֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb Then he made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a molding|זֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb He made|עָֽשָׂה־\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּי֩\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֜ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֨ת\rb* \rb below|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the molding|לְזֵר֗וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |צַלְעֹתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |עַ֖ל\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb opposite sides|צִדָּ֑יו\rb* \rb to hold|לְבָתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb the poles|לְבַדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb used to carry|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb* \rb it.|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \v 28 \rb And he made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָה֙\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֤מֶן\rb* \rb and the pure,|טָה֑וֹר\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb fragrant|הַסַּמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb incense,|קְטֹ֥רֶת\rb* \rb the work of a perfumer.|רֹקֵֽחַ׃פ\rb*
\c 38
\s1 The Bronze Altar
\r \ref Exodus 27:1–8|EXO 27:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Bezalel constructed|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb*\f + \fr 38:1 \ft Literally \fqa He constructed\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb from acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood.|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb It was square,|רָב֔וּעַ\rb* \rb five|חָמֵשׁ֩\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb long,|אָרְכּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb five|וְחָֽמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb wide,|רָחְבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and three|וְשָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high.|קֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 38:1 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 4.5 feet high (2.3 meters in length and width, and 1.4 meters high).\f* \v 2 \rb He made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb a horn|קַרְנֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb at each of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb its four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb corners,|פִּנֹּתָ֔יו\rb* \rb so that the horns and altar|קַרְנֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb of one piece,|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb and he overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb the altar with bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb He made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the altar’s|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb utensils|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of bronze—|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*  \rb its pots,|הַסִּירֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb shovels,|הַיָּעִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb sprinkling bowls,|הַמִּזְרָקֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb meat forks,|הַמִּזְלָגֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and firepans.|הַמַּחְתֹּ֑ת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |כֵּלָ֖יו\rb* \v 4 \rb He made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a grate|מִכְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb mesh|רֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb for the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb under|תַּ֧חַת\rb* \rb its ledge,|כַּרְכֻּבּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb halfway|חֶצְיֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb up from the bottom.|מִלְּמַ֖טָּה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb At the four|אַרְבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb corners|הַקְּצָוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb of the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb grate|לְמִכְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb he cast|וַיִּצֹ֞ק\rb* \rb four|בְּאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb rings|טַבָּעֹ֛ת\rb* \rb as holders|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for the poles.|לַבַּדִּֽים׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And he made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb and overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then he inserted|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles|הַבַּדִּ֜ים\rb* \rb into the rings|בַּטַּבָּעֹ֗ת\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the sides|צַלְעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb for carrying|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb* \rb it.|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb He made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the altar|אֹתֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb with boards|לֻחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb so that it was hollow.|נְב֥וּב\rb*
\s1 The Bronze Basin
\r \ref Exodus 30:17–21|EXO 30:17-21\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb Next he made|וַיַּ֗עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb basin|הַכִּיּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb and its stand|כַּנּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb from the mirrors|בְּמַרְאֹת֙\rb* \rb of the women who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |צָֽבְא֔וּ\rb* \rb served|הַצֹּ֣בְאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Courtyard
\r \ref Exodus 27:9–19|EXO 27:9-19\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb Then he constructed|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the courtyard.|הֶחָצֵ֑ר\rb* \rb The south|נֶ֣גֶב\rb*\rb |תֵּימָ֗נָה\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֣ת׀\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb was a hundred|מֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb cubits long|בָּאַמָּֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 38:9 \fqa \ref 100|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 150|150\ref* feet or 45.7 meters.\f* \rb and had curtains|קַלְעֵ֤י\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֔ר\rb* \rb linen,|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \v 10 \rb with twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb bases,|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and with silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb hooks|וָוֵ֧י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on the posts.|הָעַמֻּדִ֛ים\rb* \v 11 \rb The north|צָפוֹן֙\rb* \rb side|וְלִפְאַ֤ת\rb* \rb was also a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits long,|בָֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb with twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb The hooks|וָוֵ֧י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of the posts|הָֽעַמּוּדִ֛ים\rb* \rb were silver.|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \v 12 \rb The west|יָ֗ם\rb* \rb side|וְלִפְאַת־\rb* \rb was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits long|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 38:12 \fqa \ref 50|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref* feet or 22.9 meters.\f* \rb and had curtains,|קְלָעִים֙\rb* \rb with ten|עֲשָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb The hooks|וָוֵ֧י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשׁוּקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of the posts|הָעַמֻּדִ֛ים\rb* \rb were silver.|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And the east|קֵ֥דְמָה\rb* \rb side,|וְלִפְאַ֛ת\rb* \rb toward the sunrise,|מִזְרָ֖חָה\rb* \rb was also fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits long.|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb The curtains|קְלָעִ֛ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb one side|הַכָּתֵ֑ף\rb* \rb of the entrance were fifteen|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits long,|אַמָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 38:14 \fqa \ref 15|5\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 22|22\ref*.5 feet or 6.9 meters.\f* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמּוּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 15 \rb And the curtains|קְלָעִ֕ים\rb* \rb on the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֗ית\rb* \rb side|וְלַכָּתֵ֣ף\rb* \rb were also fifteen|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cubits long,|אַמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|עַמֻּדֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb bases|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as well.|מִזֶּ֤ה\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |הֶֽחָצֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |לְשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \v 16 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the curtains|קַלְעֵ֧י\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֛ר\rb* \rb were made of finely spun|מָשְׁזָֽר׃\rb* \rb linen.|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \v 17 \rb The bases|וְהָאֲדָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb for the posts|לָֽעַמֻּדִים֮\rb* \rb were bronze,|נְחֹשֶׁת֒\rb* \rb the hooks|וָוֵ֨י\rb* \rb and bands|וַחֲשׁוּקֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |הָֽעַמּוּדִ֜ים\rb* \rb were silver,|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb and the plating|וְצִפּ֥וּי\rb* \rb for the tops|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of the posts was silver.|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\rb |וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb So all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the posts|עַמֻּדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶחָצֵֽר׃\rb* \rb were banded|מְחֻשָּׁקִ֣ים\rb* \rb with silver.|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb The curtain|וּמָסַ֞ךְ\rb* \rb for the entrance|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to the courtyard|הֶחָצֵר֙\rb*\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb was embroidered|רֹקֵ֔ם\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb It was twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 38:18 \fqa \ref 20|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 30|30\ref* feet or 9.1 meters.\f* \rb and, like|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb the curtains|קַלְעֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the courtyard,|הֶחָצֵֽר׃\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb high,|וְקוֹמָ֤ה\rb*\f + \fr 38:18 \fqa 5 cubits\ft is \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet or 2.3 meters.\f* \rb |בְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb*\v 19 \rb with four|אַרְבָּעָ֔ה\rb* \rb posts|וְעַמֻּֽדֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb bases.|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb Their hooks|וָוֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb were silver,|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb as well as the bands|וַחֲשֻׁקֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and the plating|וְצִפּ֧וּי\rb* \rb of their tops.|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \v 20 \rb All|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb the tent pegs|הַיְתֵדֹ֞ת\rb* \rb for the tabernacle|לַמִּשְׁכָּ֧ן\rb* \rb and for the surrounding|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb courtyard|וְלֶחָצֵ֛ר\rb* \rb were bronze.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃ס\rb*
\s1 An Inventory of Materials
\r \ref Ezra 2:68–70|EZR 2:68-70\ref*; \ref Nehemiah 7:70–73|NEH 7:70-73\ref*)
\p \v 21 \rb This|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb is the inventory|פְקוּדֵ֤י\rb* \rb for the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּן֙\rb* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֔ת\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb recorded|פֻּקַּ֖ד\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb by|עֲבֹדַת֙\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb under the direction|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of Ithamar|אִֽיתָמָ֔ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb the priest.|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Bezalel|וּבְצַלְאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uri,|אוּרִ֥י\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hur,|ח֖וּר\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb With him was|וְאִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Oholiab|אָהֳלִיאָ֞ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahisamach,|אֲחִיסָמָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Dan,|דָ֖ן\rb* \rb an engraver,|חָרָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb designer,|וְחֹשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb and embroiderer|וְרֹקֵ֗ם\rb* \rb in blue,|בַּתְּכֵ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb purple,|וּבָֽאַרְגָּמָ֔ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn|וּבְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and fine linen.|וּבַשֵּֽׁשׁ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb from the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֗ה\rb* \rb used|הֶֽעָשׂוּי֙\rb* \rb for the work|לַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb*\rb |בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb on the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb totaled|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |זְהַ֣ב\rb* \rb 29|תֵּ֤שַׁע\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and 730|וּשְׁבַ֨ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֧וֹת\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb shekels,|שֶׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 38:24 \ft The total weight of the gold was \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.1 tons or 1 metric ton.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb shekel.|בְּשֶׁ֥קֶל\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb The silver|וְכֶ֛סֶף\rb* \rb from those numbered|פְּקוּדֵ֥י\rb* \rb among the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb totaled 100|מְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and 1,775|וְאֶלֶף֩\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֨ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֜וֹת\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֛ים\rb* \rb shekels,|שֶׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 38:25 \ft The total weight of the silver was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.79 tons or 3.44 metric tons.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb shekel—|בְּשֶׁ֥קֶל\rb* \v 26 \rb a beka|בֶּ֚קַע\rb* \rb per person,|לַגֻּלְגֹּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb that is, half|מַחֲצִ֥ית\rb* \rb a shekel,|הַשֶּׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 38:26 \fqa A beka\ft is half a shekel, or \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.2 ounces or 5.7 grams.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb from everyone|לְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb of age|מִבֶּ֨ן\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb who had crossed over|הָעֹבֵ֜ר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb be numbered,|הַפְּקֻדִ֗ים\rb* \rb a total of 603,550|לְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men.|וַחֲמִשִּֽׁים׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb The hundred|מְאַת֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of silver|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 38:27 \fqa \ref 100|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb were|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb used to cast|לָצֶ֗קֶת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the bases|אַדְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the bases|אַדְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the veil—|הַפָּרֹ֑כֶת\rb* \rb 100|מְאַ֧ת\rb* \rb bases|אֲדָנִ֛ים\rb* \rb from the 100|לִמְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb talents,|הַכִּכָּ֖ר\rb* \rb one talent|כִּכָּ֥ר\rb* \rb per base.|לָאָֽדֶן׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb With the 1,775 shekels|הָאֶ֜לֶף\rb* [of silver]\f + \fr 38:28 \fqa \ref 1,775|5\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 44|44\ref*.6 pounds or 20.2 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb |וּשְׁבַ֤ע\rb*\rb |הַמֵּאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֔ים\rb*\rb he made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the hooks|וָוִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the posts,|לָעַמּוּדִ֑ים\rb* \rb overlaid|וְצִפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb their tops,|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and supplied bands|וְחִשַּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb for them.|אֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb The bronze|וּנְחֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb from the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb totaled 70|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and 2,400|וְאַלְפַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb shekels.|שָֽׁקֶל׃\rb*\f + \fr 38:29 \ft The total weight of the bronze was \ref approximately 2|2\ref*.67 tons or 2.42 metric tons.\f* \v 30 \rb He used it to make|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bases|אַדְנֵי֙\rb* \rb for the entrance|פֶּ֚תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb and its bronze|הַנְּחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb grating,|מִכְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the utensils|כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 31 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the bases|אַדְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb for the surrounding|סָבִ֔יב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb and|אַדְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb its gate,|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*\rb |הֶחָצֵ֑ר\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tent pegs|יִתְדֹ֧ת\rb* \rb for the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יִתְדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb its surrounding|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb courtyard.|הֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb*
\c 39
\s1 The Ephod
\r \ref Exodus 28:6–14|EXO 28:6-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the blue,|הַתְּכֵ֤לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְהָֽאַרְגָּמָן֙\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn|וְתוֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb they made|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb specially woven|שְׂרָ֖ד\rb* \rb garments|בִגְדֵי־\rb* \rb for ministry|לְשָׁרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb in the sanctuary,|בַּקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as well as the holy|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb for Aaron,|לְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb just as|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Bezalel made|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\f + \fr 39:2 \ft Literally \fqa He made\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֑ד\rb* \rb of finely spun|מָשְׁזָֽר׃\rb* \rb linen|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb embroidered with gold,|זָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb and with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn.|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \v 3 \rb They hammered out|וַֽיְרַקְּע֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb thin sheets|פַּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָב֮\rb* \rb and cut|וְקִצֵּ֣ץ\rb* \rb threads from them|פְּתִילִם֒\rb* \rb to interweave|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּת֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb with the blue,|הַתְּכֵ֙לֶת֙\rb*\rb |וּבְת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb purple,|הָֽאַרְגָּמָ֔ן\rb*\rb |וּבְת֛וֹךְ\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|תּוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבְת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb and fine linen—|הַשֵּׁ֑שׁ\rb*  \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb of a skilled craftsman.|חֹשֵֽׁב׃\rb* \v 4 \rb They made|עָֽשׂוּ־\rb* \rb shoulder pieces|כְּתֵפֹ֥ת\rb* \rb for the ephod,|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb which were attached|חֹבְרֹ֑ת\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of its corners,|קִצְווֹתוֹ\rb* \rb so it could be fastened.|חֻבָּֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb And the skillfully woven waistband|וְחֵ֨שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of|עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb the ephod|אֲפֻדָּת֜וֹ\rb* \rb was of one piece with the ephod,|מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb of the same|הוּא֮\rb* \rb workmanship—|כְּמַעֲשֵׂהוּ֒\rb*  \rb with gold,|זָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and with finely spun|מָשְׁזָ֑ר\rb* \rb linen,|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb They mounted|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the onyx|הַשֹּׁ֔הַם\rb*\rb |מֻֽסַבֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb in gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb filigree settings,|מִשְׁבְּצֹ֣ת\rb* \rb engraved|מְפֻתָּחֹת֙\rb*\rb |פִּתּוּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb like a seal|חוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then they fastened|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the shoulder pieces|כִּתְפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֔ד\rb* \rb as memorial|זִכָּר֖וֹן\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the sons|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Breastpiece
\r \ref Exodus 28:15–30|EXO 28:15-30\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb He made|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the breastpiece|הַחֹ֛שֶׁן\rb* \rb with the same workmanship|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |חֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb*\rb |כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb as the ephod,|אֵפֹ֑ד\rb* \rb with gold,|זָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb with blue,|תְּכֵ֧לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֛ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn,|וְתוֹלַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb and with finely spun|מָשְׁזָֽר׃\rb* \rb linen.|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \v 9 \rb It|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַחֹ֑שֶׁן\rb* \rb was square|רָב֧וּעַ\rb*\rb |הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb when folded over double,|כָּפ֖וּל\rb* \rb a span|זֶ֧רֶת\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and a span|וְזֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb wide.|רָחְבּ֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 39:9 \ft The breastpiece, when folded over, was \ref approximately 9|9\ref* inches or 22.9 centimeters in both length and width.\f*\rb |כָּפֽוּל׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb And they mounted|וַיְמַלְאוּ־\rb* \rb on it|ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb rows|ט֣וּרֵי\rb* \rb of gemstones:|אָ֑בֶן\rb*\f + \fr 39:10 \ft The precise identification of some of these gemstones is uncertain.\f*
\li1 \rb The first|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb row had|ט֗וּר\rb*\rb |הַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a ruby,|אֹ֤דֶם\rb* \rb a topaz,|פִּטְדָה֙\rb* \rb and an emerald;|וּבָרֶ֔קֶת\rb*
\li1 \v 11 \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb row had|וְהַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a turquoise,|נֹ֥פֶךְ\rb* \rb a sapphire,|סַפִּ֖יר\rb* \rb and a diamond;|וְיָהֲלֹֽם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 12 \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb row had|וְהַטּ֖וּר\rb* \rb a jacinth,|לֶ֥שֶׁם\rb* \rb an agate,|שְׁב֖וֹ\rb* \rb and an amethyst;|וְאַחְלָֽמָה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 13 \rb and the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb row had|וְהַטּוּר֙\rb* \rb a beryl,|תַּרְשִׁ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb an onyx,|שֹׁ֖הַם\rb* \rb and a jasper.|וְיָשְׁפֵ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb These stones were mounted|מֽוּסַבֹּ֛ת\rb* \rb in gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb filigree|מִשְׁבְּצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb settings.|בְּמִלֻּאֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb The twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb stones|וְ֠הָאֲבָנִים\rb* \rb corresponded to|עַל־\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמֹ֨ת\rb*\rb |הֵ֛נָּה\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb stone was engraved|פִּתּוּחֵ֤י\rb* \rb like a seal|חֹתָם֙\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of one of the twelve|לִשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb tribes.|שָֽׁבֶט׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb For|עַל־\rb* \rb the breastpiece|הַחֹ֛שֶׁן\rb* \rb they made|וַיַּעֲשׂ֧וּ\rb* \rb braided|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb chains|עֲבֹ֑ת\rb* \rb like cords|גַּבְלֻ֖ת\rb*\rb |שַׁרְשְׁרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold.|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \v 16 \rb They also made|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֗וּ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb filigree settings|מִשְׁבְּצֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb rings,|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and fastened|וַֽיִּתְּנ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb rings|הַטַּבָּעֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb corners|קְצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece.|הַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Then they fastened|וַֽיִּתְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb chains|הָעֲבֹתֹ֣ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb gold rings|הַטַּבָּעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the corners|קְצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece,|הַחֹֽשֶׁן׃\rb* \v 18 \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb they fastened|נָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb the other|שְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb ends|קְצוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb chains|הָֽעֲבֹתֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb filigree settings,|הַֽמִּשְׁבְּצֹ֑ת\rb* \rb attaching them|וַֽיִּתְּנֻ֛ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the shoulder pieces|כִּתְפֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front.|מ֥וּל\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb They made|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֗וּ\rb* \rb two more|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and attached them|וַיָּשִׂ֕ימוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the other two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb corners|קְצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the breastpiece,|הַחֹ֑שֶׁן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the inside|בָּֽיְתָה׃\rb* \rb edge|שְׂפָת֕וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb next to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ephod.|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb They made|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֮\rb* \rb two additional|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb gold|זָהָב֒\rb* \rb rings|טַבְּעֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and attached them|וַֽיִּתְּנֻ֡ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the bottom|מִלְמַ֙טָּה֙\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁתֵּי֩\rb* \rb shoulder pieces|כִתְפֹ֨ת\rb* \rb of the ephod,|הָאֵפֹ֤ד\rb* \rb on its front,|מִמּ֣וּל\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb near|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb the seam|מֶחְבַּרְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb just above|מִמַּ֕עַל\rb* \rb its woven waistband.|לְחֵ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |הָאֵפֹֽד׃\rb* \v 21 \rb Then they tied|וַיִּרְכְּס֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rings|מִטַּבְּעֹתָיו֩\rb* \rb of the breastpiece|הַחֹ֡שֶׁן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the rings|טַבְּעֹ֨ת\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֜ד\rb* \rb with a cord|בִּפְתִ֣יל\rb* \rb of blue yarn,|תְּכֵ֗לֶת\rb* \rb so that the breastpiece|הַחֹ֔שֶׁן\rb* \rb was|לִֽהְיֹת֙\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the waistband|חֵ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb swing out|יִזַּ֣ח\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the ephod,|הָאֵפֹ֑ד\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*
\s1 Additional Priestly Garments
\r \ref Exodus 28:31–43|EXO 28:31-43\ref*)
\p \v 22 \rb They made|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|מְעִ֥יל\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb entirely|כְּלִ֖יל\rb* \rb of blue cloth,|תְּכֵֽלֶת׃\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of a weaver,|אֹרֵ֑ג\rb* \v 23 \rb with an opening|וּפִֽי־\rb* \rb in the center|בְּתוֹכ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of the robe|הַמְּעִ֥יל\rb* \rb like that|כְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb of a garment,|תַחְרָ֑א\rb*\f + \fr 39:23 \ft The meaning of the Hebrew word is uncertain; possibly \fqa a coat of mail\ft .\f* \rb with a collar|שָׂפָ֥ה\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the opening|לְפִ֛יו\rb* \rb so that it would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb tear.|יִקָּרֵֽעַ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb They made|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb pomegranates|רִמּוֹנֵ֕י\rb* \rb of blue,|תְּכֵ֥לֶת\rb* \rb purple,|וְאַרְגָּמָ֖ן\rb* \rb and scarlet yarn|וְתוֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb and finely spun linen|מָשְׁזָֽר׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the lower hem|שׁוּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the robe.|הַמְּעִ֔יל\rb* \v 25 \rb They also made|וַיַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb bells|פַעֲמֹנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and attached|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|הַפַּֽעֲמֹנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb*\rb |הָרִמֹּנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb the hem|שׁוּלֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַמְּעִיל֙\rb* \rb between|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the pomegranates,|הָרִמֹּנִֽים׃\rb* \v 26 \rb alternating|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the bells|פַּעֲמֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and pomegranates|וְרִמֹּן֙\rb*\rb |פַּעֲמֹ֣ן\rb*\rb |וְרִמֹּ֔ן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb around the lower hem|שׁוּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the robe|הַמְּעִ֖יל\rb* \rb to be worn for ministry,|לְשָׁרֵ֕ת\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃ס\rb*
